. 3060 measurement arm phase 1 RUNNING in background (CP0 x3 prof-ON, CP0off, MP0 x5 with H probe, MP0off); phase 2 (MPmax + REPRO @81920) after P_max derivation.", "status": "running", "done": ["gate PASS +0.31%", "formal binary fp 9b10076406621865 archived", "PR #156 open", "phase 1 legs launched"], "next": ["phase 1 results + H probe -> P_max -> phase 2 legs -> report with NVML-first order"], "blockers": [], "decisions": ["gate verdict computed on same-session interleaved legs"], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1219, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T02:11:06.586Z', '§93 EXECUTED: banked 6dbe376b8. Prefill-step PROF line implemented (PROF prefill ctx=%p n_tokens tps t_wall/t_cpu/t_dev/t_sync — first large-batch step, never averaged into windows), committed b4fb1590a + pushed (PR #156 updated). Rebuild archived: libllama fp 8b8c78ed835aaded (server fp unchanged 31755340782b8a8f, fused 499adb154daff04d). Leg script now verifies BOTH fps. NOTE: gate legs ran flag-OFF so carry no PROF lines — added ONE CUDA0 prof-ON calibration leg (C0CAL) for the gen5/x16 instrument-trust evidence, per §93 framing. Phase 1 v2 RUNNING (prefill-tagged binary): CP0 x3, CP0off, MP0 x5 (r1 = H probe), MP0off. Early raw from cancelled first phase-1 (old binary, pre-patch): CP0-r1 13.0140 tok/s decode / prefill 4.72 on 3060 — matches campaign 3060 numbers. Phase 2 after P_max.', 'running', '["§93 banked + patch b4fb1590a", "rebuilt + re-archived (libllama 8b8c78ed)", "phase 1 v2 running"]', '["C0CAL calibration leg", "phase 1 results -> P_max -> phase 2 (MPmax + REPRO @81920)"]', '[]', '["C0CAL added: gate legs were flag-OFF so no PROF calibration existed (1 leg, justified)"]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": ["docs/leader-handoff-state.md"]}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1219, "ts": "2026-09-20T02:11:06.586Z", "summary": "§93 EXECUTED: banked 6dbe376b8. Prefill-step PROF line implemented (PROF prefill ctx=%p n_tokens tps t_wall/t_cpu/t_dev/t_sync — first large-batch step, never averaged into windows), committed b4fb1590a + pushed (PR #156 updated). Rebuild archived: libllama fp 8b8c78ed835aaded (server fp unchanged 31755340782b8a8f, fused 499adb154daff04d). Leg script now verifies BOTH fps. NOTE: gate legs ran flag-OFF so carry no PROF lines — added ONE CUDA0 prof-ON calibration leg (C0CAL) for the gen5/x16 instrument-trust evidence, per §93 framing. Phase 1 v2 RUNNING (prefill-tagged binary): CP0 x3, CP0off, MP0 x5 (r1 = H probe), MP0off. Early raw from cancelled first phase-1 (old binary, pre-patch): CP0-r1 13.0140 tok/s decode / prefill 4.72 on 3060 — matches campaign 3060 numbers. Phase 2 after P_max.", "status": "running", "done": ["§93 banked + patch b4fb1590a", "rebuilt + re-archived (libllama 8b8c78ed)", "phase 1 v2 running"], "next": ["C0CAL calibration leg", "phase 1 results -> P_max -> phase 2 (MPmax + REPRO @81920)"], "blockers": [], "decisions": ["C0CAL added: gate legs were flag-OFF so no PROF calibration existed (1 leg, justified)"], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": ["docs/leader-handoff-state.md"]}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1220, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T02:23:03.133Z', 'Phase-1 v2 relaunch after incident: the phase-1 job died at leg-1 curl step (bash syntax error at line 73) AND left an orphaned server holding the 3060 (WINDOW_CLOSED gpu-busy x9). ROOT CAUSE: leader edited arm3060MTP.sh (C0CAL addition) WHILE a leg was executing it — bash incremental re-read hit shifted bytes. Script itself was fine; verified SYNTAX_OK, orphan killed, GPU clean. New lesson: never patch a running leg script. Phase 1 v3 RUNNING (11 legs: CP0 x3, CP0off, MP0 x5 w/ H probe, MP0off, C0CAL CUDA0 calibration) with prefill-tagged binary, both fps verified. Prior partial CP0-r1 (13.0140/4.72) kept as raw, leg VOID (resp never captured).', 'running', '["orphan killed", "script syntax verified", "phase 1 v3 launched with C0CAL"]', '["phase 1 results -> H probe -> P_max -> phase 2"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": "never patch a running leg script", "docs_updated": []}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1220, "ts": "2026-09-20T02:23:03.133Z", "summary": "Phase-1 v2 relaunch after incident: the phase-1 job died at leg-1 curl step (bash syntax error at line 73) AND left an orphaned server holding the 3060 (WINDOW_CLOSED gpu-busy x9). ROOT CAUSE: leader edited arm3060MTP.sh (C0CAL addition) WHILE a leg was executing it — bash incremental re-read hit shifted bytes. Script itself was fine; verified SYNTAX_OK, orphan killed, GPU clean. New lesson: never patch a running leg script. Phase 1 v3 RUNNING (11 legs: CP0 x3, CP0off, MP0 x5 w/ H probe, MP0off, C0CAL CUDA0 calibration) with prefill-tagged binary, both fps verified. Prior partial CP0-r1 (13.0140/4.72) kept as raw, leg VOID (resp never captured).", "status": "running", "done": ["orphan killed", "script syntax verified", "phase 1 v3 launched with C0CAL"], "next": ["phase 1 results -> H probe -> P_max -> phase 2"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": "never patch a running leg script", "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1221, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T02:24:48.174Z', 'Deep tick: quota healthy (session 20%, week 61%). Summary rebuild DEFERRED — §92/§93 arm is mid-flight (phase 1 v3 running, 11 legs ~55 min); rebuild #9 fires at the arm consolidation point (phase 1+2 results + §76 discriminator verdict) rather than mid-arm. Lessons current (5 campaign rules + never-patch-a-running-leg-script added this session). Docs current (handoff bank through §93; PR #156 open). No other work while GPU legs hold the rig.', 'running', '["quota 20%/61%", "rebuild deferred with delta note"]', '["phase 1 results -> H probe -> P_max -> phase 2 -> consolidation rebuild #9"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1221, "ts": "2026-09-20T02:24:48.174Z", "summary": "Deep tick: quota healthy (session 20%, week 61%). Summary rebuild DEFERRED — §92/§93 arm is mid-flight (phase 1 v3 running, 11 legs ~55 min); rebuild #9 fires at the arm consolidation point (phase 1+2 results + §76 discriminator verdict) rather than mid-arm. Lessons current (5 campaign rules + never-patch-a-running-leg-script added this session). Docs current (handoff bank through §93; PR #156 open). No other work while GPU legs hold the rig.", "status": "running", "done": ["quota 20%/61%", "rebuild deferred with delta note"], "next": ["phase 1 results -> H probe -> P_max -> phase 2 -> consolidation rebuild #9"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(104, 'p-58c3ab092b', 't-d94162d3f0', '2026-09-20T02:59:20.214Z', 'Owner reported 2 defects. Diagnosed: (1) app lands on Chat after #776 rework -> Atlas/Brain not default (owner reads as missing atlas tab); (2) tier bar renders health.tiers nobody populates -> RAM-dominant allocation, false for ngl 99 llama.cpp. Filed #785 with fix specs (default view=brain; real tier reporting from ggml backend buffer sizes at engine load, server-layer only, no collision files). Handed off to agent dc1874da (running, notify on finish).', 'idle', '["#785 filed", "handoff sent"]', '["await agent", "verify on VM"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '5c3486e5', 'command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', '{"n": 104, "ts": "2026-09-20T02:59:20.214Z", "summary": "Owner reported 2 defects. Diagnosed: (1) app lands on Chat after #776 rework -> Atlas/Brain not default (owner reads as missing atlas tab); (2) tier bar renders health.tiers nobody populates -> RAM-dominant allocation, false for ngl 99 llama.cpp. Filed #785 with fix specs (default view=brain; real tier reporting from ggml backend buffer sizes at engine load, server-layer only, no collision files). Handed off to agent dc1874da (running, notify on finish).", "status": "idle", "done": ["#785 filed", "handoff sent"], "next": ["await agent", "verify on VM"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "5c3486e5", "author_model": "command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1222, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T03:04:39.831Z', 'Phase 1 v3 done (11/11). 3060 ctx16384: C-P0 median 12.9823 (CP0off 12.9380, overhead nil); M-P0 median 13.4832, acceptance bimodal (0.42-0.51 -> 10.3/11.25; 0.74-0.86 -> 13.9/14.4/15.25); leader band 13.6-15.0 partially hit. H probe 6229 MiB -> P_max 4 (ncmoe 44). C0CAL CUDA0 18.87/121.74. Profiler defects fixed: prefill threshold 32->256 (42-tok warmup stole tag); t_dev -1 sentinel -> cudaEventSynchronize (server syncs per step anyway). Commit ff3537723 pushed, re-archived fp 4e47bf4cbf205103 / libllama a577f8ce41b7f51c. Mini-set (CP0+MP0+C0CAL) running to validate before phase 2.', 'running', '["phase 1 complete", "P_max 4", "profiler fixed ff3537723"]', '["validate PROF prefill lines", "phase 2 MP4+REPRO via arm3060P2.sh"]', '[]', '["eventSynchronize replaces query-guard"]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1222, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:04:39.831Z", "summary": "Phase 1 v3 done (11/11). 3060 ctx16384: C-P0 median 12.9823 (CP0off 12.9380, overhead nil); M-P0 median 13.4832, acceptance bimodal (0.42-0.51 -> 10.3/11.25; 0.74-0.86 -> 13.9/14.4/15.25); leader band 13.6-15.0 partially hit. H probe 6229 MiB -> P_max 4 (ncmoe 44). C0CAL CUDA0 18.87/121.74. Profiler defects fixed: prefill threshold 32->256 (42-tok warmup stole tag); t_dev -1 sentinel -> cudaEventSynchronize (server syncs per step anyway). Commit ff3537723 pushed, re-archived fp 4e47bf4cbf205103 / libllama a577f8ce41b7f51c. Mini-set (CP0+MP0+C0CAL) running to validate before phase 2.", "status": "running", "done": ["phase 1 complete", "P_max 4", "profiler fixed ff3537723"], "next": ["validate PROF prefill lines", "phase 2 MP4+REPRO via arm3060P2.sh"], "blockers": [], "decisions": ["eventSynchronize replaces query-guard"], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(105, 'p-58c3ab092b', 't-d94162d3f0', '2026-09-20T03:04:53.073Z', 'Owner directive implemented: Recorded metrics panel now tabbed per telemetry family (Colibri | REAP | Edge0) replacing card row. Colibri tab = measured values (3201 specialists/5186 generalists/5186 weak/mean spec 0.59 on p100-35b); REAP+Edge0 tabs = honest not-wired panes with pending dots (schema stays null until observers land). Deployed to VM :8620, Playwright verified all 3 tabs, zero JS errors. Committed. Note: dev :8619 was down (agent #785 work); VM verified instead.', 'idle', '["tabbed metrics panel deployed+verified"]', '["await agent #785 result", "verify combined state"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '5c3486e5', 'command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', '{"n": 105, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:04:53.073Z", "summary": "Owner directive implemented: Recorded metrics panel now tabbed per telemetry family (Colibri | REAP | Edge0) replacing card row. Colibri tab = measured values (3201 specialists/5186 generalists/5186 weak/mean spec 0.59 on p100-35b); REAP+Edge0 tabs = honest not-wired panes with pending dots (schema stays null until observers land). Deployed to VM :8620, Playwright verified all 3 tabs, zero JS errors. Committed. Note: dev :8619 was down (agent #785 work); VM verified instead.", "status": "idle", "done": ["tabbed metrics panel deployed+verified"], "next": ["await agent #785 result", "verify combined state"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "5c3486e5", "author_model": "command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(106, 'p-58c3ab092b', 't-d94162d3f0', '2026-09-20T03:14:48.717Z', 'Filed hydra_vortex#786: wire the two missing telemetry families. REAP saliency (router gate magnitude x activation norm per layer/expert, extends Stage-A ids-only readout; collision protocol: proposal + owner sign-off before touching llama-graph/context) and Edge0 prerouter predictability (telemetry-only: one documented reference predictor, hit-rate + prefetch-gain; needs owner decision on predictor definition). Acceptance: tabs lose pending dot with real numbers, validator-clean v2 artifacts, null controls, VM+dev verified.', 'idle', '["#786 filed"]', '["owner decision: Edge0 reference predictor", "dispatch agent after #785 lands"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '5c3486e5', 'command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', '{"n": 106, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:14:48.717Z", "summary": "Filed hydra_vortex#786: wire the two missing telemetry families. REAP saliency (router gate magnitude x activation norm per layer/expert, extends Stage-A ids-only readout; collision protocol: proposal + owner sign-off before touching llama-graph/context) and Edge0 prerouter predictability (telemetry-only: one documented reference predictor, hit-rate + prefetch-gain; needs owner decision on predictor definition). Acceptance: tabs lose pending dot with real numbers, validator-clean v2 artifacts, null controls, VM+dev verified.", "status": "idle", "done": ["#786 filed"], "next": ["owner decision: Edge0 reference predictor", "dispatch agent after #785 lands"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "5c3486e5", "author_model": "command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(107, 'p-58c3ab092b', 't-d94162d3f0', '2026-09-20T03:22:10.435Z', 'Agent dc1874da was aborted by owner mid-#785 (no commits, no comments, VM unaffected - verified). Owner chose re-dispatch: fresh handoff sent for #785 (Atlas default view + truthful VRAM tiers from ggml backend buffer sizes), with cleanup note for aborted-run residue (out-nano-8891 dir, submodule noise). Monitoring on finish.', 'idle', '["state assessed", "re-dispatch sent"]', '["await agent finish", "verify #785 on VM"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '5c3486e5', 'command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', '{"n": 107, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:22:10.435Z", "summary": "Agent dc1874da was aborted by owner mid-#785 (no commits, no comments, VM unaffected - verified). Owner chose re-dispatch: fresh handoff sent for #785 (Atlas default view + truthful VRAM tiers from ggml backend buffer sizes), with cleanup note for aborted-run residue (out-nano-8891 dir, submodule noise). Monitoring on finish.", "status": "idle", "done": ["state assessed", "re-dispatch sent"], "next": ["await agent finish", "verify #785 on VM"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "5c3486e5", "author_model": "command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1223, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T03:27:41.176Z', 'Instrument hunt, round 2. Mini-set read: 3060 prefill 512 tok = 72.4s wall, t_dev 0-5.4ms; CUDA0 prefill 2.83s (181 tps) but t_dev 0.0 TOO — event bracket only measured last tiny CUDA segment (multi-split), CUDA0 calibration FAILED, readings inadmissible per 93 rule. Also t_cpu useless (spin-wait inflates process CPU on both). Free checks: fatbin CLEAN (143x sm_86 + 143x sm_120 SASS, no PTX) and PCIe median 3 MB/s during 3060 prefill (quiet) — wholesale CPU fallback looks unlikely; 26x gap points at shape-dependent sm_86 kernel path. FIX: caller-managed CUDA event span (begin before sched compute, end after; graph_compute records suppressed while span open). Commit 973752f5e pushed; re-archived server ff0bda54d59eb659 / libllama d3448cb406018ff9; scripts updated. Gate caught a load spike (omp+gdu), waited, span validation legs RUNNING (CP0 + C0CAL).', 'running', '["span instrument 973752f5e", "fatbin verified sm_86 SASS"]', '["read span t_dev: 3060 vs CUDA0 prefill -> 93 verdict", "phase 2 after validation"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1223, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:27:41.176Z", "summary": "Instrument hunt, round 2. Mini-set read: 3060 prefill 512 tok = 72.4s wall, t_dev 0-5.4ms; CUDA0 prefill 2.83s (181 tps) but t_dev 0.0 TOO — event bracket only measured last tiny CUDA segment (multi-split), CUDA0 calibration FAILED, readings inadmissible per 93 rule. Also t_cpu useless (spin-wait inflates process CPU on both). Free checks: fatbin CLEAN (143x sm_86 + 143x sm_120 SASS, no PTX) and PCIe median 3 MB/s during 3060 prefill (quiet) — wholesale CPU fallback looks unlikely; 26x gap points at shape-dependent sm_86 kernel path. FIX: caller-managed CUDA event span (begin before sched compute, end after; graph_compute records suppressed while span open). Commit 973752f5e pushed; re-archived server ff0bda54d59eb659 / libllama d3448cb406018ff9; scripts updated. Gate caught a load spike (omp+gdu), waited, span validation legs RUNNING (CP0 + C0CAL).", "status": "running", "done": ["span instrument 973752f5e", "fatbin verified sm_86 SASS"], "next": ["read span t_dev: 3060 vs CUDA0 prefill -> 93 verdict", "phase 2 after validation"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1224, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-20T03:31:38.608Z', '93 VERDICT: CPU-fallback REFUTED. Span instrument calibrates CLEAN on both GPUs: 3060 prefill 512tok t_wall 72681.6ms / t_dev 72674.8ms (~100% device); CUDA0 t_wall 2860.7 / t_dev 2854.1 (~100%). The 3060 prefill runs ENTIRELY on its GPU — the 26x gap is genuine device-side slowness, shape-dependent (prefill 25x, decode 1.45x). Mechanism (corroborated by 82 cp.async finding): sm_86 SASS cubins lack fast MMA/cp.async variants -> large-batch matmuls take slow non-MMA path in fork kernel dispatch. 76 closes as sm_86 kernel-path issue (config/link/OS all exonerated; fatbin verified 143x sm_86 SASS, no PTX). Decode numbers healthy: CP0 12.887, C0CAL 18.9195 (overhead nil). Next: grep __CUDA_ARCH__ gates to pin exact dispatch bug; phase 2 launching (MP4 x5 + REPRO @81920).', 'running', '["93 verdict: device-bound prefill, CPU fallback refuted", "instrument calibrated both GPUs"]', '["pin arch-gate dispatch bug", "phase 2: MP4 + REPRO"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": "event-span-per-decode-step-for-split-backends", "docs_updated": []}', '0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba', '', '{"n": 1224, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:31:38.608Z", "summary": "93 VERDICT: CPU-fallback REFUTED. Span instrument calibrates CLEAN on both GPUs: 3060 prefill 512tok t_wall 72681.6ms / t_dev 72674.8ms (~100% device); CUDA0 t_wall 2860.7 / t_dev 2854.1 (~100%). The 3060 prefill runs ENTIRELY on its GPU — the 26x gap is genuine device-side slowness, shape-dependent (prefill 25x, decode 1.45x). Mechanism (corroborated by 82 cp.async finding): sm_86 SASS cubins lack fast MMA/cp.async variants -> large-batch matmuls take slow non-MMA path in fork kernel dispatch. 76 closes as sm_86 kernel-path issue (config/link/OS all exonerated; fatbin verified 143x sm_86 SASS, no PTX). Decode numbers healthy: CP0 12.887, C0CAL 18.9195 (overhead nil). Next: grep __CUDA_ARCH__ gates to pin exact dispatch bug; phase 2 launching (MP4 x5 + REPRO @81920).", "status": "running", "done": ["93 verdict: device-bound prefill, CPU fallback refuted", "instrument calibrated both GPUs"], "next": ["pin arch-gate dispatch bug", "phase 2: MP4 + REPRO"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": "event-span-per-decode-step-for-split-backends", "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0082a065-08b4-49fa-bd6e-5333e1ec31ba", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(108, 'p-58c3ab092b', 't-d94162d3f0', '2026-09-20T03:33:28.809Z', 'Owner architecture directive -> verified 3 gaps + filed epic #787: (1) Profiling dead = fork lacks /profile, upstream UI complete (ProfileTurn contract documented); (2) upstream Atlas tab = the SITE galaxy canvas (The mind measured, drag-to-spin affinity galaxy) - port as tab; (3) per-turn/per-prompt telemetry: turn model (seq + ring buffer), per-turn routing slices via Stage-A counter snapshots, /profile + /turns APIs, shared turn selector + delta badges, client-side sparse delta, expert-metrics turn-record schema. 4 sub-tasks, epic branch epic/787-per-turn-telemetry PROPOSED awaiting owner go-ahead. #785 agent still running.', 'idle', '["#787 filed with design"]', '["owner: epic branch go-ahead + dispatch order"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '5c3486e5', 'command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash', '{"n": 108, "ts": "2026-09-20T03:33:28.809Z", "summary": "Owner architecture directive -> verified 3 gaps + filed epic #787: (1) Profiling dead = fork lacks /profile, upstream UI complete (ProfileTurn contract documented); (2) upstream Atlas tab = the SITE galaxy canvas (The mind measured, drag-to-spin affinity galaxy) - port as tab; (3) per-turn/per-prompt telemetry: turn model (seq + ring buffer), per-turn routing slices via Stage-A counter snapshots, /profile + /turns APIs, shared turn selector + delta badges, client-side sparse delta, expert-metrics turn-record schema. 4 sub-tasks, epic branch epic/787-per-turn-telemetry PROPOSED awaiting owner go-ahead. #785 agent still running.", "status": "idle", "done": ["#787 filed with design"], "next": ["owner: epic branch go-ahead + dispatch order"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "5c3486e5", "author_model": "command