t aggregate throughput test)"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1280, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-23T06:48:13.877Z', 'Arm A (static3060, N=5) complete: rep1(cold)=12.18 tok/s decode, rep2=12.31, rep3=12.71 tok/s, peak VRAM 11807 MiB, no voids. Arm B (cache3060, N=42) now booted and mid-rep-1 prefill.', 'running', '["Arm A (static3060) P1 A/B leg complete: 3/3 reps, no voids, peak VRAM 11807 MiB matches dose-search prediction"]', '["Wait for Arm B (cache3060) to complete 3 reps", "Apply amended decision rule (rep-1 cold decode_tps_server as primary metric, reps 2-3 as replay upper bound for cache arm only)", "Check override-precedence gate and headroom gate for Arm B", "Report P1 A/B result + P1-before completion to architect on next deep tick"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'leader', 'claude-sonnet-5', '{"n": 1280, "ts": "2026-09-23T06:48:13.877Z", "summary": "Arm A (static3060, N=5) complete: rep1(cold)=12.18 tok/s decode, rep2=12.31, rep3=12.71 tok/s, peak VRAM 11807 MiB, no voids. Arm B (cache3060, N=42) now booted and mid-rep-1 prefill.", "status": "running", "done": ["Arm A (static3060) P1 A/B leg complete: 3/3 reps, no voids, peak VRAM 11807 MiB matches dose-search prediction"], "next": ["Wait for Arm B (cache3060) to complete 3 reps", "Apply amended decision rule (rep-1 cold decode_tps_server as primary metric, reps 2-3 as replay upper bound for cache arm only)", "Check override-precedence gate and headroom gate for Arm B", "Report P1 A/B result + P1-before completion to architect on next deep tick"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1281, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-23T07:00:23.457Z', 'Deep tick: P1 A/B amendment applied (rep-1-cold as primary metric, replay-upper-bound framing for cache arm, logged in sec 34). Arm A (static3060, N=5) complete: cold decode 12.18 tok/s, no voids. Arm B (cache3060, N=42) healthy mid rep-1 prefill (44%). Sent architect status consult, no blocker.', 'running', '["Architect''s methodology amendment logged and applied without disrupting the in-progress run", "Arm A complete: cold decode 12.18 tok/s, prefill 8.98 tok/s, peak VRAM 11807 MiB, no voids"]', '["Wait for Arm B rep-1 (cold) decode result", "Apply decision rule: compare rep-1 cold decode_tps_server between arms", "Check override-precedence + headroom gates for Arm B", "Report P1-before completion + verdict to architect, open BIOS reboot window"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'leader', 'claude-sonnet-5', '{"n": 1281, "ts": "2026-09-23T07:00:23.457Z", "summary": "Deep tick: P1 A/B amendment applied (rep-1-cold as primary metric, replay-upper-bound framing for cache arm, logged in sec 34). Arm A (static3060, N=5) complete: cold decode 12.18 tok/s, no voids. Arm B (cache3060, N=42) healthy mid rep-1 prefill (44%). Sent architect status consult, no blocker.", "status": "running", "done": ["Architect''s methodology amendment logged and applied without disrupting the in-progress run", "Arm A complete: cold decode 12.18 tok/s, prefill 8.98 tok/s, peak VRAM 11807 MiB, no voids"], "next": ["Wait for Arm B rep-1 (cold) decode result", "Apply decision rule: compare rep-1 cold decode_tps_server between arms", "Check override-precedence + headroom gates for Arm B", "Report P1-before completion + verdict to architect, open BIOS reboot window"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1282, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-23T07:18:52.773Z', 'P1 A/B decisive result: Arm B (cache3060, N=42) rep-1 cold decode collapsed to 1.51 tok/s vs Arm A (static3060, N=5) 12.18 tok/s (~8x), far past the -5% tie-break bound. Prefill unaffected (8.56 vs 8.98), VRAM fine both arms. Verdict: static3060 wins, logged in design doc sec 34. Flagged the unexplained decode-side collapse mechanism to architect out-of-cycle given the magnitude; not blocking, proceeding toward P2 prep while Arm B''s remaining reps finish.', 'running', '["P1 A/B verdict reached: static3060 (N=5) is the 3060''s P1 serving config, decisive margin", "Result + tie-break application recorded in design doc sec 34"]', '["Let Arm B reps 2-3 finish (replay upper bound, non-decisive)", "Report P1-before completion to architect on next deep tick to open BIOS reboot window", "Begin P2 prep (concurrent aggregate throughput test) using static3060 config as the 3060 side"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'leader', 'claude-sonnet-5', '{"n": 1282, "ts": "2026-09-23T07:18:52.773Z", "summary": "P1 A/B decisive result: Arm B (cache3060, N=42) rep-1 cold decode collapsed to 1.51 tok/s vs Arm A (static3060, N=5) 12.18 tok/s (~8x), far past the -5% tie-break bound. Prefill unaffected (8.56 vs 8.98), VRAM fine both arms. Verdict: static3060 wins, logged in design doc sec 34. Flagged the unexplained decode-side collapse mechanism to architect out-of-cycle given the magnitude; not blocking, proceeding toward P2 prep while Arm B''s remaining reps finish.", "status": "running", "done": ["P1 A/B verdict reached: static3060 (N=5) is the 3060''s P1 serving config, decisive margin", "Result + tie-break application recorded in design doc sec 34"], "next": ["Let Arm B reps 2-3 finish (replay upper bound, non-decisive)", "Report P1-before completion to architect on next deep tick to open BIOS reboot window", "Begin P2 prep (concurrent aggregate throughput test) using static3060 config as the 3060 side"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1283, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-23T07:36:54.260Z', 'P1-before fully closed. PCIe decode-collapse diagnostic (3 boots) confirmed H1 (link-bound): cache mechanism moves ~400-600 MiB/token on both GPUs but Gen1 (3060) can''t carry it while Gen5 (5060 Ti) can. Baseline (static3060, no cache) confirms it''s cache-specific, not general Gen1 traffic. H3/#791 not indicated. Full results + two-config P2 plan documented in design doc sec 34. Reported to architect as the deep-tick that opens the BIOS Gen3 reboot window per s157.', 'running', '["3-boot PCIe diagnostic complete: cache3060, cache5060_n42, static3060 baseline", "H1 (link-bound) confirmed decisively; H3/#791 ruled out, no follow-up boot needed", "P1-before (dose search + A/B verdict + collapse mechanism) fully closed and documented", "BIOS Gen3 reboot window opened per s157 instruction"]', '["Await architect confirmation on two-config P2 interpretation (or proceed with Config 1 default)", "Run P2 concurrent aggregate throughput test", "After owner''s BIOS fix: P1-after (repeat dose+A/B at new link speed) and P3 (prefill collapse re-measure)"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'leader', 'claude-sonnet-5', '{"n": 1283, "ts": "2026-09-23T07:36:54.260Z", "summary": "P1-before fully closed. PCIe decode-collapse diagnostic (3 boots) confirmed H1 (link-bound): cache mechanism moves ~400-600 MiB/token on both GPUs but Gen1 (3060) can''t carry it while Gen5 (5060 Ti) can. Baseline (static3060, no cache) confirms it''s cache-specific, not general Gen1 traffic. H3/#791 not indicated. Full results + two-config P2 plan documented in design doc sec 34. Reported to architect as the deep-tick that opens the BIOS Gen3 reboot window per s157.", "status": "running", "done": ["3-boot PCIe diagnostic complete: cache3060, cache5060_n42, static3060 baseline", "H1 (link-bound) confirmed decisively; H3/#791 ruled out, no follow-up boot needed", "P1-before (dose search + A/B verdict + collapse mechanism) fully closed and documented", "BIOS Gen3 reboot window opened per s157 instruction"], "next": ["Await architect confirmation on two-config P2 interpretation (or proceed with Config 1 default)", "Run P2 concurrent aggregate throughput test", "After owner''s BIOS fix: P1-after (repeat dose+A/B at new link speed) and P3 (prefill collapse re-measure)"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1284, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-23T08:01:52.378Z', 'Architect''s P2 correction applied (shared resource = host RAM bandwidth, not PCIe root complex, ~12 GB/s from 5060 Ti cache vs ~50 GB/s dual-channel DDR4 ceiling). Filed issue #794 for the cache counter undercounting defect. Pre-registered and launched P2 Config 1 (5060Ti cache N=84 + 3060 static N=5, solo+concurrent, disjoint P-core taskset pinning). Owner did not respond to a P2-timing AskUserQuestion (BIOS reboot risk); proceeded under standing auto-drive authorization since the run is cheap to redo if interrupted.', 'running', '["Design doc sec 34 corrected with architect''s RAM-bandwidth explanation and pre-registered Gen3 prediction", "Issue #794 filed for cache PCIe-counter undercounting", "P2 pre-registered: two configs, solo+concurrent per config, taskset-pinned P-core split"]', '["Let P2 Config 1 finish (solo 5060, solo 3060, concurrent)", "Run P2 Config 2 (static control, no cache)", "Compute combined tok/s + interference ratios, compare configs", "After owner''s BIOS reboot (whenever it happens): P1-after single-boot confirm, then P3"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'leader', 'claude-sonnet-5', '{"n": 1284, "ts": "2026-09-23T08:01:52.378Z", "summary": "Architect''s P2 correction applied (shared resource = host RAM bandwidth, not PCIe root complex, ~12 GB/s from 5060 Ti cache vs ~50 GB/s dual-channel DDR4 ceiling). Filed issue #794 for the cache counter undercounting defect. Pre-registered and launched P2 Config 1 (5060Ti cache N=84 + 3060 static N=5, solo+concurrent, disjoint P-core taskset pinning). Owner did not respond to a P2-timing AskUserQuestion (BIOS reboot risk); proceeded under standing auto-drive authorization since the run is cheap to redo if interrupted.", "status": "running", "done": ["Design doc sec 34 corrected with architect''s RAM-bandwidth explanation and pre-registered Gen3 prediction", "Issue #794 filed for cache PCIe-counter undercounting", "P2 pre-registered: two configs, solo+concurrent per config, taskset-pinned P-core split"], "next": ["Let P2 Config 1 finish (solo 5060, solo 3060, concurrent)", "Run P2 Config 2 (static control, no cache)", "Compute combined tok/s + interference ratios, compare configs", "After owner''s BIOS reboot (whenever it happens): P1-after single-boot confirm, then P3"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "leader", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5"}');
