33), unconditional emit (:269), Validate requires non-zero (:461, main.go:64 exit), no global default, manager no post-filter -> plain remove = head dead at boot (different deploy failure). Plus: struct is only 7 fields, all other draft keys travel params map with generic emitter (:343-354) -> no silent-drop for load-mode/spec-type/ubatch/ctx/n-cpu-moe; rope nulls skip+warn as preferred; server convergence already PASS on the exact Option-A argv. Options table: A = head 2-site patch (conditional emit + validate warn, ships via deploy build, dev+my rec) vs B = server no-op flag (wrong layer, full rebuild chain) vs C = basename-conditional. RPC currently unused per ruling 5 (standalone, deferred sec 35) so optional-RPC consistent. Runtime proof optional via golang image pull. Push still HELD.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": ["P2 PUSH HELD - architect re-ruling rpc_port (Option A head 2-site patch leading); push+deploy+step-4+gates after", "EAN defect -> task-ff0e020578 owner; C1 deferred; P2 envs EAN/CAPTURE OFF", "baseline/local 27B down (curl 000) - owner restart needed; fleet_recommend still ranks it top", "Parent MAIN push/PR owner-gated (feat bump e848cb563 pushed)", "/tmp/opencode 8.7GB owner decision (swap 68.54% vs 70%)", "Core-route removal (models.json/workers.json) queued AFTER P2 gates - 7-day usage check first", "Capture slots 2-3 queued: collector after redeploy build leg, eb8be805 after collector"], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "72cc5fbc-99b5-4eba-af00-5aa16b4c01d6", "author_model": ""}');
