4s healthy, eb8be805 partial 208322s unclosed. t-abf10888f3: 5920->6117s (~102min silent), 0ev, 26/46, 20 open - 13th consecutive drift wake. t-34d7bdf5d6 72152s, 2/5. smoke/p1, t-a4d9544ed8 5/5, t-62504d3c56 12/12 unchanged. Stale 93c8e901 worker row 1585s. Next fire 18:30:00Z.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1470, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-27T18:31:22.309Z', 'Paused after d8k-n28; d8k-n42 VOID (my SIGKILL). Both defects confirmed+fixed: denominator used plan_calls not tokens, so no derived MiB/tok is published now (correct: 11917.11 MiB / 64 gen tok = 186.2); probe prefill declared non-measurement (only GROW prefill counts: 8.28 t/s / 2561 tok). FLAG DIFF: historical 10.52 t/s cell had NO MTP FLAGS; -t 6 identical (n_threads=6) so threads ruled out; only other deltas are -c 81920 vs 8192 and N 42 vs 28, both of which should be faster. CORRECTION: 10463 vs 7387 MiB is the -c gap (72K tok x 27648 B = 1.99 GiB KV), not a bigger cache - cache runs the other way (N=42 slabs 3.44 GiB vs N=28 2.30 GiB). ANSWER: my two runs differ in one flag. ngl=99 -> host_ops=0, 419 MiB/tok, 1.29 t/s, 573 MB/s = PCIe-bound. ngl=0 -> host_ops=1728 strategy_switches=336, 186 MiB/tok, 0.66 t/s, 131 MB/s = 23% of link, NOT PCIe-bound. ngl=0 host-stages the draft plane. Two cells running to prove it: d8k-n28-nomtp then d8k-n28-ngl99. KEPT: covered=49/49 required_unsupported=0, MTP accept 0.92-0.97, bytes-h 66.67%, decode 0.664/0.674/0.591/0.662 (mean 0.662 sd 0.038 n=3), slab 1.8310 MiB. registered=49 = 48 layers + draft plane. CHECKPOINT.md written first.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1470, "ts": "2026-09-27T18:31:22.309Z", "summary": "Paused after d8k-n28; d8k-n42 VOID (my SIGKILL). Both defects confirmed+fixed: denominator used plan_calls not tokens, so no derived MiB/tok is published now (correct: 11917.11 MiB / 64 gen tok = 186.2); probe prefill declared non-measurement (only GROW prefill counts: 8.28 t/s / 2561 tok). FLAG DIFF: historical 10.52 t/s cell had NO MTP FLAGS; -t 6 identical (n_threads=6) so threads ruled out; only other deltas are -c 81920 vs 8192 and N 42 vs 28, both of which should be faster. CORRECTION: 10463 vs 7387 MiB is the -c gap (72K tok x 27648 B = 1.99 GiB KV), not a bigger cache - cache runs the other way (N=42 slabs 3.44 GiB vs N=28 2.30 GiB). ANSWER: my two runs differ in one flag. ngl=99 -> host_ops=0, 419 MiB/tok, 1.29 t/s, 573 MB/s = PCIe-bound. ngl=0 -> host_ops=1728 strategy_switches=336, 186 MiB/tok, 0.66 t/s, 131 MB/s = 23% of link, NOT PCIe-bound. ngl=0 host-stages the draft plane. Two cells running to prove it: d8k-n28-nomtp then d8k-n28-ngl99. KEPT: covered=49/49 required_unsupported=0, MTP accept 0.92-0.97, bytes-h 66.67%, decode 0.664/0.674/0.591/0.662 (mean 0.662 sd 0.038 n=3), slab 1.8310 MiB. registered=49 = 48 layers + draft plane. CHECKPOINT.md written first.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(87, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', '2026-09-27T18:40:31.394Z', 'NARROW POLL (f9016d28 fire 5). now=18:40:22Z server-copied. wakes_remaining 15 (>1) => no digest, no collection, no messages. wakes_done 0 / checkup_id null on all tracks, 6th consecutive wake. t-d1cf43b723 RECOVERED blocked -> active at 18:31:22Z (leader age 531s): dev 6a24a038 isolated the flag diff. His two runs differ in ngl: ngl=99 -> host_ops=0, 419 MiB/tok, 1.29 t/s, 573 MB/s = PCIe-bound; ngl=0 -> host_ops=1728, 186 MiB/tok, 0.66 t/s, 131 MB/s = 23% of link, NOT PCIe-bound (ngl=0 host-stages the draft plane). Historical 10.52 t/s cell had NO MTP flags, so the unexplained gap is a config difference, not a regression. Also corrected: 10463 vs 7387 MiB is the -c gap (72K tok x 27648 B = 1.99 GiB KV), not a bigger cache - cache runs the other way. Both instrument defects confirmed+fixed; no derived MiB/tok published until denominator is tokens. Two proof cells running. t-f3ba82ac9c 140->720s, turns 84->86, 9/9, healthy. t-abf10888f3 6084->6859s (~114min silent), 0 workers, 20 open - 13th quiet wake, still NOT scored. t-34d7bdf5d6 72124->72899s, 3 running 2/5. Others unchanged. Two standing owner decisions still open: dead wake counter, dual-poller d585277e vs f9016d28.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '93c8e901-bbd7-4f3b-a288-86eb05f882bf', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 87, "ts": "2026-09-27T18:40:31.394Z", "summary": "NARROW POLL (f9016d28 fire 5). now=18:40:22Z server-copied. wakes_remaining 15 (>1) => no digest, no collection, no messages. wakes_done 0 / checkup_id null on all tracks, 6th consecutive wake. t-d1cf43b723 RECOVERED blocked -> active at 18:31:22Z (leader age 531s): dev 6a24a038 isolated the flag diff. His two runs differ in ngl: ngl=99 -> host_ops=0, 419 MiB/tok, 1.29 t/s, 573 MB/s = PCIe-bound; ngl=0 -> host_ops=1728, 186 MiB/tok, 0.66 t/s, 131 MB/s = 23% of link, NOT PCIe-bound (ngl=0 host-stages the draft plane). Historical 10.52 t/s cell had NO MTP flags, so the unexplained gap is a config difference, not a regression. Also corrected: 10463 vs 7387 MiB is the -c gap (72K tok x 27648 B = 1.99 GiB KV), not a bigger cache - cache runs the other way. Both instrument defects confirmed+fixed; no derived MiB/tok published until denominator is tokens. Two proof cells running. t-f3ba82ac9c 140->720s, turns 84->86, 9/9, healthy. t-abf10888f3 6084->6859s (~114min silent), 0 workers, 20 open - 13th quiet wake, still NOT scored. t-34d7bdf5d6 72124->72899s, 3 running 2/5. Others unchanged. Two standing owner decisions still open: dead wake counter, dual-poller d585277e vs f9016d28.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "93c8e901-bbd7-4f3b-a288-86eb05f882bf", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
