s. t-f3ba82ac9c: leader 3014->3426s, 2->3 ev/8m, 9/9, 3 open workers = me plus stale rows 93c8e901 (10721s) and ef8023ae (3426s); archiving outside my limits. t-d1cf43b723: leader 13->107s, 3->6 ev/8m, 47/58, 11 open, open workers 2->3: dev 6a24a038 REDISPATCHED at 12161s (same agent id as the worker that blocked transiently at fires 5-7 and closed out at fire 15 - dev work cycles). 8c8a2d29 partial 14008s, eb8be805 partial 217459s unclosed. t-abf10888f3: 14843->15254s (~254min silent), 0ev, 26/46, 20 open - 37th consecutive drift wake, still lowest-health in the fleet and the one a real final wake should score first. t-34d7bdf5d6 81288s. smoke/p1, t-a4d9544ed8 5/5, t-62504d3c56 12/12 unchanged. HEARTBEAT d585277e NOW EXHAUSTED (maxRuns 30) - 6m checkup stops unless recreated.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(124, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', '2026-09-27T21:01:27.689Z', '6m checkup FIRE 31. now=21:01:08.612Z. wakes_remaining 15, wakes_done 0 - narrow poll per protocol, no digest/collection/messages. NEW FINDING - maxRuns NOT ENFORCED: d585277e was created with maxRuns 30 and this is fire 31, so the declared cap did not stop it. That makes TWO server-side config-vs-behaviour divergences in the same subsystem: (1) wakes_done never advances from 0, so wakes_remaining==1 is unreachable and the final-wake digest plus all escalation are dead code; (2) maxRuns is not enforced, so the 6m checkup will not self-terminate either. Together: the collector neither advances nor expires, it just polls forever. Correcting my fire-30 report, which wrongly said the heartbeat was exhausted. Deltas over 57s. t-f3ba82ac9c leader 3482s, 5ev/8m, 9/9, 3 open workers = me plus stale 93c8e901 (10778s) and ef8023ae (3482s). t-d1cf43b723 leader 164s, 3ev/8m, 47/58, 11 open, 3 open workers. t-abf10888f3 15311s (~255min silent), 0ev, 26/46, 20 open - 38th drift wake, still lowest-health. t-34d7bdf5d6 81345s. smoke/p1, t-a4d9544ed8 5/5, t-62504d3c56 12/12 unchanged. Next fire ~21:06Z.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b', '', '{"n": 124, "ts": "2026-09-27T21:01:27.689Z", "summary": "6m checkup FIRE 31. now=21:01:08.612Z. wakes_remaining 15, wakes_done 0 - narrow poll per protocol, no digest/collection/messages. NEW FINDING - maxRuns NOT ENFORCED: d585277e was created with maxRuns 30 and this is fire 31, so the declared cap did not stop it. That makes TWO server-side config-vs-behaviour divergences in the same subsystem: (1) wakes_done never advances from 0, so wakes_remaining==1 is unreachable and the final-wake digest plus all escalation are dead code; (2) maxRuns is not enforced, so the 6m checkup will not self-terminate either. Together: the collector neither advances nor expires, it just polls forever. Correcting my fire-30 report, which wrongly said the heartbeat was exhausted. Deltas over 57s. t-f3ba82ac9c leader 3482s, 5ev/8m, 9/9, 3 open workers = me plus stale 93c8e901 (10778s) and ef8023ae (3482s). t-d1cf43b723 leader 164s, 3ev/8m, 47/58, 11 open, 3 open workers. t-abf10888f3 15311s (~255min silent), 0ev, 26/46, 20 open - 38th drift wake, still lowest-health. t-34d7bdf5d6 81345s. smoke/p1, t-a4d9544ed8 5/5, t-62504d3c56 12/12 unchanged. Next fire ~21:06Z.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b", "author_model": ""}');
