679s unclosed). t-abf10888f3: 15311->15474s (~258min silent), 0ev, 26/46, 20 open - 39th consecutive drift wake, still lowest-health in the fleet and the one a real final wake should score first. t-34d7bdf5d6 81508s. smoke/p1, t-a4d9544ed8 5/5, t-62504d3c56 12/12 unchanged. Next fire ~21:06Z.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1480, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-27T21:08:43.566Z', '1. ERROR VERBATIM, all of it: `CELL_RESULT tag=d32k-n28-nomtp ctx=40960 N=28 status=REQUEST_FAIL rc=1`. No send_error, no exception, no OOM. Loaded fine (7953 vs predicted 7869 MiB), never served a request: `BYTES no non-teardown grouped occurrence`, 1 PCIe sample. 2. NEITHER GROW nor PROBE - the client died before issuing anything. Two verifiable lines: 132 passed SIX args, 134 unpacked SEVEN (sys.argv[7]) -> IndexError. My $CTX patch had a trailing space in its match pattern so the replace no-opped and I never verified it applied. Fix proof, non-GPU dry run: now prints `LADDER tokens=[3000,5300,8980,14868,32000] cap=38848` then `GROW_FAIL step=0 ... URLError(ConnectionRefusedError(111))`; was IndexError. 3. DONE: dead cells auto-archived VOID-*; driver needs done marker AND >=1 GROW/PROBE line; archives VOID_/GROW_FAIL/PROBE_FAIL or no-request; GUARDTEST* moved to tests/. 4. RELAUNCHED and running: d32k-n42-nomtp -c 40960, cap=38848, VRAM predicted 9039 vs observed 9471. 80K PREDICTED VRAM (-c 106496): N=28 9,725 79% FITS; N=42 10,895 88.7% FITS; N=56 12,066 98.2% expect OOM; N=84 14,406 117% WILL OOM. Your call on 80K.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1480, "ts": "2026-09-27T21:08:43.566Z", "summary": "1. ERROR VERBATIM, all of it: `CELL_RESULT tag=d32k-n28-nomtp ctx=40960 N=28 status=REQUEST_FAIL rc=1`. No send_error, no exception, no OOM. Loaded fine (7953 vs predicted 7869 MiB), never served a request: `BYTES no non-teardown grouped occurrence`, 1 PCIe sample. 2. NEITHER GROW nor PROBE - the client died before issuing anything. Two verifiable lines: 132 passed SIX args, 134 unpacked SEVEN (sys.argv[7]) -> IndexError. My $CTX patch had a trailing space in its match pattern so the replace no-opped and I never verified it applied. Fix proof, non-GPU dry run: now prints `LADDER tokens=[3000,5300,8980,14868,32000] cap=38848` then `GROW_FAIL step=0 ... URLError(ConnectionRefusedError(111))`; was IndexError. 3. DONE: dead cells auto-archived VOID-*; driver needs done marker AND >=1 GROW/PROBE line; archives VOID_/GROW_FAIL/PROBE_FAIL or no-request; GUARDTEST* moved to tests/. 4. RELAUNCHED and running: d32k-n42-nomtp -c 40960, cap=38848, VRAM predicted 9039 vs observed 9471. 80K PREDICTED VRAM (-c 106496): N=28 9,725 79% FITS; N=42 10,895 88.7% FITS; N=56 12,066 98.2% expect OOM; N=84 14,406 117% WILL OOM. Your call on 80K.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1481, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-27T21:27:20.956Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v13 - HARNESS HYGIENE LANDED; 32K ROW GENUINELY RUNNING. q2drive.sh has 9 VOID lines, a dead-cell rule at line 32, and rc+elapsed teed at line 53. A real VOID marker exists, so auto-void fired. All GUARDTEST artifacts cleared - closing the structural gap that cost three cells. THE 32K CELL IS PAST THE POINT WHERE EVERY PRIOR ONE DIED: d32k-n42-nomtp at ctx=40960 N=42 has two completed prefill phases including 3432 tokens at progress 1.00 in 408 s, ZERO context-overflow errors, rig at 9499 MiB / 100% util. The -c margin fix works in production, not just in GUARDTEST. NO VERDICT CLAIMED: the cell is in prefill, which cannot substitute for the gate metric. CAVEAT: rc-capture is unproven until a real failure exercises it. Held: 8K banked (+18.6%); MTP 2.04x; six-point prefill curve banked; three pre-registered 80K outcomes unchanged. 80K needs predicted VRAM at -c 102400 first.', 'running', '["Harness hygiene verified: 9 VOID lines, dead-cell rule, rc+elapsed teed; auto-void marker exists; GUARDTEST cleared", "d32k-n42-nomtp past the prior death point: 3432 tokens at progress 1.00, zero context-400s, 9499 MiB / 100% util"]', '["Await 32K decode, then 80K; predicted VRAM at -c 102400"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1481, "ts": "2026-09-27T21:27:20.956Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v13 - HARNESS HYGIENE LANDED; 32K ROW GENUINELY RUNNING. q2drive.sh has 9 VOID lines, a dead-cell rule at line 32, and rc+elapsed teed at line 53. A real VOID marker exists, so auto-void fired. All GUARDTEST artifacts cleared - closing the structural gap that cost three cells. THE 32K CELL IS PAST THE POINT WHERE EVERY PRIOR ONE DIED: d32k-n42-nomtp at ctx=40960 N=42 has two completed prefill phases including 3432 tokens at progress 1.00 in 408 s, ZERO context-overflow errors, rig at 9499 MiB / 100% util. The -c margin fix works in production, not just in GUARDTEST. NO VERDICT CLAIMED: the cell is in prefill, which cannot substitute for the gate metric. CAVEAT: rc-capture is unproven until a real failure exercises it. Held: 8K banked (+18.6%); MTP 2.04x; six-point prefill curve banked; three pre-registered 80K outcomes unchanged. 80K needs predicted VRAM at -c 102400 first.", "status": "running", "done": ["Harness hygiene verified: 9 VOID lines, dead-cell rule, rc+elapsed teed; auto-void marker exists; GUARDTEST cleared", "d32k-n42-nomtp past the prior death point: 3432 tokens at progress 1.00, zero context-400s, 9499 MiB / 100% util"], "next": ["Await 32K decode, then 80K; predicted VRAM at -c 102400"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1482, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-27T22:03:16.199Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v15 - I RETRACT LAST TICK''S RIG-ANOMALY FLAG: the idle pid 2217334 is the SAME process now running d32k-n28-nomtp. The driver reuses one server across cells, so a between-cell idle sample is expected. GUARD RE-CONFIRMED A THIRD TIME (result-GT.txt PREFLIGHT_FAIL, required -c 40960), so the -c rule is now proven by three negative tests plus two production cells that ran past the depth where the original three died. 32K IS ADVANCING: 3189 tokens at progress 1.00 in 381 s. No decode number yet. LAST TICK''S FINDING STANDS: prefill used only 7.7% of the Gen1 x4 ceiling, so prefill is NOT PCIe-bound; my turn-1466 ''PCIe-limited'' framing is decode-only and cannot justify ranking work at serving depth. MEASURED: prefill 7.84 tok/s, 18.0 min per 32K request, ~1.3 h at 80K. 8K banked (+18.6%); MTP 2.04x.', 'blocked', '["RETRACTED the rig-anomaly flag: pid 2217334 is the reused server, not a leak; guard re-confirmed a third time", "Turn-1483 prefill finding stands: PCIe-bound in DECODE only, prefill 7.7% of link ceiling"]', '["Worker: shorten the grow target so decode runs, or accept 8K as deepest affordable depth; predicted VRAM for 80K at -c 102400", "OWNER: MTP 2.04x; merge #808+#159"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1482, "ts": "2026-09-27T22:03:16.199Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v15 - I RETRACT LAST TICK''S RIG-ANOMALY FLAG: the idle pid 2217334 is the SAME process now running d32k-n28-nomtp. The driver reuses one server across cells, so a between-cell idle sample is expected. GUARD RE-CONFIRMED A THIRD TIME (result-GT.txt PREFLIGHT_FAIL, required -c 40960), so the -c rule is now proven by three negative tests plus two production cells that ran past the depth where the original three died. 32K IS ADVANCING: 3189 tokens at progress 1.00 in 381 s. No decode number yet. LAST TICK''S FINDING STANDS: prefill used only 7.7% of the Gen1 x4 ceiling, so prefill is NOT PCIe-bound; my turn-1466 ''PCIe-limited'' framing is decode-only and cannot justify ranking work at serving depth. MEASURED: prefill 7.84 tok/s, 18.0 min per 32K request, ~1.3 h at 80K. 8K banked (+18.6%); MTP 2.04x.", "status": "blocked", "done": ["RETRACTED the rig-anomaly flag: pid 2217334 is the reused server, not a leak; guard re-confirmed a third time", "Turn-1483 prefill finding stands: PCIe-bound in DECODE only, prefill 7.7% of link ceiling"], "next": ["Worker: shorten the grow target so decode runs, or accept 8K as deepest affordable depth; predicted VRAM for 80K at -c 102400", "OWNER: MTP 2.04x; merge #808+#159"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
