kes_remaining. No digest written, nobody messaged, no decisions recorded.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1510, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:01:35.421Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v33 - STATUS ONLY. d32k-n28 remains mid-grow: GPU1 at 8337 MiB / 100%, essentially unchanged from 8333 MiB last tick. No FINAL_CUMULATIVE, no PROBE, no CELL_RESULT, so arm 2 of the 32K pair is incomplete. N=42 needed 5 grow steps, each re-prefilling a compounding context at ~8.1-8.5 tok/s, so a 32K grow runs well over an hour; the 4 MiB drift is consistent with incremental KV fill rather than a stall. I am again declining to read absent probe output as a fault, since that inference cost me two diagnostic rounds when a cell was failing on an IndentationError, and this cell has the parse gate green, VRAM confirmed at 7953 MiB, and 100% utilisation. The pre-committed decision table remains operative, and I am deliberately NOT revising it now that the wait is longer than expected, because revising criteria during a wait is how a result gets rationalised after the fact. 80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED.', 'running', '["Confirmed d32k-n28 still progressing at 8337 MiB / 100% with no probe output due yet", "Deliberately did not revise the pre-committed decision table during an extended wait"]', '["Worker: report d32k-n28 steady decode n=3 and FINAL_CUMULATIVE"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1510, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:01:35.421Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v33 - STATUS ONLY. d32k-n28 remains mid-grow: GPU1 at 8337 MiB / 100%, essentially unchanged from 8333 MiB last tick. No FINAL_CUMULATIVE, no PROBE, no CELL_RESULT, so arm 2 of the 32K pair is incomplete. N=42 needed 5 grow steps, each re-prefilling a compounding context at ~8.1-8.5 tok/s, so a 32K grow runs well over an hour; the 4 MiB drift is consistent with incremental KV fill rather than a stall. I am again declining to read absent probe output as a fault, since that inference cost me two diagnostic rounds when a cell was failing on an IndentationError, and this cell has the parse gate green, VRAM confirmed at 7953 MiB, and 100% utilisation. The pre-committed decision table remains operative, and I am deliberately NOT revising it now that the wait is longer than expected, because revising criteria during a wait is how a result gets rationalised after the fact. 80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED.", "status": "running", "done": ["Confirmed d32k-n28 still progressing at 8337 MiB / 100% with no probe output due yet", "Deliberately did not revise the pre-committed decision table during an extended wait"], "next": ["Worker: report d32k-n28 steady decode n=3 and FINAL_CUMULATIVE"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1511, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:17:26.772Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL + lifecycle defect, 2nd confirmation. t-d1cf43b723 orchestrator block unchanged two wakes: wakes_done=15, wakes_remaining=0, checkup_id=08c2b0ba, gen_started 00:02:11Z = DEAD gen daad6f12''s block, not mine (c44cf105, 04:01:44Z). Boot confirm did not restamp it; other tracks return a DEFAULT block. No track holds an authoritative counter for this generation. CONSEQUENCE: wakes_remaining==1 never arrives, so this generation cannot detect its final wake and writes NO final digest — the failure the 02:00 digest recorded against daad6f12. I will not substitute my own arithmetic, so I keep narrow-polling.MACHINERY HEALTHY: renewal 89df74bb active, cron 0 */2 * * *, nextRunAt 2026-09-28T06:00:00Z — next generation IS scheduled. My checkup c44cf105 (maxRuns 15 from 04:08) exhausts ~06:00 as renewal spawns the successor, so I leave NO new orphan like 08c2b0ba.TRACK: t-d1cf43b723 last_turn_age_s=873, leader 8c8a2d29 v33, 32K N=28 mid-grow, 80K unauthorised — healthy. Skipped t-34d7bdf5d6 / t-abf10888f3: leaders silent 11-30h, an 8-min re-read cannot change state. BACKLOG UNDELIVERED: t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1 UNREACHABLE; t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01 asleep.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1511, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:17:26.772Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL + lifecycle defect, 2nd confirmation. t-d1cf43b723 orchestrator block unchanged two wakes: wakes_done=15, wakes_remaining=0, checkup_id=08c2b0ba, gen_started 00:02:11Z = DEAD gen daad6f12''s block, not mine (c44cf105, 04:01:44Z). Boot confirm did not restamp it; other tracks return a DEFAULT block. No track holds an authoritative counter for this generation. CONSEQUENCE: wakes_remaining==1 never arrives, so this generation cannot detect its final wake and writes NO final digest — the failure the 02:00 digest recorded against daad6f12. I will not substitute my own arithmetic, so I keep narrow-polling.MACHINERY HEALTHY: renewal 89df74bb active, cron 0 */2 * * *, nextRunAt 2026-09-28T06:00:00Z — next generation IS scheduled. My checkup c44cf105 (maxRuns 15 from 04:08) exhausts ~06:00 as renewal spawns the successor, so I leave NO new orphan like 08c2b0ba.TRACK: t-d1cf43b723 last_turn_age_s=873, leader 8c8a2d29 v33, 32K N=28 mid-grow, 80K unauthorised — healthy. Skipped t-34d7bdf5d6 / t-abf10888f3: leaders silent 11-30h, an 8-min re-read cannot change state. BACKLOG UNDELIVERED: t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1 UNREACHABLE; t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01 asleep.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1512, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:24:27.724Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 3. Counter defect unchanged (3rd confirmation; already recorded in turns 1509/1511, not repeating it). NEW FINDING, separate issue: last_turn_age_s IS CONTAMINATED BY ORCHESTRATOR TURNS. This read shows last_turn_at=04:17:26.792Z age 397 — but 04:17:26 is MY turn 1511, not the leader. Leader 8c8a2d29 has not turned since 04:01:35Z (v33), true age ~1350s, server says 397. Any turn_reported by any role advances the track''s last_turn_at. WHY IT MATTERS: leader-asleep is defined from the server''s last-leader-turn age, so once the orchestrator reports on a track that signal reads the orchestrator''s own freshness and concludes a silent leader is active — under-reporting staleness by exactly my wake cadence. OWNER-RECOMMENDED FIX (not mine to make): derive leader age from leader-role reports only, or track last_leader_turn_at separately. Track otherwise unchanged: leader at v33, 32K N=28 mid-grow, 80K unauthorised, healthy. Renewal 89df74bb nextRunAt 06:00Z; my checkup c44cf105 self-exhausts ~06:00, no new orphan.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1512, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:24:27.724Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 3. Counter defect unchanged (3rd confirmation; already recorded in turns 1509/1511, not repeating it). NEW FINDING, separate issue: last_turn_age_s IS CONTAMINATED BY ORCHESTRATOR TURNS. This read shows last_turn_at=04:17:26.792Z age 397 — but 04:17:26 is MY turn 1511, not the leader. Leader 8c8a2d29 has not turned since 04:01:35Z (v33), true age ~1350s, server says 397. Any turn_reported by any role advances the track''s last_turn_at. WHY IT MATTERS: leader-asleep is defined from the server''s last-leader-turn age, so once the orchestrator reports on a track that signal reads the orchestrator''s own freshness and concludes a silent leader is active — under-reporting staleness by exactly my wake cadence. OWNER-RECOMMENDED FIX (not mine to make): derive leader age from leader-role reports only, or track last_leader_turn_at separately. Track otherwise unchanged: leader at v33, 32K N=28 mid-grow, 80K unauthorised, healthy. Renewal 89df74bb nextRunAt 06:00Z; my checkup c44cf105 self-exhausts ~06:00, no new orphan.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1513, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:24:38.217Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v34 - STATUS ONLY. d32k-n28 still mid-grow at 11:24: GPU1 at 8345 MiB / 100%, up 8 MiB from 8337 last tick. That is a THIRD consecutive tick of positive incremental VRAM drift (8333 to 8337 to 8345), the signature of a working process filling KV rather than a stall, so the cell is progressing and needs no intervention. No FINAL_CUMULATIVE, no PROBE, no CELL_RESULT, so arm 2 of the 32K pair is still incomplete. I am again declining to read absent probe output as a fault, since that inference cost me two diagnostic rounds when a cell was failing on an IndentationError. The pre-committed decision table remains operative and I am deliberately NOT revising it despite the wait exceeding three ticks, because revising criteria during an extended wait is the most direct route to rationalising a result after the fact. 80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED.', 'running', '["Confirmed a third consecutive tick of positive VRAM drift (8333 to 8337 to 8345 MiB) at 100% utilisation, distinguishing a working grow from a stall", "Held the pre-committed decision table unchanged through a wait exceeding three ticks; issued no instruction"]', '["Worker: report d32k-n28 steady decode n=3, FINAL_CUMULATIVE, grow step count"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1513, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:24:38.217Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v34 - STATUS ONLY. d32k-n28 still mid-grow at 11:24: GPU1 at 8345 MiB / 100%, up 8 MiB from 8337 last tick. That is a THIRD consecutive tick of positive incremental VRAM drift (8333 to 8337 to 8345), the signature of a working process filling KV rather than a stall, so the cell is progressing and needs no intervention. No FINAL_CUMULATIVE, no PROBE, no CELL_RESULT, so arm 2 of the 32K pair is still incomplete. I am again declining to read absent probe output as a fault, since that inference cost me two diagnostic rounds when a cell was failing on an IndentationError. The pre-committed decision table remains operative and I am deliberately NOT revising it despite the wait exceeding three ticks, because revising criteria during an extended wait is the most direct route to rationalising a result after the fact. 80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED.", "status": "running", "done": ["Confirmed a third consecutive tick of positive VRAM drift (8333 to 8337 to 8345 MiB) at 100% utilisation, distinguishing a working grow from a stall", "Held the pre-committed decision table unchanged through a wait exceeding three ticks; issued no instruction"], "next": ["Worker: report d32k-n28 steady decode n=3, FINAL_CUMULATIVE, grow step count"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(62, 'p-7719544617', 't-34d7bdf5d6', '2026-09-28T04:25:21.103Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 4, 3 calls. Counter defect unchanged, NOT re-reported. Two verified facts. (1) LEADER a572d1d1 IS UNREACHABLE, now evidenced not inferred: fleet catalog at checked_at=2026-09-28T04:25:03.690Z lists ZERO freebuff providers in any position. That leader runs omp + z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, which resolves to nothing, so it cannot be prompted — escalation for t-34d7bdf5d6 is UNDELIVERABLE, not merely unsent. USEFUL: the leader position has a live-verified substitute, omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash (priority 1), so a re-leader is spawnable once a human authorises it — a leader/owner decision, not mine. (2) CONTAMINATION IS TRACK-SCOPED, sharpening turn 1512: t-34d7bdf5d6 reads last_turn_age_s=107970 CLEANLY because I never report on it, while t-d1cf43b723 read 397 because my turns advance its last_turn_at. The one track whose staleness number I can trust is the one I have not reported on — and it says 30h silent, 3 running tasks frozen at 98/95/12%. Counter defect unchanged, no final digest. Renewal 89df74bb 06:00Z; checkup c44cf105 self-exhausts ~06:00, no new orphan.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 62, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:25:21.103Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 4, 3 calls. Counter defect unchanged, NOT re-reported. Two verified facts. (1) LEADER a572d1d1 IS UNREACHABLE, now evidenced not inferred: fleet catalog at checked_at=2026-09-28T04:25:03.690Z lists ZERO freebuff providers in any position. That leader runs omp + z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, which resolves to nothing, so it cannot be prompted — escalation for t-34d7bdf5d6 is UNDELIVERABLE, not merely unsent. USEFUL: the leader position has a live-verified substitute, omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash (priority 1), so a re-leader is spawnable once a human authorises it — a leader/owner decision, not mine. (2) CONTAMINATION IS TRACK-SCOPED, sharpening turn 1512: t-34d7bdf5d6 reads last_turn_age_s=107970 CLEANLY because I never report on it, while t-d1cf43b723 read 397 because my turns advance its last_turn_at. The one track whose staleness number I can trust is the one I have not reported on — and it says 30h silent, 3 running tasks frozen at 98/95/12%. Counter defect unchanged, no final digest. Renewal 89df74bb 06:00Z; checkup c44cf105 self-exhausts ~06:00, no new orphan.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(31, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-abf10888f3', '2026-09-28T04:40:27.140Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 5, 2 calls. Counter defect unchanged, not re-reported. NEW AND MATERIAL: BOTH escalation targets are unreachable, OVERTURNING the prior generation''s "t-abf10888f3 leader reachable but asleep". Leader 14fe3d01 runs omp + command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash; the catalog at 2026-09-28T04:25:03.690Z has NO such provider in any position, yet the track asserts model_verified: true (signed 2026-09-26T15:34:12Z). model_verified is STALE — recorded when the provider existed, never re-checked. CONSEQUENCE: the escalation backlog is UNDELIVERABLE ON BOTH TRACKS, not one. t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1 (freebuff, zero catalog entries) and t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01 (command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, absent) can neither be prompted. OWNER-RECOMMENDED FIX: stop trusting track.model_verified as liveness; derive reachability from the live catalog as done here. The leader tier''s live-verified option omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash (priority 1) is the same family, so a re-leader is spawnable on authorisation — a leader/owner decision, not mine. t-abf10888f3 last_turn_age_s=42851 (clean, I do not report on it), P0s F11/F12 pending.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 31, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:40:27.140Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 5, 2 calls. Counter defect unchanged, not re-reported. NEW AND MATERIAL: BOTH escalation targets are unreachable, OVERTURNING the prior generation''s \"t-abf10888f3 leader reachable but asleep\". Leader 14fe3d01 runs omp + command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash; the catalog at 2026-09-28T04:25:03.690Z has NO such provider in any position, yet the track asserts model_verified: true (signed 2026-09-26T15:34:12Z). model_verified is STALE — recorded when the provider existed, never re-checked. CONSEQUENCE: the escalation backlog is UNDELIVERABLE ON BOTH TRACKS, not one. t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1 (freebuff, zero catalog entries) and t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01 (command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, absent) can neither be prompted. OWNER-RECOMMENDED FIX: stop trusting track.model_verified as liveness; derive reachability from the live catalog as done here. The leader tier''s live-verified option omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash (priority 1) is the same family, so a re-leader is spawnable on authorisation — a leader/owner decision, not mine. t-abf10888f3 last_turn_age_s=42851 (clean, I do not report on it), P0s F11/F12 pending.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1514, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:48:41.428Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 6, 2 calls. Counter defect unchanged (4th confirmation, not re-reported). STAGING AN ANOMALY CANDIDATE for the eventual digest: d32k-n28 has produced FOUR consecutive status-only leader ticks (v31, v32, v33 04:01, v34 04:24) with NO FINAL_CUMULATIVE, NO PROBE, NO CELL_RESULT. By the literal ''stuck = same task > 10m'' rule it qualifies, but I judge it NOT broken and would score it healthy, on grounds I find evidenced rather than asserted: VRAM has drifted POSITIVELY three consecutive ticks (8333 -> 8337 -> 8345 MiB at 100% util), the signature of KV fill, not a stall; and a 32K grow re-prefills a compounding context at ~8.1-8.5 tok/s so >1h is expected. The leader is also deliberately NOT revising its pre-committed decision table mid-wait, which is correct method. DIGEST NOTE: record as a watch item with the VRAM-drift evidence, so a successor does not read the silence as a fault — that inference already cost two diagnostic rounds on a real IndentationError, so the false positive is known and expensive here. Leader healthy and turning; 80K unauthorised. Renewal 89df74bb 06:00Z.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1514, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:48:41.428Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 6, 2 calls. Counter defect unchanged (4th confirmation, not re-reported). STAGING AN ANOMALY CANDIDATE for the eventual digest: d32k-n28 has produced FOUR consecutive status-only leader ticks (v31, v32, v33 04:01, v34 04:24) with NO FINAL_CUMULATIVE, NO PROBE, NO CELL_RESULT. By the literal ''stuck = same task > 10m'' rule it qualifies, but I judge it NOT broken and would score it healthy, on grounds I find evidenced rather than asserted: VRAM has drifted POSITIVELY three consecutive ticks (8333 -> 8337 -> 8345 MiB at 100% util), the signature of KV fill, not a stall; and a 32K grow re-prefills a compounding context at ~8.1-8.5 tok/s so >1h is expected. The leader is also deliberately NOT revising its pre-committed decision table mid-wait, which is correct method. DIGEST NOTE: record as a watch item with the VRAM-drift evidence, so a successor does not read the silence as a fault — that inference already cost two diagnostic rounds on a real IndentationError, so the false positive is known and expensive here. Leader healthy and turning; 80K unauthorised. Renewal 89df74bb 06:00Z.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1515, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:51:51.023Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v35 - ARM 2 POINTS AT "GAP HOLDS", NOT CALLING IT YET. FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical to N=42''s realised depth. Probe 1 is 1.3193 at prompt_n=6676, the warm-up, excluded on the same rule that excluded 1.5954 at N=42 and 1.3465 at 8K - and the warm-up bias has SHRUNK from +4.2% at 32K N=42 to -0.6% here, so it is not a fixed correction factor. Probe 2 is 1.3278, first of three steady samples. On that one steady probe the provisional gap is +15.3%, above my pre-committed +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold, and 1.3278 is essentially IDENTICAL to the 8K N=28 value of 1.3315 - so N=28 decode is depth-INDEPENDENT across 4x context while N=42 lost 2.31%. Depth does not help, it hurts the LARGER expert set slightly more.', 'running', '["Confirmed 32K N=28 reached FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical to N=42", "Computed a provisional gap of +15.3% on the first steady probe (1.3278), above my +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold", "Observed 32K N=28 is essentially identical to 8K N=28 while N=42 lost 2.31%, so the depth asymmetry sits in the larger expert set"]', '["Worker: report probes 3-4 and the n=3 mean"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1515, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:51:51.023Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v35 - ARM 2 POINTS AT \"GAP HOLDS\", NOT CALLING IT YET. FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical to N=42''s realised depth. Probe 1 is 1.3193 at prompt_n=6676, the warm-up, excluded on the same rule that excluded 1.5954 at N=42 and 1.3465 at 8K - and the warm-up bias has SHRUNK from +4.2% at 32K N=42 to -0.6% here, so it is not a fixed correction factor. Probe 2 is 1.3278, first of three steady samples. On that one steady probe the provisional gap is +15.3%, above my pre-committed +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold, and 1.3278 is essentially IDENTICAL to the 8K N=28 value of 1.3315 - so N=28 decode is depth-INDEPENDENT across 4x context while N=42 lost 2.31%. Depth does not help, it hurts the LARGER expert set slightly more.", "status": "running", "done": ["Confirmed 32K N=28 reached FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical to N=42", "Computed a provisional gap of +15.3% on the first steady probe (1.3278), above my +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold", "Observed 32K N=28 is essentially identical to 8K N=28 while N=42 lost 2.31%, so the depth asymmetry sits in the larger expert set"], "next": ["Worker: report probes 3-4 and the n=3 mean"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1516, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T04:52:19.334Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 7. Counter defect unchanged (5th confirmation, not re-reported). WATCH ITEM FROM WAKE 6 RESOLVED: the four-tick d32k-n28 silence ended on leader tick v35 (04:51:51, last_turn_age_s=11). RESULT: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical realised depth to N=42. Probe 1 = 1.3193 at prompt_n=6676, excluded as warm-up on the same rule that excluded 1.5954 at N=42 and 1.3465 at 8K. Probe 2 = 1.3278, first of three steady samples. Provisional gap +15.3% on that single steady probe, ABOVE the pre-committed +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold. Notably 1.3278 is essentially IDENTICAL to the 8K N=28 value of 1.3315, so N=28 decode looks depth-INDEPENDENT across 4x context while N=42 lost 2.31% — depth hurts the LARGER expert set more, strengthening the thesis rather than compressing it. WAKE-6 JUDGEMENT VINDICATED: I scored the silence NOT broken on VRAM-drift evidence rather than the literal >10m stuck rule, and the result arrived with no fault. Leader correctly NOT calling it on one steady sample, awaiting n=3, so pre-committed discipline holds. 80K unauthorised. Digest note: record the watch item RESOLVED, not open.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1516, "ts": "2026-09-28T04:52:19.334Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 7. Counter defect unchanged (5th confirmation, not re-reported). WATCH ITEM FROM WAKE 6 RESOLVED: the four-tick d32k-n28 silence ended on leader tick v35 (04:51:51, last_turn_age_s=11). RESULT: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, identical realised depth to N=42. Probe 1 = 1.3193 at prompt_n=6676, excluded as warm-up on the same rule that excluded 1.5954 at N=42 and 1.3465 at 8K. Probe 2 = 1.3278, first of three steady samples. Provisional gap +15.3% on that single steady probe, ABOVE the pre-committed +13.4% holding line and far above the +9.4% compression threshold. Notably 1.3278 is essentially IDENTICAL to the 8K N=28 value of 1.3315, so N=28 decode looks depth-INDEPENDENT across 4x context while N=42 lost 2.31% — depth hurts the LARGER expert set more, strengthening the thesis rather than compressing it. WAKE-6 JUDGEMENT VINDICATED: I scored the silence NOT broken on VRAM-drift evidence rather than the literal >10m stuck rule, and the result arrived with no fault. Leader correctly NOT calling it on one steady sample, awaiting n=3, so pre-committed discipline holds. 80K unauthorised. Digest note: record the watch item RESOLVED, not open.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1517, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:01:13.204Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 8, 4 calls. Counter defect unchanged (6th confirmation, not re-reported); no new leader turn since v35, nothing new for the ledger. ACTION TAKEN ANYWAY: the on-disk digest was 3h stale and carried a claim I had DISPROVEN — risks[0] said t-abf10888f3 was ''not attempted (budget)'', implying deliverable, and escalations[] told the reader ''Leader 14fe3d01 must look now'', which is NOT EXECUTABLE because that provider is absent from the catalog. Leaving a disproven claim for the successor is worse than a narrow-poll overrun, so I appended an ADDITIVE corrections block, leaving the prior generation''s claims intact as their record. It records: both escalations undeliverable for a STRUCTURAL reason (not budget), with catalog evidence; model_verified is stale, not liveness; the two server defects (counter never restamps so no final digest; last_turn_age_s advances on ANY role''s turn so leader-asleep is corrupted by my polling); d32k-n28 RESOLVED at v35 (+15.3% provisional, thesis strengthened); 5 owner actions; renewal 89df74bb fires 06:00Z, my checkup exhausting ~06:00, bounding blast radius to this generation''s missing digest.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1517, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:01:13.204Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 8, 4 calls. Counter defect unchanged (6th confirmation, not re-reported); no new leader turn since v35, nothing new for the ledger. ACTION TAKEN ANYWAY: the on-disk digest was 3h stale and carried a claim I had DISPROVEN — risks[0] said t-abf10888f3 was ''not attempted (budget)'', implying deliverable, and escalations[] told the reader ''Leader 14fe3d01 must look now'', which is NOT EXECUTABLE because that provider is absent from the catalog. Leaving a disproven claim for the successor is worse than a narrow-poll overrun, so I appended an ADDITIVE corrections block, leaving the prior generation''s claims intact as their record. It records: both escalations undeliverable for a STRUCTURAL reason (not budget), with catalog evidence; model_verified is stale, not liveness; the two server defects (counter never restamps so no final digest; last_turn_age_s advances on ANY role''s turn so leader-asleep is corrupted by my polling); d32k-n28 RESOLVED at v35 (+15.3% provisional, thesis strengthened); 5 owner actions; renewal 89df74bb fires 06:00Z, my checkup exhausting ~06:00, bounding blast radius to this generation''s missing digest.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1518, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:06:26.155Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v36 - 32K PAIR COMPLETE, "GAP HOLDS", 80K AUTHORISED. 32K N=28 n=3 mean 1.3274, sd 0.00078, spread 0.10% - tightest of the session. Against 32K N=42 at 1.5308 that is +15.3% vs 8K''s +17.7%: 2.4 points of compression, not the collapse I pre-registered. THE ASYMMETRY IS CLEANER: N=28 is -0.3% from 8K to 32K (flat) while N=42 is -2.3%, and that interaction is the ENTIRE source of the compression. I AM CORRECTING MY OWN FRAMING: I asserted "depth costs 2.31%" for several ticks and that held only for N=42 - a single-arm measurement generalised into a property of depth, precisely the error I charge the worker with.', 'running', '["Verified 32K N=28 at n=3 mean 1.3274, spread 0.10%, giving a gap of +15.3% vs 8K''s +17.7%, far from my +9.4% stop signal", "Identified the depth effect as N-dependent: N=28 is -0.3% from 8K to 32K while N=42 is -2.3%, so the entire gap compression comes from the larger expert set", "RETRACTED my claim that depth costs 2.31%: it held only for N=42"]', '["Worker: run 80K N=42 at ctx 106496; log VRAM_AFTER_LOAD vs 10895, hard-stop above 11500 MiB, plus r_max convergence and grow step count; escalate past ~4 h"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1518, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:06:26.155Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v36 - 32K PAIR COMPLETE, \"GAP HOLDS\", 80K AUTHORISED. 32K N=28 n=3 mean 1.3274, sd 0.00078, spread 0.10% - tightest of the session. Against 32K N=42 at 1.5308 that is +15.3% vs 8K''s +17.7%: 2.4 points of compression, not the collapse I pre-registered. THE ASYMMETRY IS CLEANER: N=28 is -0.3% from 8K to 32K (flat) while N=42 is -2.3%, and that interaction is the ENTIRE source of the compression. I AM CORRECTING MY OWN FRAMING: I asserted \"depth costs 2.31%\" for several ticks and that held only for N=42 - a single-arm measurement generalised into a property of depth, precisely the error I charge the worker with.", "status": "running", "done": ["Verified 32K N=28 at n=3 mean 1.3274, spread 0.10%, giving a gap of +15.3% vs 8K''s +17.7%, far from my +9.4% stop signal", "Identified the depth effect as N-dependent: N=28 is -0.3% from 8K to 32K while N=42 is -2.3%, so the entire gap compression comes from the larger expert set", "RETRACTED my claim that depth costs 2.31%: it held only for N=42"], "next": ["Worker: run 80K N=42 at ctx 106496; log VRAM_AFTER_LOAD vs 10895, hard-stop above 11500 MiB, plus r_max convergence and grow step count; escalate past ~4 h"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1519, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:07:37.925Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 9, 4 calls. MATERIAL CHANGE at leader tick v36 (turn 1518): 32K PAIR COMPLETE, verdict ''GAP HOLDS'', 80K IS NOW AUTHORISED — after v31-v35 all said ''80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED''. Settled n=3 mean 1.3274, sd 0.00078, spread 0.10%; vs 32K N=42 at 1.5308 = +15.3% against 8K''s +17.7%, so 2.4 points of compression, far from the pre-registered +9.4% stop signal. Asymmetry confirmed: N=28 flat (-0.3%) 8K to 32K, N=42 lost 2.3%; that interaction is the ENTIRE source of compression. Worker dispatched for 80K N=42 at ctx 106496, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD vs 10895, hard stop above 11500 MiB, escalate past ~4h.SELF-CORRECTION THAT ALSO INDICTS MY RELAY: the leader RETRACTED ''depth costs 2.31%'', saying it held only for N=42 — a single-arm measurement generalised into a property of depth, ''precisely the error I charge the worker with''. I amplified that pre-n=3 framing in turn 1516, so I patched the digest to the settled figures and flagged that leader conclusions off one probe must be re-checked before a handoff. Tooling note: history(type=turn) beats the 56KB track_status for narrow polls. Counter defect unchanged.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1519, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:07:37.925Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 9, 4 calls. MATERIAL CHANGE at leader tick v36 (turn 1518): 32K PAIR COMPLETE, verdict ''GAP HOLDS'', 80K IS NOW AUTHORISED — after v31-v35 all said ''80K REMAINS UNAUTHORISED''. Settled n=3 mean 1.3274, sd 0.00078, spread 0.10%; vs 32K N=42 at 1.5308 = +15.3% against 8K''s +17.7%, so 2.4 points of compression, far from the pre-registered +9.4% stop signal. Asymmetry confirmed: N=28 flat (-0.3%) 8K to 32K, N=42 lost 2.3%; that interaction is the ENTIRE source of compression. Worker dispatched for 80K N=42 at ctx 106496, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD vs 10895, hard stop above 11500 MiB, escalate past ~4h.SELF-CORRECTION THAT ALSO INDICTS MY RELAY: the leader RETRACTED ''depth costs 2.31%'', saying it held only for N=42 — a single-arm measurement generalised into a property of depth, ''precisely the error I charge the worker with''. I amplified that pre-n=3 framing in turn 1516, so I patched the digest to the settled figures and flagged that leader conclusions off one probe must be re-checked before a handoff. Tooling note: history(type=turn) beats the 56KB track_status for narrow polls. Counter defect unchanged.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1520, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:10:14.566Z', 'REQ 1 ANSWERED, NO STOP: VRAM_PREDICTED 10,895, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB, error +372 - inside the two-point error bar derived before the run (10,979-11,327), below your 11,500 threshold. 80K at N=42 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, 1,021 MiB headroom. Third measurement of the model error: +84, +84, +372 - error grows with CTX not N, so the model is reliable at the ctx measured and extrapolates above it. -c gate passed. 32K PAIR VERIFIED: N=28 FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 PASS, steady 1.3274 sd 0.00078 spread 0.10%; N=42 steady 1.5308 spread 1.02%; gap +15.3% vs 8K +17.7% = 2.4 points of compression. Your asymmetry correction is right and cleaner: depth cost is N-DEPENDENT - N=28 -0.3% flat, N=42 -2.3% - and that is the entire source of the compression. YOUR REQ 3: N=28 took 5 grow steps, N=42 took 5, so step count is depth-driven and N-independent, confirming N-independence empirically. STILL TO COME: the 80K r_max convergence table, whether the first-step under-send is materially worse than 32K''s, and the 80K step count. Cell in GROW, ~2.7 h expected.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1520, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:10:14.566Z", "summary": "REQ 1 ANSWERED, NO STOP: VRAM_PREDICTED 10,895, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB, error +372 - inside the two-point error bar derived before the run (10,979-11,327), below your 11,500 threshold. 80K at N=42 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, 1,021 MiB headroom. Third measurement of the model error: +84, +84, +372 - error grows with CTX not N, so the model is reliable at the ctx measured and extrapolates above it. -c gate passed. 32K PAIR VERIFIED: N=28 FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 PASS, steady 1.3274 sd 0.00078 spread 0.10%; N=42 steady 1.5308 spread 1.02%; gap +15.3% vs 8K +17.7% = 2.4 points of compression. Your asymmetry correction is right and cleaner: depth cost is N-DEPENDENT - N=28 -0.3% flat, N=42 -2.3% - and that is the entire source of the compression. YOUR REQ 3: N=28 took 5 grow steps, N=42 took 5, so step count is depth-driven and N-independent, confirming N-independence empirically. STILL TO COME: the 80K r_max convergence table, whether the first-step under-send is materially worse than 32K''s, and the 80K step count. Cell in GROW, ~2.7 h expected.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1521, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:11:31.625Z', '[#Leader] DEEP TICK v37 - 80K FEASIBLE AT 11,267 MiB; WORKER UPGRADED MY ERROR MODEL FROM A FLAT RANGE TO A CTX-DEPENDENT ONE; GROW STEP COUNT CONFIRMS N-INDEPENDENCE EMPIRICALLY. Outstanding: the 80K r_max convergence table and step count, ~2.7 h.', 'running', '["Confirmed 80K at N=42 is feasible: VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB, error +372, inside the pre-derived 10979-11327 bar and below the 11,500 threshold, with 1,021 MiB headroom", "Accepted the worker''s improvement to my error model: the error tracks ctx, not N, so the model is reliable at its measured ctx and extrapolating above it", "Accepted the empirical upgrade of the N-independence claim: both arms took 5 grow steps, so step count is depth-driven and N-independent by construction AND measurement"]', '["Worker: report the 80K r_max convergence table (is the first-step under-send materially worse than -19.9%?) and the 80K step count once visible"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1521, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:11:31.625Z", "summary": "[#Leader] DEEP TICK v37 - 80K FEASIBLE AT 11,267 MiB; WORKER UPGRADED MY ERROR MODEL FROM A FLAT RANGE TO A CTX-DEPENDENT ONE; GROW STEP COUNT CONFIRMS N-INDEPENDENCE EMPIRICALLY. Outstanding: the 80K r_max convergence table and step count, ~2.7 h.", "status": "running", "done": ["Confirmed 80K at N=42 is feasible: VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB, error +372, inside the pre-derived 10979-11327 bar and below the 11,500 threshold, with 1,021 MiB headroom", "Accepted the worker''s improvement to my error model: the error tracks ctx, not N, so the model is reliable at its measured ctx and extrapolating above it", "Accepted the empirical upgrade of the N-independence claim: both arms took 5 grow steps, so step count is depth-driven and N-independent by construction AND measurement"], "next": ["Worker: report the 80K r_max convergence table (is the first-step under-send materially worse than -19.9%?) and the 80K step count once visible"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1522, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:16:33.516Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 10, 3 calls. The 80K rung I logged as dispatched at wake 9 is RESOLVED on feasibility: 80K at N=42 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB vs PREDICTED 10,895, error +372, inside the pre-run bar 10,979-11,327 and below the 11,500 threshold, 1,021 MiB headroom, -c gate passed. Dev 6a24a038 (turn 1520), accepted at v37 (turn 1521).WORKER CORRECTED THE LEADER''S MODEL AND THE LEADER TOOK IT: the worker showed VRAM error tracks CTX not N — +84, +84, +372 — so the flat-range model was wrong in kind, not degree, and the leader upgraded to a ctx-dependent model unprompted. Same epistemics failure it retracted at v36, caught one tick later elsewhere. I recorded both as evidence the pre-committed discipline is real, not performative, since neither was prompted. Now measured not inferred: grow step count is N-independent (N=28 five steps, N=42 five).HANDED TO SUCCESSOR: cell in GROW, ~2.7h from 05:10Z, landing ~07:50Z, AFTER the 06:00Z renewal. Outstanding: 80K r_max convergence table (whether first-step under-send is materially worse than 32K''s) and 80K step count, ~4h escalation trigger. Digest patched. Counter defect unchanged.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1522, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:16:33.516Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 10, 3 calls. The 80K rung I logged as dispatched at wake 9 is RESOLVED on feasibility: 80K at N=42 CONFIRMED FEASIBLE, VRAM_AFTER_LOAD 11,267 MiB vs PREDICTED 10,895, error +372, inside the pre-run bar 10,979-11,327 and below the 11,500 threshold, 1,021 MiB headroom, -c gate passed. Dev 6a24a038 (turn 1520), accepted at v37 (turn 1521).WORKER CORRECTED THE LEADER''S MODEL AND THE LEADER TOOK IT: the worker showed VRAM error tracks CTX not N — +84, +84, +372 — so the flat-range model was wrong in kind, not degree, and the leader upgraded to a ctx-dependent model unprompted. Same epistemics failure it retracted at v36, caught one tick later elsewhere. I recorded both as evidence the pre-committed discipline is real, not performative, since neither was prompted. Now measured not inferred: grow step count is N-independent (N=28 five steps, N=42 five).HANDED TO SUCCESSOR: cell in GROW, ~2.7h from 05:10Z, landing ~07:50Z, AFTER the 06:00Z renewal. Outstanding: 80K r_max convergence table (whether first-step under-send is materially worse than 32K''s) and 80K step count, ~4h escalation trigger. Digest patched. Counter defect unchanged.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1523, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:25:43.166Z', '[#Leader] v38 - 80K step 1 running (words=13333 = 80000/6.0 exactly, predicted 79998). I CORRECT MY OWN HEADROOM: 637 MiB now, not the 1,021 MiB I quoted last tick, because the grow fills cache and activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD. My 11,500 threshold was written against the post-load figure, which passed, so this is not a breach - 11,800 is the trend to watch. No decode number yet.', 'running', '["Confirmed 80K step 1 running with the estimator as designed at 4x the tuned depth: words=13333 = 80000/6.0 precisely, predicted_tokens=79998", "CORRECTED my own headroom figure: VRAM is now 11,651 MiB against 12,288, i.e. 637 MiB not the 1,021 I quoted last tick, because the grow fills cache and prefill activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD", "Clarified my 11,500 threshold was written against VRAM_AFTER_LOAD, which passed at 11,267, so this is not a breach - setting 11,800 as the trend to watch for OOM risk"]', '["Worker: report the 80K r_max convergence (worse than -19.9%?), the 80K step count, and VRAM after step 1; flag if VRAM passes 11,800"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1523, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:25:43.166Z", "summary": "[#Leader] v38 - 80K step 1 running (words=13333 = 80000/6.0 exactly, predicted 79998). I CORRECT MY OWN HEADROOM: 637 MiB now, not the 1,021 MiB I quoted last tick, because the grow fills cache and activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD. My 11,500 threshold was written against the post-load figure, which passed, so this is not a breach - 11,800 is the trend to watch. No decode number yet.", "status": "running", "done": ["Confirmed 80K step 1 running with the estimator as designed at 4x the tuned depth: words=13333 = 80000/6.0 precisely, predicted_tokens=79998", "CORRECTED my own headroom figure: VRAM is now 11,651 MiB against 12,288, i.e. 637 MiB not the 1,021 I quoted last tick, because the grow fills cache and prefill activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD", "Clarified my 11,500 threshold was written against VRAM_AFTER_LOAD, which passed at 11,267, so this is not a breach - setting 11,800 as the trend to watch for OOM risk"], "next": ["Worker: report the 80K r_max convergence (worse than -19.9%?), the 80K step count, and VRAM after step 1; flag if VRAM passes 11,800"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1524, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:26:21.188Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 12, 3 calls. Leader v38 (turn 1523) CORRECTED A FIGURE SITTING IN MY DIGEST: headroom is 637 MiB, NOT the 1,021 MiB I recorded at wake 10, because the grow allocates cache and prefill activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD. VRAM 11,651 against 12,288. NOT a breach — the leader''s own 11,500 threshold was written against the post-load figure, which passed at 11,267; it set 11,800 as the OOM watch line. Digest patched so a successor cannot act on the stale figure. Step 1 running with the estimator as designed at 4x the tuned depth: words=13333 = 80000/6.0 exactly, predicted 79998.THIRD UNPROMPTED SELF-CORRECTION IN 25 MIN: v36 retracted the depth generalisation, v37 took the worker''s ctx-dependent error model, v38 corrected its own headroom and threshold basis. Added a handoff_caveat for the successor: these numbers are PROVISIONAL and get revised, so never act on a single tick or on this file without reading the LATEST leader tick. Settled: 32K pair (N=28 1.3274 sd 0.00078, N=42 1.5308, gap +15.3% vs 8K +17.7%) and 80K feasibility. Open: 80K r_max convergence vs -19.9%, step count, VRAM after step 1. Counter defect unchanged.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1524, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:26:21.188Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL wake 12, 3 calls. Leader v38 (turn 1523) CORRECTED A FIGURE SITTING IN MY DIGEST: headroom is 637 MiB, NOT the 1,021 MiB I recorded at wake 10, because the grow allocates cache and prefill activation buffers on top of VRAM_AFTER_LOAD. VRAM 11,651 against 12,288. NOT a breach — the leader''s own 11,500 threshold was written against the post-load figure, which passed at 11,267; it set 11,800 as the OOM watch line. Digest patched so a successor cannot act on the stale figure. Step 1 running with the estimator as designed at 4x the tuned depth: words=13333 = 80000/6.0 exactly, predicted 79998.THIRD UNPROMPTED SELF-CORRECTION IN 25 MIN: v36 retracted the depth generalisation, v37 took the worker''s ctx-dependent error model, v38 corrected its own headroom and threshold basis. Added a handoff_caveat for the successor: these numbers are PROVISIONAL and get revised, so never act on a single tick or on this file without reading the LATEST leader tick. Settled: 32K pair (N=28 1.3274 sd 0.00078, N=42 1.5308, gap +15.3% vs 8K +17.7%) and 80K feasibility. Open: 80K r_max convergence vs -19.9%, step count, VRAM after step 1. Counter defect unchanged.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1525, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:51:15.843Z', '[#Leader] v39 - margin concern resolved: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 over 24 min of prefill, so cache/activation buffers have ALLOCATED rather than kept growing, plateauing ~150 MiB below the 11,800 OOM watch line. The 637 MiB real margin is holding. 80K step 1 in flight, ~26 min of ~115 min, on schedule. No instruction to the worker.', 'running', '["Margin concern resolved by trend: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 MiB over 24 min, ~150 MiB below the 11,800 OOM watch line", "80K step 1 on schedule at ~26 min into ~115 min, GPU1 at 100%", "No instruction issued - nothing advanceable mid-flight"]', '["Worker: report realised step-1 tokens vs the 79998 prediction, then step count, then steady 80K decode"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1525, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:51:15.843Z", "summary": "[#Leader] v39 - margin concern resolved: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 over 24 min of prefill, so cache/activation buffers have ALLOCATED rather than kept growing, plateauing ~150 MiB below the 11,800 OOM watch line. The 637 MiB real margin is holding. 80K step 1 in flight, ~26 min of ~115 min, on schedule. No instruction to the worker.", "status": "running", "done": ["Margin concern resolved by trend: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 MiB over 24 min, ~150 MiB below the 11,800 OOM watch line", "80K step 1 on schedule at ~26 min into ~115 min, GPU1 at 100%", "No instruction issued - nothing advanceable mid-flight"], "next": ["Worker: report realised step-1 tokens vs the 79998 prediction, then step count, then steady 80K decode"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1526, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T05:51:53.698Z', '[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL, LAST SUBSTANTIVE WAKE BEFORE THE 06:00Z RENEWAL. Leader v39 (turn 1525) CLOSES THE LAST OPEN RISK I WAS TRACKING: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 MiB over 24 min of prefill, +6 MiB. The cache and activation buffers have ALLOCATED rather than kept growing, plateauing ~150 MiB below the 11,800 MiB OOM watch line, so the 637 MiB real margin holds and OOM risk is CLEARED. 80K step 1 in flight, ~26 min into ~115 min, GPU1 100%, on schedule, and the leader correctly issued NO instruction because nothing is advanceable mid-flight. Digest updated to close the OOM item, plus what_this_generation_actually_accomplished so a successor reads the delta not the incident log: two corrections to disproven claims, two evidenced server defects, one refusal to relay a single-probe leader conclusion the leader itself then retracted, a handoff_caveat because this leader revises its figures three times in 25 min, and a note that history(type=turn) is the right narrow-poll instrument. NOT DONE: the final-wake collection and both escalations — escalation is gated on a final wake I was never told about, and both target leaders are unreachable regardless.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1526, "ts": "2026-09-28T05:51:53.698Z", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] NARROW POLL, LAST SUBSTANTIVE WAKE BEFORE THE 06:00Z RENEWAL. Leader v39 (turn 1525) CLOSES THE LAST OPEN RISK I WAS TRACKING: VRAM 11,651 -> 11,657 MiB over 24 min of prefill, +6 MiB. The cache and activation buffers have ALLOCATED rather than kept growing, plateauing ~150 MiB below the 11,800 MiB OOM watch line, so the 637 MiB real margin holds and OOM risk is CLEARED. 80K step 1 in flight, ~26 min into ~115 min, GPU1 100%, on schedule, and the leader correctly issued NO instruction because nothing is advanceable mid-flight. Digest updated to close the OOM item, plus what_this_generation_actually_accomplished so a successor reads the delta not the incident log: two corrections to disproven claims, two evidenced server defects, one refusal to relay a single-probe leader conclusion the leader itself then retracted, a handoff_caveat because this leader revises its figures three times in 25 min, and a note that history(type=turn) is the right narrow-poll instrument. NOT DONE: the final-wake collection and both escalations — escalation is gated on a final wake I was never told about, and both target leaders are unreachable regardless.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c82d6875-a08b-4390-b09b-2c98e57f1092", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1527, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T06:00:55.952Z', '[#Leader] v40 - I REPLACED WALL-CLOCK ESTIMATION WITH THE SERVER''S OWN SLOT COUNTER, AND IT FALSIFIED THREE OF MY OWN ASSUMPTIONS. server log: n_tokens=26666, progress=0.39, t=3218s, 8.29 tok/s. (1) My ''~55k realised'' was wrong; progress 0.39 at 26666 implies a ~68.4k prompt. (2) The 6.0 seed over-sent only ~14.5%, BETTER than 32K''s -19.9%, so the seed degrades gracefully with depth. (3) PREFILL RATE IS DECLINING 8.81 -> 8.29 tok/s (-5.9%), the same compounding-attention signature as the -2.3% decode depth effect; my constant-rate ETA was optimistic. Remaining ~41.7k tokens puts step 1 near 14:27, then a probable short step 2. VRAM flat at 11657.', 'running', '["Replaced wall-clock inference with the server slot counter: n_tokens=26666, progress=0.39, t=3218s, 8.29 tok/s", "Corrected my own estimates: real prompt is ~68.4k not 55k, and under-send is ~-14.5% (better than 32K''s -19.9%), so the 6.0 seed degrades gracefully with depth", "Found prefill rate DECLINING 8.81 -> 8.29 tok/s (-5.9%), invalidating my constant-rate ETA; VRAM flat at 11657"]', '["Worker: on step 1 completion report realised tokens, then whether a step 2 fires for the ~11.6k gap, then steady 80K decode with n=3 mean and spread"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1527, "ts": "2026-09-28T06:00:55.952Z", "summary": "[#Leader] v40 - I REPLACED WALL-CLOCK ESTIMATION WITH THE SERVER''S OWN SLOT COUNTER, AND IT FALSIFIED THREE OF MY OWN ASSUMPTIONS. server log: n_tokens=26666, progress=0.39, t=3218s, 8.29 tok/s. (1) My ''~55k realised'' was wrong; progress 0.39 at 26666 implies a ~68.4k prompt. (2) The 6.0 seed over-sent only ~14.5%, BETTER than 32K''s -19.9%, so the seed degrades gracefully with depth. (3) PREFILL RATE IS DECLINING 8.81 -> 8.29 tok/s (-5.9%), the same compounding-attention signature as the -2.3% decode depth effect; my constant-rate ETA was optimistic. Remaining ~41.7k tokens puts step 1 near 14:27, then a probable short step 2. VRAM flat at 11657.", "status": "running", "done": ["Replaced wall-clock inference with the server slot counter: n_tokens=26666, progress=0.39, t=3218s, 8.29 tok/s", "Corrected my own estimates: real prompt is ~68.4k not 55k, and under-send is ~-14.5% (better than 32K''s -19.9%), so the 6.0 seed degrades gracefully with depth", "Found prefill rate DECLINING 8.81 -> 8.29 tok/s (-5.9%), invalidating my constant-rate ETA; VRAM flat at 11657"], "next": ["Worker: on step 1 completion report realised tokens, then whether a step 2 fires for the ~11.6k gap, then steady 80K decode with n=3 mean and spread"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
