70 vs :6969 locations)", "Leader repro: lead-uifix-current.png, full-screen confirmed on :6969", "C5 queued (task-288c0932d0) + dispatched to dev with host line pointers and gates", "Decision d-b5d3c9b76e recorded"], "next": ["Dev C5 → env merge → pipeline → restart → QC r17 (no header, X works, full-screen)", "Owner: URL confirmation + beta :6970 refresh go-ahead"], "blockers": [], "decisions": ["d-b5d3c9b76e: remove dialog header keep X; both owner symptoms = stale client"], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "64b0b20e-2a1e-4759-b87e-9c3ea56b67cb", "author_model": ""}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1559, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-28T12:50:27.042Z', '[#Leader] v62 - 32K PROBE PATH VERIFIED, 80K RELEASED. probecheck: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, all four probes, genuine gated PROBES_DONE, steady n=3 mean 1.6129 tok/s SD 0.0031 spread 0.19%. A LINEAGE BREAK MATTERS MORE: earlier 32K N=42 was 1.5308, this 1.6129, 5.4% apart and NOT noise. Cause is probe lineage - old re-derived sizing versus new exact replay. The +15.3% gap was 1.5308 vs 1.3274, BOTH old-lineage, so internally consistent, but mixing lineages is unquotable, so I dispatched 32K N=28 on the new lineage first.', 'running', '["CONFIRMED 32K probe path verified: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, all four probes, genuine PROBES_DONE, steady n=3 mean 1.6129 tok/s SD 0.0031 spread 0.19%", "Caught a lineage break: earlier 32K N=42 1.5308 versus this 1.6129 is 5.4% apart, NOT noise but a change of probe lineage", "Recorded the +15.3% 32K gap as old-lineage but unquotable once either arm moves, so I dispatched 32K N=28 on the new lineage first, then 80K N=42 as d80k-n42-C"]', '["Worker: re-run 32K N=28 under the replay lineage, then 80K N=42 as d80k-n42-C", "Worker: annotate result-d80k-n42-B.txt and put the no-exception-with-%d rule in the source", "Ask me before any matched 80K N=28 run"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1559, "ts": "2026-09-28T12:50:27.042Z", "summary": "[#Leader] v62 - 32K PROBE PATH VERIFIED, 80K RELEASED. probecheck: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, all four probes, genuine gated PROBES_DONE, steady n=3 mean 1.6129 tok/s SD 0.0031 spread 0.19%. A LINEAGE BREAK MATTERS MORE: earlier 32K N=42 was 1.5308, this 1.6129, 5.4% apart and NOT noise. Cause is probe lineage - old re-derived sizing versus new exact replay. The +15.3% gap was 1.5308 vs 1.3274, BOTH old-lineage, so internally consistent, but mixing lineages is unquotable, so I dispatched 32K N=28 on the new lineage first.", "status": "running", "done": ["CONFIRMED 32K probe path verified: FINAL_CUMULATIVE 32016 vs 32000 PASS, all four probes, genuine PROBES_DONE, steady n=3 mean 1.6129 tok/s SD 0.0031 spread 0.19%", "Caught a lineage break: earlier 32K N=42 1.5308 versus this 1.6129 is 5.4% apart, NOT noise but a change of probe lineage", "Recorded the +15.3% 32K gap as old-lineage but unquotable once either arm moves, so I dispatched 32K N=28 on the new lineage first, then 80K N=42 as d80k-n42-C"], "next": ["Worker: re-run 32K N=28 under the replay lineage, then 80K N=42 as d80k-n42-C", "Worker: annotate result-d80k-n42-B.txt and put the no-exception-with-%d rule in the source", "Ask me before any matched 80K N=28 run"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
