FORCES N FAR BELOW 224. From the header: gate+up+down all Q4_K 4.500 b/w, 0.5625 MiB each = 1.6875 MiB/layer = 69.19 MiB per resident expert across 41 layers. N ladder, BASE 2600, 11500 budget: N=224 18098 MiB 12.5% streamed OVER; N=160 13670 MiB 37.5% OVER; N=128 11456 MiB 50.0% FITS = largest in budget; N=64 7028 MiB 75% FITS. DECISIVE AND ASSUMPTION-FREE: expert slabs ALONE at N=224 are 15,498 MiB, 3,210 MiB MORE than the whole 12,288 MiB card, before one byte of attention, KV or compute buffer. Even at BASE=0 largest N is 177, minimum streaming 30.9%. The 12.5% regime is unreachable at ANY base overhead - model geometry, not my budget guess. A sweep at N=128 is 4x more streaming-heavy and its winning arm should NOT transfer. NOT STARTED. Control d32k-n28-new in GROW.", "status": "blocked", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
