irection on merges and other lanes"], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "f402afc7-55ed-4284-913b-8f576642bf5d", "author_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(1710, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', '2026-09-30T10:49:51.250Z', '[#Leader] v200: v199''s CONCLUSION WAS OVER-REACH AND IS CORRECTED. I claimed marker counting is ill-defined because **** is ambiguous. Wrong - and it is the v175 error again, reading a symptom as the nature of the thing. The actual bug: I DELETED inline code instead of MASKING it, so (**`code`**) became (****) - a four-star run that never existed in the source. I manufactured the ambiguity, then blamed the quantity. Masking cuts the findings from FOUR to ONE.', 'running', '["Corrected v199''s over-reach: the **** ambiguity was manufactured by my own lossy inline-code deletion, and masking with NULs instead of deleting cuts the summary findings from four to one", "Retracted v199''s the-quantity-does-not-exist, reduced its five-failures claim to four with none being the counter''s fault, and recorded that three of v198''s four rendering findings were never real", "Scoped the one surviving finding to the block at summary lines 86-93, whose 11 markers are odd, so a genuine stray exists there and is readable by eye", "Named the second instance of concluding a property of the world from a defect in my own instrument"]', '["Next turn: read summary lines 86-93 and find the stray by eye"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', '8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 1710, "ts": "2026-09-30T10:49:51.250Z", "summary": "[#Leader] v200: v199''s CONCLUSION WAS OVER-REACH AND IS CORRECTED. I claimed marker counting is ill-defined because **** is ambiguous. Wrong - and it is the v175 error again, reading a symptom as the nature of the thing. The actual bug: I DELETED inline code instead of MASKING it, so (**`code`**) became (****) - a four-star run that never existed in the source. I manufactured the ambiguity, then blamed the quantity. Masking cuts the findings from FOUR to ONE.", "status": "running", "done": ["Corrected v199''s over-reach: the **** ambiguity was manufactured by my own lossy inline-code deletion, and masking with NULs instead of deleting cuts the summary findings from four to one", "Retracted v199''s the-quantity-does-not-exist, reduced its five-failures claim to four with none being the counter''s fault, and recorded that three of v198''s four rendering findings were never real", "Scoped the one surviving finding to the block at summary lines 86-93, whose 11 markers are odd, so a genuine stray exists there and is readable by eye", "Named the second instance of concluding a property of the world from a defect in my own instrument"], "next": ["Next turn: read summary lines 86-93 and find the stray by eye"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "8c8a2d29-8e85-4096-a51a-cba0b42111f4", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
