ion.md rebuilt 2593 tok (33 tasks, 17 done, turns 154-160 arc + open owner confirmations list); OKF 23 clean; diff checked next.", "status": "idle", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": ["TEST collector boot blocked at step 1 — paseo tools never injected on TEST daemon (task-12f20731ef); PROD boots fine — plus orphan heartbeats 08c2b0ba/7e0a1707 and 13 idle collector sessions await creator/owner cleanup"], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": "a zombie generation can be revived by a leader directive carrying the unfixed-server workaround — no respawn needed", "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238", "author_model": "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(162, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-62504d3c56', '2026-10-01T01:27:26.816Z', 'Collector recovery VERIFIED (c211499d post-nudge wake): read track_status WITHOUT re-confirming per directive; wakes_remaining 27 (time-derived, correct for 23:00 gen at 01:25Z); NARROW POLL at 8/20 budget (vs 20/20 wake1); AGENT WATCH honest (first-seen labels, checked 3 of 15 rotation, ACT bands incl leader 648K, claim-mismatch 64b0b20e flagged unresolved, 3 unreachable leaders classified undeliverable-needs-human); correct NO-SEND reasoning (every ACT/unreachable agent is its own track leader — no higher leader to batch to); roster 8 tracks with server timestamps only (no hand-subtraction), system track skipped. Design behavior restored without respawn. Its intel worth surfacing: t-d1cf43b723 leader claude-6f8c467d NOT FOUND in paseo (contract signed 13:58Z same day), t-34d7bdf5d6 + t-abf10888f3 leaders closed providerUnavailable with 3 running tasks each, t-f3ba82ac9c claim-mismatch (idle vs 1 running). Lesson added (recovery via holder verification). Server fix still with B; prompt v6 live; 05:00Z renewal = first clean-gen test.', 'idle', '[]', '[]', '["TEST collector boot blocked at step 1 — paseo tools never injected on TEST daemon (task-12f20731ef); PROD boots fine — plus orphan heartbeats 08c2b0ba/7e0a1707 and 13 idle collector sessions await creator/owner cleanup"]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": "false-stale recovery verified: holder evidence from ledger + boot-only confirm + direct cadence read resurrects a zombie generation in place", "docs_updated": []}', '4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238', 'opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash', '{"n": 162, "ts": "2026-10-01T01:27:26.816Z", "summary": "Collector recovery VERIFIED (c211499d post-nudge wake): read track_status WITHOUT re-confirming per directive; wakes_remaining 27 (time-derived, correct for 23:00 gen at 01:25Z); NARROW POLL at 8/20 budget (vs 20/20 wake1); AGENT WATCH honest (first-seen labels, checked 3 of 15 rotation, ACT bands incl leader 648K, claim-mismatch 64b0b20e flagged unresolved, 3 unreachable leaders classified undeliverable-needs-human); correct NO-SEND reasoning (every ACT/unreachable agent is its own track leader — no higher leader to batch to); roster 8 tracks with server timestamps only (no hand-subtraction), system track skipped. Design behavior restored without respawn. Its intel worth surfacing: t-d1cf43b723 leader claude-6f8c467d NOT FOUND in paseo (contract signed 13:58Z same day), t-34d7bdf5d6 + t-abf10888f3 leaders closed providerUnavailable with 3 running tasks each, t-f3ba82ac9c claim-mismatch (idle vs 1 running). Lesson added (recovery via holder verification). Server fix still with B; prompt v6 live; 05:00Z renewal = first clean-gen test.", "status": "idle", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": ["TEST collector boot blocked at step 1 — paseo tools never injected on TEST daemon (task-12f20731ef); PROD boots fine — plus orphan heartbeats 08c2b0ba/7e0a1707 and 13 idle collector sessions await creator/owner cleanup"], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": "false-stale recovery verified: holder evidence from ledger + boot-only confirm + direct cadence read resurrects a zombie generation in place", "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238", "author_model": "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash"}');
INSERT INTO orch_turns(n, project_id, track_id, ts, summary, status, done, next, blockers, decisions, knowledge, author_agent, author_model, raw) VALUES(163, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-62504d3c56', '2026-10-01T01:28:13.836Z', 'PR #69 (CI green, not merged) fixes two live PROD defects. 1) FALSE-STALE KILLED A GENERATION: the guard was checkup_id in checkup_history, but the CURRENT holder''s own id is in that history by construction, so every re-confirm by a live generation matched itself, was told it was a late dead predecessor, and obeyed — 16 empty wakes, a 45-wake generation dead after wake 2 on t-1d514bb795. Outcomes are now ORDERED and the order is the fix: no id -> schedule only; id == current holder -> idempotent no-op (nothing stamped, current cadence, note says ''you are the generation this track is on''); in history AND != current -> stale; else new. stale_generation is an INSTRUCTION so the holder''s reply is asserted too. My shipped test missed it by asserting ok + unchanged timestamp and never the field the agent acts on. 2) THE TIER FIX NEVER RAN: paseo does not inject PASEO_AGENT_CWD into the MCP server subprocess (live process has MCP_ORCH_STATE_DIR + MCP_ORCH_TIER, no PASEO_AGENT_CWD), so the byCwd branch was SKIPPED and every session fell through to MCP_ORCH_TIER=leader. d-41''s precedence fix was correct and completely inert, and its test set the env var explicitly so it exercised a path production never takes. _agent_cwd() now resolves explicit -> PASEO_AGENT_CWD -> process cwd (/proc/<mcp-pid>/cwd IS the byCwd key). Verified in the exact live config: resolves orchestrator, 7 tools incl heartbeat; an unmapped leader dir still resolves leader. 3) is_unsafe_tier_key used find_repo_root whose fallback IS the cwd, so with no markers every key read unsafe and the whole map collapsed to leader; now a strict lookup failing OPEN. 4) schedule.ts passed the repo root as --cwd on BOTH create and update; both now use defaultCwd(). Suite 418/8 -> 430/8; plugin typecheck clean + 9/9; all PR checks pass.', 'idle', '["False-stale: holder re-confirm is an idempotent no-op (red-first tests, PROD-scale 16-wake repro)", "Predecessor-after-successor still stale; new id still stamps; repeat cadence byte-identical", "Tier: _agent_cwd falls back to process cwd; proved in the exact live MCP-server config", "is_unsafe_tier_key fails OPEN when the repo root is undetectable", "schedule.ts: both --cwd call sites off the repo-root walk", "d-43 appended to DECISIONS.md; d-41/d-42 untouched", "DESIGN refreshed (cwd chain, fail-open rule, confirm outcome table)", "430 passed / 8 skipped; plugin typecheck + 9/9; all PR #69 checks green"]', '["Merge + deploy + collector re-seed: the running backend started 2026-09-28 and its installed venv copy predates session_tier_tools entirely, so #69 cannot take effect on PROD until it is deployed", "QA review of #69"]', '[]', '[]', '{"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}', 'c01b9285-d1f9-4285-aa67-6b0e5e9fb2d9', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 163, "ts": "2026-10-01T01:28:13.836Z", "summary": "PR #69 (CI green, not merged) fixes two live PROD defects. 1) FALSE-STALE KILLED A GENERATION: the guard was checkup_id in checkup_history, but the CURRENT holder''s own id is in that history by construction, so every re-confirm by a live generation matched itself, was told it was a late dead predecessor, and obeyed — 16 empty wakes, a 45-wake generation dead after wake 2 on t-1d514bb795. Outcomes are now ORDERED and the order is the fix: no id -> schedule only; id == current holder -> idempotent no-op (nothing stamped, current cadence, note says ''you are the generation this track is on''); in history AND != current -> stale; else new. stale_generation is an INSTRUCTION so the holder''s reply is asserted too. My shipped test missed it by asserting ok + unchanged timestamp and never the field the agent acts on. 2) THE TIER FIX NEVER RAN: paseo does not inject PASEO_AGENT_CWD into the MCP server subprocess (live process has MCP_ORCH_STATE_DIR + MCP_ORCH_TIER, no PASEO_AGENT_CWD), so the byCwd branch was SKIPPED and every session fell through to MCP_ORCH_TIER=leader. d-41''s precedence fix was correct and completely inert, and its test set the env var explicitly so it exercised a path production never takes. _agent_cwd() now resolves explicit -> PASEO_AGENT_CWD -> process cwd (/proc/<mcp-pid>/cwd IS the byCwd key). Verified in the exact live config: resolves orchestrator, 7 tools incl heartbeat; an unmapped leader dir still resolves leader. 3) is_unsafe_tier_key used find_repo_root whose fallback IS the cwd, so with no markers every key read unsafe and the whole map collapsed to leader; now a strict lookup failing OPEN. 4) schedule.ts passed the repo root as --cwd on BOTH create and update; both now use defaultCwd(). Suite 418/8 -> 430/8; plugin typecheck clean + 9/9; all PR checks pass.", "status": "idle", "done": ["False-stale: holder re-confirm is an idempotent no-op (red-first tests, PROD-scale 16-wake repro)", "Predecessor-after-successor still stale; new id still stamps; repeat cadence byte-identical", "Tier: _agent_cwd falls back to process cwd; proved in the exact live MCP-server config", "is_unsafe_tier_key fails OPEN when the repo root is undetectable", "schedule.ts: both --cwd call sites off the repo-root walk", "d-43 appended to DECISIONS.md; d-41/d-42 untouched", "DESIGN refreshed (cwd chain, fail-open rule, confirm outcome table)", "430 passed / 8 skipped; plugin typecheck + 9/9; all PR #69 checks green"], "next": ["Merge + deploy + collector re-seed: the running backend started 2026-09-28 and its installed venv copy predates session_tier_tools entirely, so #69 cannot take effect on PROD until it is deployed", "QA review of #69"], "blockers": [], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": null, "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "c01b9285-d1f9-4285-aa67-6b0e5e9fb2d9", "author_model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free"}');
