run-a-feature-acceptance-needs-the-pair-of-readings-not-just-the-visible-one", "docs_updated": []}', '4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238', 'opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash', '{"n": 236, "ts": "2026-10-02T02:17:59.522Z", "summary": "RUN #39 FIRST-RUN SMOKE-TEST ACCEPTANCE RECORDED (per orchestrator gap report): TWO readings, both required - (A) conversation title of runs[-1].agentId == ''#39 - 261002-12'' (dispatch-time naming), (B) runs[-1].workspaceId == wks_25051df4be8f4945 AND runs[-1].workspaceOrigin == ''reused'' (enum confirmed service.ts:197-198 - ''reused'' vs ''provisioned''; run #38 = provisioned/fresh). Title-right-workspace-wrong and workspace-right-title-wrong are both silent failures; only the pair distinguishes them. Status must also be succeeded (boot completed) - naming lands at dispatch and can succeed while boot fails. PRE-FLIGHT EXECUTED: collector dir write-test OK but ONLY after reclaiming inodes - WorkDisk was IFree 0, now 75 free (removed 74 contentless empty dirs: .tmp/.vite-temp/.wrangler/tmp tool temps + uninitialized external/ submodule stubs; ambiguous fixtures left alone); PROD paseo-home write-test OK (root fs, 6.2G) - agent session store is off WorkDisk. Reuse resolver static-verified: target.config.workspaceId set -> resolved.origin ''reused''; missing/archived pin -> degrades to ''provisioned'' (reading B catches exactly this); pinned wks_25051df4be8f4945 present, archivedAt null, pinnedAt 2026-10-01T16:50. Residual: 75 inodes = thin margin, systemic inode exhaustion remains owner-level.", "status": "running", "done": [], "next": [], "blockers": ["Run #39 (PROD 05:00Z) two-reading verification: title ''#39 - 261002-12'' + workspaceId wks_25051df4be8f4945 + workspaceOrigin ''reused'' + status succeeded - first live execution of reuse+naming", "WorkDisk inode exhaustion - reclaimed to 75 free for the run; systemic fix (node_modules-scale) owner-level, disclosed", "TEST schedule 290b46e2 paused (by design) - no live TEST naming verification path"], "decisions": [], "knowledge": {"lesson_topic": "first-run-a-feature-acceptance-needs-the-pair-of-readings-not-just-the-visible-one", "docs_updated": []}, "author_agent": "4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238", "author_model": "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash"}');
