INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3203, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T06:20:24.357Z', '{"agent_id": "556e5438-ddf9-403b-b71f-21eee8e2b5d6", "role": "dev", "model": "", "task": "P0 diagnose streaming bug", "summary": "P0 streaming diagnosis. REPRO: TEST web blocked (no TEST password in env; Playwright MCP absent) so reproduced on local dev web UI per brief fallback: agent-stream-ui ''auto-scroll sticks to bottom across token bursts'' PASSED (52.7s, mock one-minute-stream) - assistant-text pipeline works. EVIDENCE: stable :6969 (v0.9.2-hub-720c24ff45) and BETA :6970 (c3f2eda6b4) bundles are functionally IDENTICAL (13 bytes differ = version string only); TEST daemon.log shows NO turns since 09:40 +07 restart (3 agents idle, 0 agent_stream frames) but opencode-provider turn_failed with HTTP 426 ''OpenCode 1.18.0 or newer is required to use the free tier'' on Sep 24 + Sep 26 18:03 UTC (agents a3045df9, 6c7c42d6; 9 turn_failed in rotated logs) plus OpenCode event-stream ConnectionRefused during restarts. ROOT CAUSE (primary): opencode-provider turns die pre-stream at the Zen API version gate while deploy manifests pin @opencode-ai/sdk 1.14.46 (deploy/paseo-test/package.json:33) and 720c24ff4 dropped the 1.18.23 pin to fix frozen-lockfile builds - so all content types (assistant text/thinking/tool output) never stream for Zen free-tier opencode agents. EXONERATED: tool-call-sheet updateToolCall (407060e6f) early-returns on web (message.tsx:3212 shouldRenderInline=true) and app stream code is byte-identical worktree==deployed (git diff 720c24ff45 empty for agent-stream/timeline/hooks/message). SECONDARY: fetch_agent_timeline_request warns at 4.5s/3.9s on TEST (16 fetches today, 3 agent creates, 0 sends) - timeline fetch slowness may read as ''streaming broken''. Also 720c24ff4 deleted the reader.cancel regression test - guard is gone. FIX PLAN: (1) re-pin @opencode-ai/sdk >=1.18.0 WITH lockfile update (or confirm daemon uses local opencode binary 1.18.31 for Zen and SDK version is irrelevant - verify which path sends the version header); (2) restore SDK-guard test in dependency-closure style; (3) owner/leader runs one live opencode turn on TEST to verify; (4) investigate 4.5s timeline fetch separately. No fix written, nothing merged/deployed, PROD untouched, no config edited. Scratch: none outside /tmp (Playwright logs under mcphome). BLOCKED on: live-turn verification (needs TEST password + owner approval to spend quota/run turns on TEST).", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": [], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T06:20:24.357Z"}');
