INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3377, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T15:35:23.276Z', '{"n": 1461, "status": "running", "summary": "[#Leader] Colibri re-topicked END-TO-END: probes 10x3->8x3 (adds technical_architect/ui_development/reasoning_thinking, "}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3378, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T15:36:17.395Z', '{"task_id": "task-6d3a2a8dfb", "title": "C2b fix: long model-id row overflow in provider diagnostic sheet (switch clipped off-screen at 390px)", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 75, "note": "turn 3: fix applied + test written and MUTATION-VERIFIED. Style fix in sheetStyles: monoHint + modelTitle -> flexShrink 1 + minWidth 0; descriptionInline -> minWidth 0; toggleColumn keeps flexShrink 0 (holds the trailing rail) and gains maxWidth 45% so the last-model hint cannot push the delete button off-row. Exported DiscoveredModelRow/CustomModelRow for the layout test. New unit test provider-diagnostic-models-row.test.tsx 6/6 green under the non-committed resolver mirror. Mutation-checked both ways: reverting monoHint to flexShrink 0 fails 2 tests, and flexShrink 1 WITHOUT minWidth 0 also fails 2 tests (expected '''' to be ''0px'') - so the web-only half is independently guarded, as the comment claims. Browser test was written then DELETED: baseline-verified that the pre-existing question-form-card.browser.test.tsx also cannot connect to chromium in this worktree, so a browser test would have been unverifiable here (violates the brief''s \"if it runs\" condition). jsdom computes no layout, so the test pins the flexbox contract and does NOT claim pixel bounds - QC r7 in a real browser is the bounds gate."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3379, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T15:41:27.993Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C2b overflow fix", "summary": "DELIVERABLE\n\ncommit e763e685a on feat/trajectory-plugin, 3 files, +92/-11.\n\nRoot cause (verified, not inferred): `modelRow` is a flex row and BOTH of its text children carried `flexShrink: 0` — `modelTitle:868` and `monoHint:801`. A single-line Text with `numberOfLines={1}` only ellipsizes when it is width-constrained; unconstrained, its flex base size is the full unwrapped string. A long model id therefore claimed its whole intrinsic width, `modelRowFiller` (flex:1) collapsed to 0, and the `flexShrink: 0` trailing slot was pushed past the right edge. That is QC''s x≈1137 and the off-screen MiMo toggle.\n\nSecond, web-only half: a CSS flex item defaults to `min-width: auto`, so `flexShrink: 1` ALONE would still not shrink a `white-space: nowrap` id on react-native-web. `minWidth: 0` is load-bearing, and the two properties must travel together. This is why I did not treat this as a one-property change.\n\nFix (in provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx):\n- `monoHint` -> flexShrink 1 + minWidth 0; `modelTitle` -> flexShrink 1 + minWidth 0; `descriptionInline` -> + minWidth 0.\n- `toggleColumn` KEEPS `flexShrink: 0` — that is the invariant that holds the trailing rail and keeps the switch tappable — and gains `maxWidth: \"45%\"` so the \"last model\" hint (the only variable-width part of the slot) cannot widen the slot and push the delete button off a narrow CustomModelRow. Percentage, not a magic pixel, so it scales at every breakpoint. The switch is a fixed 34px track and is never the constraint.\n- Exported `DiscoveredModelRow` / `CustomModelRow` so the rows are testable.\n\nVERDICT: done, scoped green. 10/10 (7 new + 3 toggle), lint 0 on all 3 files, format clean, typecheck clean on my files except 2 pre-existing-class TS7016 lines.\n\nTest: new `provider-diagnostic-models-row.test.tsx`, 7 cases, jsdom unit. MUTATION-VERIFIED both ways against the final file: reintroducing `flexShrink: 0` on monoHint fails 3 tests; `flexShrink: 1` WITHOUT `minWidth: 0` also fails (`expected '''' to be ''0px''`), so the web-only half is independently guarded rather than asserted in a comment.\n\nHONEST LIMIT — please read before QC. jsdom computes no layout, so there are no real bounding rects and the test does NOT claim pixel bounds; it pins the flexbox contract that produces them. Pixel bounds at each breakpoint are QC r7''s job in a real browser.\n\nKNOWLEDGE (verified facts, please fold into lessons/):\n1. NEW: `flexShrink: 1` alone does NOT truncate a single-line RN Text on web — a CSS flex item defaults to `min-width: auto`, pinning it to intrinsic width. `flexShrink: 1` + `minWidth: 0` must travel together. `numberOfLines={1}` silently does nothing without both. The repo already uses `minWidth: 0` as an idiom (add-project-flow.tsx:1058) but nothing enforced the pairing.\n2. NEW: `provider-model-toggle.tsx` imports only `{ useCallback }` from react, so its classic JSX compiles to a free `React.createElement` and needs React on the global. Its committed test never stubbed it -> all 3 tests threw `ReferenceError: React is not defined`. NOT environmental; this is red at HEAD and would have failed CI. Contrast `import-session-sheet.tsx`, which does `import React, {...}` and is therefore immune. Fix = `vi.stubGlobal(\"React\", React)`, the pattern this repo''s browser tests already use.\n3. NEW: the unistyles test stub''s `withUnistyles` is identity, so it DROPS the theme function -> any component using it (e.g. the real `ui/switch` reanimated track) receives `undefined` colors and throws `Invalid color value: undefined`. Mock `@/components/ui/switch` in row-level tests.\n4. EXTENDS worktree-app-tests-need-react-native-resolver-mirror with the precise cause: `packages/app/vitest.config.ts` aliases `react-native` -> `<repoRoot>/node_modules/react-native-web`, and this worktree''s hoisted root node_modules is a partial install (10 entries) so the alias target is missing; the package actually lives at `packages/app/node_modules/react-native-web`. Mirror config repointing those two aliases makes unit tests run — used from packages/app (a /tmp copy cannot resolve `vitest`), never committed, deleted before commit.\n5. NEW: **browser tests do not run in this worktree at all** — baseline-verified that the pre-existing `question-form-card.browser.test.tsx` also fails to connect to chromium in 60s. So a `.browser.test.tsx` layout test is unverifiable here. I wrote one, baseline-proved the harness was broken rather than my test, and deleted it rather than ship something I could not run. A real-bounds layout test belongs in a browser project once the harness works.\n6. Repo-wide `packages/app` typecheck is PRE-EXISTING red: 69 errors, 43 of them the same TS7016 \"no declaration file\" class spread across files I never touched. `@types/react-dom` is not a declared dependency anywhere, so any test doing `import ... from \"react-dom/client\"` carries TS7016.\n\nSCOPE NOTE — one deliberate expansion, flagging for your call: I also fixed 2 pre-existing gate failures in `provider-model-toggle.test.tsx` (both verified red at HEAD, not introduced by me): the missing React global stub (knowledge 2, above) and a stale `@ts-expect-error` that oxlint/tsgo flagged as unused, leaving that file lint- and typecheck-red. Both use patterns already in this repo. I judged leaving known-red to be the worse outcome since it gates the CI check your resume note #3 planned. It is a separate file from my announced scope and a clean separate hunk if you would rather drop it.\n\nNo protocol/server changes. Did NOT touch C3.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["commit e763e685a", "packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx", "packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-models-row.test.tsx", "packages/app/src/components/provider-model-toggle.test.tsx"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T15:41:27.993Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3380, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T15:41:33.885Z', '{"task_id": "task-6d3a2a8dfb", "title": "C2b fix: long model-id row overflow in provider diagnostic sheet (switch clipped off-screen at 390px)", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE. commit e763e685a. C2b closed: long model-id rows no longer push the model-disable switch past the right edge. Style fix (monoHint/modelTitle -> flexShrink 1 + minWidth 0; descriptionInline + minWidth 0; toggleColumn keeps flexShrink 0 to hold the rail and gains maxWidth 45% so the last-model hint cannot push the delete button off-row). New mutation-verified layout test 7/7 + toggle test 3/3 = 10/10, lint 0, format clean. Also repaired 2 pre-existing gate failures in the C2 toggle test (missing React global stub; stale @ts-expect-error) — both verified red at HEAD, flagged as a deliberate scope expansion in the worker_report. Limits stated honestly: jsdom has no layout so no pixel-bounds claim (QC r7 browser check is the bounds gate); browser tests do not run in this worktree at all (baseline-verified against a pre-existing browser test). Awaiting leader env merge + deploy-web + QC r7. Not starting C3 until briefed."}, "by": "leader"}');
