INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3389, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T15:56:37.747Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 40, "note": "turn 2: RESEARCH COMPLETE, design note at turn end. No code written. (a) paseo-fleet ctx-inject source FOUND — PR #44 is ddvnguyen/LLM-Agents-Orchestration (not paseo), branch feat/paseo-fleet-plugin: plugins/paseo-fleet/{client/fleet-ctx-chip.tsx,server/ctx-capture.ts,shared/rpc.ts,index.server.ts}. Mechanism is 2-stage because the API forces it: server.before(\"agent.create\") sees config (systemPrompt+mcpServers) but NO agentId; server.before(\"agent.session_open\") sees agentId but only env. So facts ride a pendingCreateFacts queue (TTL 60s) and correlate at session_open, then ctx.session_open ledger row + timeline.append({id:\"fleet-ctx\"}) = one chip per agent (replace-on-same-id). Privacy contract already owner-decided in issue #46: full prompt NEVER stored/emitted/rendered, only length + sha256[:12] + <=200-char preview, truncated SERVER-side in ctx-capture.ts (node:crypto, client must not import), MCP names only never values, payload clamped <60KB. (b) Plugin-first path needs ZERO core edits: addTimelineRenderer + daemon timeline.append are both documented in this repo''s public-docs/plugins/reference.md (timeline items L894-990, L957 append, L565 hook table, L1460 composer pills). DECISIVE FINDING: reference.md L601-608 ordering shows \"derive launch configuration with Paseo runtime tools and daemon prompt\" happens BETWEEN agent.create and agent.session_open, and session_open exposes ONLY env. So NO plugin hook can observe the EFFECTIVE prompt the model actually receives — only the configured systemPrompt + counts. The tooltip must be honest about that ceiling. Second finding: fleet chip uses flexShrink:1 WITHOUT minWidth:0 (fleet-ctx-chip.tsx styles.text) — the exact web overflow bug I fixed in C2b; must apply the lesson if we reuse it. Third: fleet chip hardcodes English strings, against this repo''s i18n convention. Three viable render surfaces (A timeline chip / B composer pill popover / C trajectory-ledger extension) => per brief, STOPPING to present options rather than picking silently."}, "by": "leader"}');
