INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3391, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T15:58:21.242Z', '{"n": 56, "status": "running", "summary": "C3 design approved with leader calls on surface/privacy/localization; implementation started."}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3392, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T15:58:34.258Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C3 design note — chat view context-inject info", "summary": "BLOCKED ON DECISION — design note delivered, no code written, per the C3 brief''s \"if >2 viable approaches, STOP and present options, don''t pick silently\". I posted the three render-surface options to the operator; the prompts came back Unanswered, so I am escalating here rather than guessing on a privacy-relevant decision.\n\nDELIVERABLE (research + design note, 0 lines of code)\n\nBoth data sources researched and they turned out to be the SAME seam, plugin-only:\n\n(a) paseo-fleet ctx-inject SOURCE FOUND. PR #44 is NOT in the paseo repo — it is ddvnguyen/LLM-Agents-Orchestration, branch feat/paseo-fleet-plugin, files plugins/paseo-fleet/{client/fleet-ctx-chip.tsx, server/ctx-capture.ts, shared/rpc.ts, index.server.ts}. (I could not read it from a local checkout: /path/to/home/agents-orchestration has no fleet branch, so I read it via the GitHub API at the PR head ref.)\n\n(b) The plugin-first path needs ZERO core app edits: addTimelineRenderer + daemon timeline.append are both already documented in THIS repo at public-docs/plugins/reference.md:894-990 (timeline items), :957 (append a row from the daemon), :565 (before-hook table), :1460 (composer pills). So (a) is an implementation OF (b), not a competitor. Plugin-first is fully achievable — the only reason a core edit would ever be needed is option D (a header button), which I recommend rejecting.\n\nCapture is necessarily 2-stage because the API forces it: server.before(\"agent.create\") sees config (systemPrompt + mcpServers) but has NO agentId; server.before(\"agent.session_open\") has agentId but exposes ONLY env. Hence facts ride a pendingCreateFacts queue (60s TTL) and correlate at session open, emitting one ctx.session_open ledger row plus timeline.append({id:\"fleet-ctx\"}) = exactly one chip per agent (replace-on-same-id).\n\nPrivacy contract is ALREADY owner-decided (issue #46, \"truncated preview\"): the full prompt is never stored, emitted, or rendered — only length + sha256[:12] + a <=200-char preview, truncated SERVER-side in ctx-capture.ts (node:crypto; the client must not import it), MCP server NAMES only and never their values (commands/URLs may carry secrets), payload clamped under 60KB with the MCP list capped at 64. I am not re-litigating that decision, only surfacing how it changes per surface (see Q2).\n\nDECISIVE FINDING — this bounds what C3 can ever claim. reference.md:601-608 documents the ordering: agent.create hooks -> resolve defaults/validate -> \"derive launch configuration with Paseo runtime tools and daemon prompt\" -> agent.session_open hooks (env only). Paseo injects its own daemon prompt and runtime tools in that middle step, and NO plugin hook can observe the result. So the tooltip can show the CONFIGURED system prompt + MCP names + tool/model/mode, and can never show the effective context the model actually received. The owner''s phrase \"the stuff that silently rides along with each turn\" is precisely the unobservable part. Whatever we ship must state this rather than imply completeness — otherwise it is a misleading tooltip.\n\nTHREE VIABLE RENDER SURFACES (the decision I need):\n- A — timeline chip (fleet parity). addTimelineRenderer + timeline.append at session open; one row per agent in the transcript, tap to expand. Best match to the owner''s \"chat view\" wording and to the ctx chip T2 deliberately excluded. Cost: it puts ctx data into persisted + relayed chat history.\n- B — composer pill -> popover. addComposerPill in the composer track, fed by useRpc on open. No transcript pollution and the better privacy story, but it is a persistent control (possible noise) and not literally the chat view.\n- C — extend the existing trajectory ledger. Add ctx.session_open to the already-merged, already-QC''d Trajectory plugin. Cheapest, reuses a proven recorder/store/panel, zero new surface — but the info lives in the Trajectory panel, furthest from the chat view the owner named.\n- D — core app edit (chat header button). REJECTED: needs a shared-file announcement and A/B/C all cover it plugin-first.\n\nMy recommendation is A with the C2b layout fix applied, since it matches the stated intent and the excluded-from-T2 surface. B is the better privacy story. C is the best effort/value ratio. I did not pick, per the brief.\n\nTHREE SUB-DECISIONS the leader/owner should settle (I asked the operator; unanswered):\n1. Surface: A / B / C.\n2. Preview blast radius. Under A the <=200-char preview becomes PERSISTED and RELAYED history, a wider blast radius than fleet''s in-memory chip. Note this lane''s own established convention is STRICTER — the trajectory plugin stores textLength only and derives any preview client-side (plugins/trajectory/shared/fold.ts:40). Options: (i) keep fleet''s 200-char preview as-is, (ii) store length+hash+MCP names durably and fetch the preview only on expand, clamped harder, (iii) length+hash only, matching the trajectory convention.\n3. Localization. Fleet hardcodes English (\"Context injected\", \"yes\"/\"no\"); this repo uses i18n, and plugins/ is not a workspace member so a plugin cannot reach the app''s i18n bundle. Options: English-only plugin strings, or a plugin-local locale map.\n\nWHAT CAN GO WRONG (per the brief''s list)\n- Freshness/completeness: resume/import/refresh opens correlate no facts, so every field is null. Must render \"—\" for unknown and never fabricate. Data is captured at session open, so a mid-session prompt change reads stale. The in-memory chip map does not survive a daemon restart; the ledger row does.\n- Privacy: see sub-decision 2, plus the preview may still contain a path, project name, or a fragment of a credential. Server-side truncation is the enforcement point and the client must never see the full string.\n- Compact/mobile layout: fleet''s chip uses flexShrink: 1 WITHOUT minWidth: 0 (fleet-ctx-chip.tsx styles.text) — that is EXACTLY the web overflow bug I fixed in C2b (a CSS flex item defaults to min-width: auto, so flexShrink alone never truncates a nowrap id/label). Reusing fleet''s chip verbatim reintroduces the C2b defect at 390px. Any port must carry the C2b lesson.\n- The fleet''s inline chip hard-truncates with a manual clip() and plain style objects; this repo''s docs/design.md and docs/unistyles.md expect theme tokens and design primitives, so a straight copy is not style-compliant.\n\nESTIMATED FILE LIST (option A; B and C are the same shape)\nplugins/<ctx-plugin>/shared/ctx-schema.ts, server/ctx-capture.ts, index.server.ts, client/ctx-chip.tsx, index.client.tsx, plus tests (server: truncation/privacy clamps; client: chip row rendering incl. compact). ZERO packages/app files under A, B, or C.\n\nREQUEST: pick A/B/C and answer sub-decisions 2 and 3 (or delegate 2 to the owner as a privacy call). On your go I implement in file-sized steps with targeted vitest, scoped lint/format, and a worker_report, then QC r8 covers desktop + 390px. No code has been written for C3 and no shared file has been touched.", "status": "blocked", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["design-note (this report; no code written)", "PR #44 = ddvnguyen/LLM-Agents-Orchestration feat/paseo-fleet-plugin", "public-docs/plugins/reference.md:894-990,957,565,601-608,1460"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T15:58:34.258Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3393, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T15:58:40.678Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "blocked", "progress": 40, "note": "BLOCKED ON LEADER DECISION — design note delivered, 0 lines of code written (per brief: >2 viable approaches => STOP, don''t pick silently). Operator prompts returned Unanswered, so escalated via worker_report. Need: (1) surface A timeline-chip / B composer-pill popover / C trajectory-ledger extension — I recommend A (matches owner ''chat view'' wording + the chip T2 excluded), B has the better privacy story, C the best effort/value; (2) preview blast radius — fleet''s <=200-char preview becomes persisted+relayed history under A, while THIS lane''s own convention (trajectory) is stricter: textLength only, preview derived client-side (shared/fold.ts:40); (3) localization — fleet hardcodes English, plugins/ is not a workspace member so it cannot reach the app i18n bundle. Research facts locked in: PR #44 = ddvnguyen/LLM-Agents-Orchestration feat/paseo-fleet-plugin (not paseo; no local checkout of that branch, read via GitHub API at PR head). Both data sources are the SAME seam and are plugin-only — ZERO packages/app files needed under A/B/C. Capture is necessarily 2-stage: before(\"agent.create\") has config but no agentId, before(\"agent.session_open\") has agentId but only env => pendingFacts queue + correlate at session open. HARD CEILING discovered: reference.md:601-608 shows Paseo derives the launch config (daemon prompt + runtime tools) BETWEEN those two hooks and session_open exposes only env, so NO plugin can observe the EFFECTIVE context the model receives — the shipped tooltip must say so rather than imply completeness. Also flagged: fleet''s chip uses flexShrink:1 without minWidth:0 = the exact C2b web-overflow bug, so any port must carry the C2b fix. Holding at 40% until the leader decides."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3394, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T15:59:15.597Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 50, "note": "turn 3: decisions received (d-893c722f28) — implementing. APPROVED: (1) SURFACE A timeline chip via addTimelineRenderer + daemon timeline.append, plugin-only, ZERO packages/app files, with the MANDATORY C2b flex fix (flexShrink:1 + minWidth:0) and NOT a verbatim port of fleet''s chip styles; (2) PREVIEW POLICY length + sha256[:12] + MCP names only, NO stored 200-char preview, ''—'' for unknown, and the fidelity ceiling (Paseo''s own daemon prompt is unobservable to plugins, reference.md:601-608) must be DISCLOSED in the UI copy not hidden; (3) plugin-local i18n with a small locale map, English content initially so later translation needs no core edit. No longer blocked. First step: mirror the in-repo trajectory plugin as the plugin-first template (it is the merged+QC''d precedent) and settle how plugin tests run, since plugins/ is not a workspace member."}, "by": "leader"}');
