INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3397, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T16:01:53.882Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 55, "note": "turn 4 (C3): plugin scaffold + shared contract + server capture DONE, 9/9 green. plugins/ctx-inject/{package.json,paseo-plugin.json,tsconfig.json,vitest.config.ts,shared/ctx-schema.ts,server/ctx-capture.ts,server/ctx-capture.test.ts}. Policy enforced by construction: NO preview field exists anywhere (owner decision d-893c722f28), server-only node:crypto hash (client must never import ctx-capture), MCP names only, every unknown is null (renders as an em dash) and never 0/false. Privacy is asserted as a test: JSON.stringify of the captured facts and of the built chip row must not contain the prompt''s secret marker. VERIFIED the plugin test harness runs in this worktree with NO resolver mirror (RN aliases to packages/app/node_modules/react-native, which exists) — the C2b lesson does not apply to plugin tests. TWO DEPLOY FINDINGS THE LEADER NEEDS, flagged early because they gate QC r8: (1) .github/workflows/paseo-manual-pipeline.yml only ships plugins/freebuff (cp -r plugins/freebuff, line 757) — ''trajectory'' appears 0 times in the pipeline, so ctx-inject will NOT be deployed by the pipeline either; it needs the same manual copy to the TEST paseo home that trajectory got. (2) Per the standing knowledge note, web-only deploys do NOT refresh cached plugin client code, so a plugin reload is required before QC or it will false-fail. Also: no repo-level script runs plugin tests (plugins/ is not a workspace member); running with the pinned binary packages/plugin/node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs (4.1.10) since bare npx grabs 5.0.2 and mismatches the config''s defineConfig."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3398, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T16:06:55.749Z', '{"n": 1462, "status": "running", "summary": "[#Leader] Architect checkup = DRIFT verdict: T7 RETIRED (curve bends: 8to7 +2.24%, 7to6 +0.93% - adopt ncmoe6 config ins"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3399, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T16:14:31.225Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C3 context-inject chip", "summary": "DELIVERABLE\n\ncommit ba24ad537 on feat/trajectory-plugin. New plugin plugins/ctx-inject, 13 files, all additive: ZERO packages/app files touched, no protocol change, no shared-file announcement needed (nothing existing was modified). Surface A as approved: addTimelineRenderer + daemon timeline.append.\n\nVERDICT: done, scoped green. 21/21 (9 server capture + 12 chip component), plugin typecheck CLEAN, lint 0, format clean.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION NOTES\n\n1. I did NOT copy the fleet''s correlation, because it has an ordering bug. The fleet binds create-hook facts at `agent.created` (\"ordinary creation finishes\") and reads them at `agent.session_open` — but per public-docs/plugins/reference.md:601-608 the ordering is agent.create -> derive launch config -> agent.session_open -> open session. So agent.created fires AFTER agent.session_open, meaning a fresh create finds nothing bound and the chip is permanently all-unknown for the most common case. Mine correlates at session_open through a short-lived pending queue keyed by provider+cwd — the identity fields BOTH hooks expose — so the first open binds correctly and concurrent creations of different providers cannot steal each other''s config. A `refresh` reuses the last observed facts (same session, config unchanged); `resume`/`import` stay honestly unknown.\n\n2. Privacy policy is enforced by construction, not by convention. There is NO preview field anywhere in the schema or in the capture helpers, so a stored preview cannot be reintroduced by accident. The reduction lives in a server-only node:crypto module (ctx-capture.ts) that client code must not import; the client only ever reads the already-reduced fields off the row. MCP names only, never their config. Tests assert the reduction holds for the ENTIRE serialized object (JSON.stringify must not contain the secret marker), not just the field under test, and that MCP commands/URLs never leak.\n\n3. Fidelity ceiling is disclosed in the UI, always. The caveat sentence renders on the row itself, NOT behind the expand toggle — a caveat the user has to go looking for is not a disclosure, and the owner said \"not hidden\". Unknown is always an em dash and never \"no system prompt\", because a resumed session never runs the create hook: its facts are unknown, not absent. There is a dedicated test for that distinction.\n\n4. C2b fix carried and MUTATION-VERIFIED both ways on the chip''s summary style: removing minWidth:0 fails the layout test, and reverting flexShrink to 0 fails it too. The pair is commented in the component explaining that on web a CSS flex item defaults to min-width:auto and stays pinned to its intrinsic width even with shrink enabled — so a future reader does not \"simplify\" it away. I also used flexShrink:0 on the badge so the label does not compete with the summary.\n\n5. i18n is plugin-local as approved: client/i18n.ts, English content, `{{placeholder}}` interpolation matching the app''s i18next convention, plus count-aware _one/_other selection. A later locale is a data addition.\n\nDEFECTS I INTRODUCED AND CAUGHT (both found by my own tests, not by review)\n- The interpolation regex matched `{count}` while the templates used i18next''s `{{count}}`, so every substituted value rendered as literal `{1234}`. Caught by 3 failing tests; fixed the regex to `\\{\\{(\\w+)\\}\\}`.\n- A multi-line `React.PropsWithChildren<{` in the test mock fails to transform in .tsx (the `<` before a line break parses as a JSX assertion). Fixed by keeping type args on one line, as the existing trajectory tests do.\n\nGATES / HOW TO REPRODUCE\n- Tests: `cd plugins/ctx-inject && node ../../packages/plugin/node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run` (21/21). Use that pinned 4.1.10 binary: bare `npx vitest` resolves 5.0.2 and mismatches the config''s defineConfig (it happened to pass, but do not rely on it).\n- Typecheck: same dir, `node ../../packages/plugin/node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` — clean.\n- Plugin tests need NO resolver mirror in this worktree: the plugin-local vitest config aliases react-native to packages/app/node_modules, which exists. The C2b resolver lesson does not apply to plugin tests.\n- types/react-dom-client.d.ts is a deliberate, clearly-commented local shim: the repo declares no @types/react-dom and react-dom ships none, so this module has no declarations anywhere (the app''s own tests carry the same TS7016). It is typed as DELETE-ONCE @types/react-dom lands, because a hand-written stand-in would otherwise become a second conflicting source of truth.\n\nDEPLOY BLOCKERS FOR QC r8 — PLEASE READ BEFORE MERGING\n1. The deploy pipeline will NOT ship this plugin. .github/workflows/paseo-manual-pipeline.yml:757 copies only `plugins/freebuff`; the string \"trajectory\" appears 0 times in that workflow. So ctx-inject needs the same manual copy into the TEST paseo home that trajectory got, otherwise QC r8 will not see a chip and could report it as a false failure.\n2. Per the standing knowledge note, web-only deploys do NOT refresh cached plugin client code — a plugin reload is required before QC or the old client renderer will be used.\n3. No repo-level script runs plugin tests (plugins/ is not a workspace member). That is the outstanding T0 item about folding plugin tests into the repo test setup; I did not expand scope to fix it, but it is why the gates above are run from the plugin directory.\n\nKNOWN LIMITS (stated, not hidden)\n- On `resume`/`import` the chip renders all-unknown. That is honest (we never observed that session''s config) but it means the chip is uninformative for resumed agents. A follow-up could cache last-observed facts per agent and label them stale; I deliberately did not, because it trades accuracy for a claim we cannot back.\n- paseoToolsInjected is read from daemon config only for `purpose === \"interactive\"`; a history/refetch open reports unknown rather than paying the config read on the hot path.\n- Pixel layout at 390px is unverified here: jsdom computes no layout, so the component test pins the flex contract and makes no bounds claim. QC r8 at 390px is the bounds gate, exactly as with C2b.\n\nNo deploys, no config.json, no protocol changes, no config.json. Did not touch C2b''s files.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["commit ba24ad537", "plugins/ctx-inject/index.server.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/index.client.tsx", "plugins/ctx-inject/shared/ctx-schema.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/ctx-capture.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/client/ctx-chip.tsx", "plugins/ctx-inject/client/i18n.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/types/react-dom-client.d.ts"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:31.224Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3400, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T16:14:37.844Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE — commit ba24ad537. C3 implemented as approved (d-893c722f28): surface A timeline chip via addTimelineRenderer + daemon timeline.append, plugin-only, 13 new files under plugins/ctx-inject, ZERO packages/app files touched, no protocol change, no shared-file announcement needed. 21/21 green (9 server capture + 12 chip component), plugin typecheck CLEAN (vs the trajectory plugin''s 127-error red baseline), lint 0, format clean. Key implementation calls: (1) did NOT copy the fleet''s correlation because it has an ordering bug — it binds facts at agent.created which fires AFTER agent.session_open per reference.md:601-608, so a fresh create would be permanently all-unknown; mine correlates at session_open via a pending queue keyed by provider+cwd, the identity fields both hooks expose, so the first open binds and concurrent creates of different providers cannot cross-contaminate. (2) Privacy enforced by construction: NO preview field exists anywhere, so it cannot be reintroduced by accident; reduction is server-only node:crypto; tests assert the WHOLE serialized row contains no prompt text and no MCP command/URL. (3) Fidelity ceiling disclosed in the UI always — the caveat renders on the row, not behind the expand toggle, and unknown is always an em dash, never \"no system prompt\" (a resume never runs the create hook, so unknown != absent). (4) C2b fix carried and mutation-verified BOTH ways on the chip summary (removing minWidth:0 fails; reverting flexShrink:0 fails), with the pair commented so it is not \"simplified\" away later. (5) plugin-local i18n per approval, {{placeholder}} convention. Two self-introduced defects caught by my own tests: the interpolation regex matched {count} against {{count}} templates (rendered literal {1234}), and a multi-line PropsWithChildren<{ in a .tsx test mock fails esbuild transform. DEPLOY BLOCKERS for QC r8: the pipeline copies ONLY plugins/freebuff (trajectory appears 0 times), so ctx-inject needs the same manual copy to the TEST paseo home; and a plugin reload is required since web-only deploys do not refresh cached plugin client code. Gates: run tests/typecheck from plugins/ctx-inject with the pinned packages/plugin vitest 4.1.10 binary (bare npx grabs 5.0.2); plugin tests need NO resolver mirror."}, "by": "leader"}');
