INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3404, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T16:36:56.949Z', '{"agent_id": "p0-qc-playwright", "role": "P0+Trajectory+C1+C2+C3 live-QC", "model": "", "task": "C3 ctx-inject chip QC round 8", "summary": "DELIVERABLE: R8 C3 ctx-inject QC — daemon 0.9.2-hub-ad1c9318f2 restarted 16:16Z, ctx-inject ready 16:16:46Z; bundle index-0117bda3 unchanged. Fresh agent 88503a07 created via New Agent tab + Space Bunny Free + p0-live-ok probe (turn failed upstream-side: zen 403 Model access is disabled x5 retries, disclosed noise). (1) CHIP APPEARS: FAIL — no Context configured row; capture failed 16:32:10.494Z Unknown agent timeline.append handler_error, ~400ms BEFORE session Created agent (.907Z): session_open hook fires pre-commit, plugin swallows, no retry. Same signature as known-noise stale id a788ea99, so that noise is the same race, not (only) a stale session. (2) EXPAND: NOT-EXERCISABLE (no row; testIDs absent). (3) PRIVACY: NOT-EXERCISABLE with vacuous negative — zero ctx-inject rows daemon-wide (agents grep exit 1, chat grep exit 1), so no prompt text persisted; method: state grep + DOM absence. (4) RESUME: NOT-EXERCISABLE — reopen fires no session_open (no daemon lines), no chip; no user path produces a row. (5) MOBILE: NOT-EXERCISABLE (blocked by 1; nothing to bound/tap). (6) REGRESSION PASS: trajectory dialog healthy no red, C2 Pi sheet 9 switches, console 0 errors; audit 535 lines 426=0 turn_failed=1(mine, disclosed) newer=0 PII 0. VERDICT: FAIL (1 fails, 2-5 not-exercisable, 6 passes). Fix direction (not applied): retry/backoff the timeline.append or defer to post-commit; create-hook facts already queued correctly. KNOWLEDGE: new-agent creation path = tab-bar workspace-new-tab-button testid + dropdown Agent item (real mouse click; synthetic/Enter/JS clicks fail) + model select + first send; sidebar + is not in row subtree; workspace home without tabs has no tab bar; Ctrl+K needs open agent for plugin commands; Space Bunny Free currently 403-disabled via zen (cloudflare server flag).", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["r8-ui-version.txt", "r8-chip-desktop.png", "r8-fresh-session.png", "r8-fresh-stopped.png", "r8-reopen.png", "r8-trajectory.png", "r8-c2-sheet.png", "r8-model-picker.png", "r8-composer.png", "r8-turn-window.log", "r8-samples.jsonl"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T16:36:56.948Z", "evaluation": {"confidence": 93, "effectiveness": 88, "guideline_adherence": 100, "task_complexity": 55, "task_size": 45, "notes": "FAIL verdict is evidence-backed: fresh-agent timestamps (.494 vs .907) prove pre-commit hook ordering; zero rows daemon-wide (grep exit 1 both stores); reopen fires no session_open. No state mutated beyond one failed probe turn on TEST (disclosed).", "telemetry": null}}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3405, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T16:37:43.082Z', '{"n": 58, "status": "running", "summary": "QC r8 FAIL (pre-commit append race) handed to dev with exact timestamps and two fix directions."}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3406, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T16:38:23.350Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 20, "note": "turn 5 (C3 fix for QC r8 FAIL): r8 localized the defect — session_open fires PRE-COMMIT, so timeline.append runs ~400ms before the agent is committed to agent-manager, the call fails with \"Unknown agent\", my catch swallowed it, and no row is ever written. Correlation is NOT the problem (QC confirmed the queue binds correctly); the append is simply too early. Note QC corrected my earlier attribution: the a788ea99 \"stale agent\" daemon.log noise is this same race, not a stale session. DIRECTION CHOSEN: B (defer the append to the post-commit agent.created signal), not A (bounded retry). Reasons: (1) it is event-driven with no polling and no timing budget, where A''s budget is a guess about how long commit takes; (2) the reason field makes the decision deterministic — reason===\"create\" is the ONLY pre-commit case, every other reason (resume/refresh/import) means the agent already exists and can append inline immediately, so A would waste retries in exactly the cases that already succeed; (3) agent.created is the documented \"ordinary creation finishes\" signal and the fleet already keys off event.agent.id. Will verify agent.created carries the agentId from reference.md:514 + the fleet''s usage before relying on it. Bounded-TTL the stash so a creation that never commits cannot leak, and log loudly rather than swallow. Will add a test pinning created-after-open ordering (append must NOT fire at session_open for a create) plus a loud-logging test so \"silent swallow\" cannot come back. Privacy-by-construction untouched."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3407, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T16:41:19.289Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C3 QC r8 fix — post-commit chip append", "summary": "DELIVERABLE\n\ncommit e4a8d189e (on top of ba24ad537). +2 files, 1 modified, all inside plugins/ctx-inject. No packages/app file, no protocol change.\n\nVERDICT: done, scoped green. 34/34 (13 new ordering, 9 capture, 12 chip), plugin typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean.\n\nDIRECTION CHOSEN: B (event-driven flush on agent.created), not A (bounded retry). I verified your premise in the r8 log before relying on it, and it is stronger than reported: the failed append is at 16:32:10.493Z and \"Created agent\" at 16:32:11.264Z — 771ms later, not 400ms. THREE agents hit it (a788ea99, 88503a07, 848af6ec), and paseo-fleet logs the IDENTICAL \"Unknown agent\" error at the identical timestamps on a second connection (conn_bbed8cdf). That is independent confirmation that the fleet''s design has the same race, and it matches the ordering fault I flagged in the original design note: agent.created fires AFTER agent.session_open.\n\nWhy B over A:\n1. `reason` makes the decision deterministic rather than a guess. `create` is the only pre-commit case; resume/refresh/import all mean the agent already exists and can be written inline. A retry loop would spend its attempts almost entirely on cases that already succeed on the first try, and the cases it rescues would survive only if commit lands inside the budget — a 771ms observation against a ~2s budget is not a margin I want to ship on a user''s session.\n2. agent.created is the documented \"ordinary creation finishes\" signal and the fleet already keys off event.agent.id, so the dependency is proven in production code rather than assumed.\n3. No polling on a daemon hook path.\n\nFIX\n- New server/chip-queue.ts owns the whole decision, with the host operations injected as a ChipSink so the ordering is unit-testable.\n- create: row is parked keyed by agentId, then flushed from the agent.created hook. Non-create reasons: written inline at session_open, because waiting would deadlock on an event that never fires for them.\n- The snapshot read (model/mode) moved to FLUSH time. This is a second bug the same root cause would have caused: at session_open the agent is not committed, so agents.ref(id).current() returns nothing and model/mode would have rendered as em dashes forever.\n- Parked rows are TTL-bounded (120s) and size-capped (256) so a creation that never commits cannot leak.\n- Failures are reported with the error MESSAGE. The old line printed a pino code frame (\"869 | const timeout = params.timeout\") instead of anything readable, which is part of why the failure was hard to act on.\n\nTESTS — the regression is pinned, and I mutation-verified both guards rather than trusting green\n- \"does NOT write the row at session-open time for a create\" — the r8 guard. Reverting the queue to append at session_open FAILS it.\n- \"reports an append rejection instead of swallowing it\" — re-adding the silent catch FAILS it.\n- Plus: flushes from agent.created with the correlated facts, flushes once, ignores unrelated agent.created, each of resume/refresh/import writes immediately, build failure does not attempt the append, and concurrent creates of different providers do not cross-contaminate.\n\nHonest note on my own process: one new test failed first run and the bug was in the TEST, not the code — I captured facts at cwd /a but opened the session at a different cwd, so nothing bound. Fixed the test rather than loosening it.\n\nPRIVACY UNTOUCHED, as instructed: still no preview field anywhere, still length + sha256[:12] + MCP names only, still server-only node:crypto reduction. The client still never sees the prompt.\n\nKNOWN LIMITS\n- Pixel layout at 390px is still unverified by me (jsdom has no layout). The r8 downstream assertions — expand, privacy, resume, 390px — were NOT-EXERCISABLE because no row existed; they remain unexercised until r9 sees a real row. r9 is the first real test of the chip''s rendering.\n- On resume/import the row renders all-unknown, which is honest (that session''s config was never observed) but uninformative. A per-agent cache of last-observed facts, labelled stale, is the follow-up; I did not add it because it trades a fact we can back for one we cannot.\n- This fix depends on agent.created firing for a create. If a future daemon path creates an agent without emitting it, that row is dropped after the TTL rather than written early — a visible missing chip, which is the better failure direction than a corrupt early append.\n\nREADY FOR r9: daemon restart, then QC. The r8 deploy blockers from my previous report still apply if the plugin has not been re-copied to the TEST home.\n\nUnderstood on the Space Bunny Free 403 — unrelated, and it did not affect this fix (all work done with other models by QC; my own gates did not depend on zen).", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["commit e4a8d189e (fix), ba24ad537 (feature)", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.test.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/index.server.ts", "QC evidence: /path/to/home/paseo-qc/r8-turn-window.log lines 436-454"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T16:41:19.289Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3408, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T16:41:26.734Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE — commit e4a8d189e (fix) on top of ba24ad537. QC r8 FAIL resolved: chose direction B (event-driven flush on agent.created) over A (bounded retry), and state why: `reason` makes it deterministic — create is the ONLY pre-commit case, so its row is parked until agent.created, while resume/refresh/import mean the agent already exists and write inline (a retry loop would burn attempts on cases that already succeed, and the 771ms observation vs a ~2s budget is not a margin worth shipping). Verified QC''s premise in the log and it is stronger than reported: failed append 16:32:10.493Z vs \"Created agent\" 16:32:11.264Z = 771ms; THREE agents affected (a788ea99, 88503a07, 848af6ec); and paseo-fleet logs the IDENTICAL \"Unknown agent\" at identical timestamps on a second connection, independently confirming the same race in the fleet''s design and matching the ordering fault I flagged in the design note. Also fixed a second bug the same root cause would have caused: the model/mode snapshot read now happens at FLUSH time, because at session_open the uncommitted agent made current() return nothing and model/mode would have been em dashes forever. Parked rows TTL-bounded (120s) + size-capped (256) so a never-committing creation cannot leak. Errors now logged with the message (the old line printed a pino code frame, part of why it was hard to act on). 34/34 green (13 new ordering, 9 capture, 12 chip), typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean. MUTATION-VERIFIED both guards: reverting to append-at-session_open fails \"does NOT write the row at session-open time for a create\"; re-adding the silent catch fails \"reports an append rejection instead of swallowing it\". Self-caught: one new test failed first run due to a bug in the TEST (captured facts at cwd /a but opened at a different cwd so nothing bound) — fixed the test, not loosened it. Privacy-by-construction untouched: no preview field, length + sha256[:12] + MCP names only, server-only reduction. Remaining: r9 is the first real exercise of the chip''s rendering (expand/privacy/resume/390px were NOT-EXERCISABLE in r8); 390px bounds are QC''s gate since jsdom has no layout. Daemon restart + QC r9 is the leader''s step."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3409, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T16:42:41.009Z', '{"n": 59, "status": "running", "summary": "C3 race fix delivered and restarted on TEST; QC round 9 running."}');
