INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3411, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T16:55:13.585Z', '{"agent_id": "p0-qc-playwright", "role": "P0+Trajectory+C1+C2+C3 live-QC", "model": "", "task": "C3 ctx-inject chip QC round 9", "summary": "DELIVERABLE: R9 C3 retest (fix e4a8d189e) — daemon restarted, ctx-inject ready 16:42:17Z with readable rejection logs; bundle unchanged. Fresh agent 0b603aff (opencode, created 16:44:12Z). (1) CHIP APPEARS PASS: row in ~5s with correlated create facts (no system prompt / no MCP servers / Session create / Captured 16:44), caveat on row. (2) EXPAND MIXED: mechanics PASS (desktop click + mobile native tap; testIDs absent from DOM so clicked via text); length+hash NOT-EXERCISABLE (UI agents configure no systemPrompt; detail correctly not configured); Model/Mode FAIL — em dashes: flush reads snapshot at agent.created before model/mode attach (creation record later shows model opencode/space-bunny-free + currentModeId build); Paseo-tools dash is CORRECT (providers.opencode.paseoTools UNSET). (3) PRIVACY PASS (limits disclosed): nothing to leak — config.systemPrompt empty, zero ctx-inject payloads in TEST JSON state (grep exit 1), DOM has no long runs, schema has no text field; fleet with-prompt path not exercised. (4) RESUME FAIL: reopen 0bebc110 fired inline write but append rejected Unknown agent — exists in store but not live in agent-manager; inline path assumes live handle. No false no-system-prompt claim rendered (that half holds). (5) MOBILE PASS: row x16-374 inside 390, caveat visible, native tap expands (sheet must be dismissed first). (6) REGRESSION PASS: trajectory healthy, C2 9 switches, console 0; audit 244 lines 426=0 turn_failed=1 newer=0 PII 0 (turn_failed is the disclosed Space Bunny/zen-403 probe). VERDICT: FAIL (2-model/mode + 4 fail; 1/3/5/6 pass). KNOWLEDGE: new agent landed in the workspace-worktree agent dir (not llm-server-monitoring) — attribute by creation timestamp + Captured field, not sidebar title; Switch-tab sheet intercepts taps; revisit fires no session_open for idle sessions but DOES for some (0bebc110 fired inline-write); provider retries settle (~1m15s) leaving idle failed agents.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["r9-ui-version.txt", "r9-chip-desktop.png", "r9-chip-expanded.png", "r9-chip-mobile.png", "r9-mobile-expanded.png", "r9-chip-resume.png", "r9-trajectory.png", "r9-c2-sheet.png", "r9-turn-window.log", "r9-samples.jsonl"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T16:55:13.585Z", "evaluation": {"confidence": 94, "effectiveness": 90, "guideline_adherence": 100, "task_complexity": 60, "task_size": 50, "notes": "Mixed verdict is precise: create-path flush verified end-to-end with correlated facts; the two FAILs are root-caused (flush-before-model-attach; inline-write assumes live handle). No code touched; TEST holds two idle failed-turn agents (88503a07, 0b603aff) from disclosed probes.", "telemetry": null}}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3412, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'turn_reported', '2026-09-27T16:55:57.870Z', '{"n": 60, "status": "running", "summary": "QC r9 mixed — chip live, two timing residuals handed to dev for fix round 2."}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3413, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T16:57:06.763Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 20, "note": "turn 6 (C3 fix for QC r9 MIXED/FAIL): both defects researched to a definitive answer before choosing. DEFECT 1 -> direction (a), verified not guessed: packages/protocol/src/agent-types.ts:511-532 shows AgentSessionConfig carries model? (520) and modeId? (519) and thinkingOptionId? (521), and before(\"agent.create\") delivers exactly that config. So model/mode are available at CREATE time with zero timing dependency — the cleanest option. (b) is rejected as unnecessary once (a) is known, and (c) is discarded: the timeline append API is append-only replace-by-id, there is no update, so a correction row is not expressible. DEFECT 2 -> bounded retry is correct and I confirmed no deterministic signal exists: the full plugin lifecycle event set is agent.archived/create/created/permission_requested/permission_resolved/session_open/turn_ended/turn_started plus workspace.*, i.e. nothing for \"agent became live in agent-manager\", and agent.created explicitly excludes resume, so park-until-available is impossible. Per the leader''s own instruction, when the failure IS the case a bounded retry is the right tool. Design: ChipSink gains a probe() returning {live, controls} so \"agent not live yet\" becomes an explicit retryable signal instead of a silent null (this is the trap — the snapshot read is try/caught and returns null, so a not-yet-live agent would have produced em dashes with no error and no retry). The probe result also feeds the snapshot, so model/mode are read only once the agent is live. create path takes model/mode from the create config (authoritative, no timing); resume path falls back to the live snapshot at append time. Retry policy: 4 attempts, backoff 200/500/1000ms (~1.7s, inside the leader''s 1-2s), retrying only on an \"Unknown agent\" rejection, fail-fast on any other error, and a loud final error otherwise. Injectable sleep so tests do not really wait. NOT touching the paseo-tools em dash: QC confirmed providers.opencode.paseoTools is UNSET in TEST, so the dash is correct. Privacy-by-construction untouched."}, "by": "leader"}');
