INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3421, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'lesson_added', '2026-09-27T17:01:58.862Z', '{"slug": "plugin-session_open-fires-pre-commit-timeline.ap", "title": "Plugin session_open fires pre-commit; timeline.append rejects unknown agent", "tags": ["build", "verification"], "by": "64b0b20e-2a1e-4759-b87e-9c3ea56b67cb", "updated": false}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3422, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T17:02:33.643Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C3 QC r9 fixes — configured model/mode + not-live retry", "summary": "DELIVERABLE\n\ncommit bee1e0512. 5 files touched, all inside plugins/ctx-inject. No packages/app file, no protocol change.\n\nVERDICT: done, scoped green. 44/44 (19 ordering+retry, 13 capture, 12 chip), plugin typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean.\n\nDEFECT 1 — MODEL/MODE: CHOSE (a), verified rather than guessed. packages/protocol/src/agent-types.ts:511-532 shows AgentSessionConfig carries model? (520), modeId? (519) and thinkingOptionId? (521), and before(\"agent.create\") delivers exactly that config. So both are available at create time with zero timing dependency, which is the cleanest option. I rejected (b) as unnecessary once (a) was known — no delay signal is needed when the data was never timing-dependent — and discarded (c): the timeline append API is append-only replace-by-id with no update verb, so a correction row is not expressible. ConfigFacts now carries model/modeId; buildChipData prefers the CONFIGURED value and falls back to the live snapshot only for a session that never ran the create hook, which is exactly the resume path. A model change made after creation will not rewrite the row, and that is correct: the row documents what the session was created with.\n\nDEFECT 2 — RESUME RACE: bounded retry, and I confirmed no deterministic signal exists rather than assuming. The complete plugin lifecycle set is agent.archived / create / created / permission_requested / permission_resolved / session_open / turn_ended / turn_started, plus workspace.*. Nothing signals \"the agent is now live in agent-manager\", and agent.created explicitly excludes resume, so park-until-available is impossible. Per your own instruction, when the failure IS the case a bounded retry is the right tool: 4 attempts with 200/500/1000ms backoff (~1.7s, inside your 1-2s window), retrying ONLY on an \"Unknown agent\" rejection and failing fast on anything else, since retrying a 64KiB payload violation or a closed session only delays the report. Final failure logs loudly with the message. I took your correction on the earlier calculus explicitly: that reasoning was for the create path, and you were right that it does not carry over here.\n\nTHE TRAP I HAD TO DESIGN AROUND (worth the reviewer''s attention): the snapshot read is try/caught and returns null, so a not-yet-live agent would have produced model=— and mode=— with NO error and therefore NO retry. That is the same wrong answer as defect 1, arriving silently through the retry''s back door. So ChipSink gained an explicit probe() reporting liveness as a retryable signal, and the snapshot is now read only from the attempt that actually found the agent live. There is a test asserting the probe sequence is [null, null, live-controls] for precisely this.\n\nTESTS — mutation-verified, not just green\n- Defect 1: dropping the configured model/mode fallback fails 3 tests (capture precedence + two queue tests). I also caught a tautology in my own first draft: the queue test re-implemented the precedence locally, so it could not fail that mutation. It now calls the real buildChipData, and the mutation fails 3 instead of 1.\n- Defect 2a: treating not-live as fatal fails \"waits and re-probes while the agent is not live yet\".\n- Defect 2b: removing the \"Unknown agent\" retry fails 2 tests (recovery + budget exhaustion).\n- Also covered: non-availability errors are NOT retried; exhausting the budget logs a loud error; a not-live agent throughout reports stage \"not-live\".\n- The r8 guards still hold (append-at-session-open and the silent-catch checks).\n\nSelf-correction: two of my new tests failed first run and both were bugs in the TEST, not the code — a recorder type typo (Recorder[\"controls\"] vs controlsSeen) and a vi.fn override that replaced the recorder''s own append so its success array stayed empty. I fixed the tests rather than loosening assertions.\n\nNOT TOUCHED, AS YOU ASKED\n- The paseo-tools em dash. QC confirmed providers.opencode.paseoTools is UNSET in TEST, so the dash is correct and I changed nothing there. It stays null-when-unknown rather than false.\n- Privacy-by-construction: still no preview field anywhere, still length + sha256[:12] + MCP names only, still server-only node:crypto reduction. Tests still assert the whole serialized row contains no prompt text.\n\nKNOWLEDGE FOR THE LEDGER\n1. The daemon commits an agent to agent-manager well after the hooks run (measured 771ms in r8). Any plugin that writes agent-scoped state from a before-hook races it, and the failure surfaces only as \"Unknown agent\" from requireAgent in agent-manager.\n2. There is no post-commit-per-se event. agent.created covers creates; resume/refresh/import have nothing, so those paths must poll or probe. That asymmetry is a property of the plugin API, not of this plugin.\n3. A try/caught snapshot read that returns null will silently convert \"not ready\" into \"absent\", and null is indistinguishable from a genuine unknown. Liveness needs its own signal.\n4. plugin-created agents on TEST carry no systemPrompt (UI agents), so the length/hash detail is NOT-EXERCISABLE there; only a configured-prompt agent exercises it. Worth QC knowing for r10 expectations.\n\nREADY FOR r10: daemon restart then QC. The plugin must be re-copied to the TEST paseo home if the leader has not already done so — the deploy pipeline ships only plugins/freebuff, and a plugin reload is required since web-only deploys do not refresh cached client code.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["commit bee1e0512 (fix), e4a8d189e (r8), ba24ad537 (feature)", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/ctx-capture.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.test.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/index.server.ts", "QC evidence: /path/to/home/paseo-qc/r9-turn-window.log, r9-samples.jsonl"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T17:02:33.642Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3423, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T17:02:40.876Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE — commit bee1e0512. Both QC r9 defects fixed, 44/44 green (19 ordering/retry, 13 capture, 12 chip), plugin typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean. DEFECT 1 chose direction (a), verified not guessed: agent-types.ts:511-532 shows AgentSessionConfig carries model/modeId/thinkingOptionId and before(\"agent.create\") delivers that config, so both are available at create time with ZERO timing dependency. Rejected (b) as unnecessary once (a) was known; discarded (c) because the timeline append API is append-only replace-by-id with no update verb, so a correction row is not expressible. ConfigFacts now carries model/modeId and buildChipData prefers the configured value, falling back to the live snapshot only for sessions that never ran the create hook (the resume path). DEFECT 2 chose bounded retry, after confirming no deterministic signal exists: the full lifecycle set is agent.archived/create/created/permission_*/session_open/turn_ended/turn_started and agent.created explicitly excludes resume, so park-until-available is impossible. 4 attempts, 200/500/1000ms (~1.7s), retrying ONLY on an \"Unknown agent\" rejection, fail-fast on any other error, loud final log. Took the leader''s correction on my earlier retry calculus explicitly: that was for the create path and does not carry over. KEY DESIGN POINT: the snapshot read is try/caught and returns null, so a not-yet-live agent would have given model/mode em dashes with NO error and NO retry — the same wrong answer silently through the retry''s back door. ChipSink.probe now reports liveness as an explicit retryable signal, and the snapshot is read only from the attempt that found the agent live; a test asserts the probe sequence is [null, null, live]. MUTATION-VERIFIED: dropping configured model/mode fails 3 tests (I also caught a tautology in my own first draft where the queue test re-implemented the precedence locally and could not fail that mutation, so it now calls the real buildChipData); treating not-live as fatal fails 1; removing the Unknown-agent retry fails 2. r8 guards still hold. Two new tests failed first run and both were TEST bugs (a Recorder type typo, and a vi.fn override that replaced the recorder''s own append) — fixed the tests, not the assertions. Paseo-tools em dash deliberately untouched (QC confirmed UNSET in TEST, so the dash is correct). Privacy-by-construction untouched. Leader restarts TEST and runs QC r10; plugin must be re-copied to the TEST home + reloaded if not already done."}, "by": "leader"}');
