INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3446, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T17:17:24.634Z', '{"agent_id": "0c3682da-36a0-4a47-a81d-d6cb2f131f6b", "role": "orchestrator", "model": "", "task": "orchestrator narrow poll wake 2 + lifecycle defect", "summary": "WAKE 2 narrow poll (no digest, no msgs). now=17:16:04.755Z. LIFECYCLE DEFECT: wakes_done STILL 0, wakes_remaining STILL 15, generation_started_at + checkup_id STILL null after two turn_reports (turns 62,63). Root cause: the wake counter is advanced by a heartbeat(role,action,checkup_id) tool NOT exposed in the orchestrator tier; turn_report does not advance it. So wakes_remaining==1 is UNREACHABLE and the final-wake digest plus all escalation are dead code this generation. I will not count wakes myself nor fabricate a final wake. My heartbeat 9fdb5ebb fires fine (agent-scoped); break is server-side. Hazard: prior generation d522c863 (run a4922fb0) is idle/finished with no recorded checkup_id, so it likely still owns a live heartbeat into a dead session; I cannot list or delete another agent''s heartbeat. Renewal 89df74bb active (next 18:00Z) so the next generation repeats this. Snapshot (my turns excluded): t-f3ba82ac9c leader 15s, 7ev/8m, 8/9; t-d1cf43b723 leader 561s, 2ev, 46/57, dev eb8be805 partial 204011s (verify later); t-abf10888f3 leader 1807s, 26/46; t-34d7bdf5d6 leader 67841s (candidate stale); smoke/p1 idle (not degraded); t-a4d9544ed8 5/5; t-62504d3c56 12/12.", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": [], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T17:17:24.633Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3447, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T17:19:38.060Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C3 QC r10 fix — append-first, no stricter gate", "summary": "DELIVERABLE\n\ncommit 180d59efd. 3 files, all in plugins/ctx-inject. No packages/app file, no protocol change.\n\nVERDICT: done, scoped green. 48/48 (23 ordering+retry, 13 capture, 12 chip), plugin typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean.\n\nQC WAS RIGHT AND THIS WAS MY ERROR. I accept it without qualification.\n\nWHY R10''S GATE WAS STRICTER THAN APPEND — the alignment claim, verifiable from the code\nRound 9''s probe() required `agents.ref(id).current() != null` before I would even ATTEMPT the append. `current()` returns a live SESSION HANDLE. `timeline.append` is served by `agent.timeline.append` -> `appendTimelineItem` -> `requireAgent` in agent-manager, which only needs the agent''s MAP ENTRY. A live handle implies a map entry, but not conversely: an agent can be committed to the map and still have no live session, precisely while a provider is still starting up or has 403-disabled. So the gate was a strict superset of the write''s precondition. I then used that gate as the retry trigger, which inverted the logic: instead of \"write, and learn from the write''s own failure\", it became \"do not write until a stronger condition holds\". On TEST, where Space Bunny Free is 403-disabled and provider setup is slow, the condition never held inside the budget, so the append was never issued at all and the row was lost. r9 passed precisely because it had no gate. Confirmed in r10 evidence: \"flush exhausted `agent never became available` 2.1s after session_open\" — a message only my probe could produce, and it fires before any append is attempted.\n\nMy round-9 reasoning was half right and I should be precise about the error: the SYMPTOM I described was real — a try/caught `current()` returning null cannot distinguish \"not ready yet\" from \"genuinely unknown\", so model/mode would silently render as em dashes. But I fixed a read-ambiguity problem with a gate on the WRITE, and that gate blocked writes that would have succeeded. The two concerns are separable, and round 10 proves separating them is mandatory.\n\nTHE FIX, IN YOUR PRIORITY ORDER\n1. probe() is DELETED, not weakened. There is no liveness check anywhere in front of the append. buildData runs, append is attempted, and only an \"Unknown agent\" rejection buys another attempt — the operation''s own failure is the only ground truth for its own precondition.\n2. Checked whether any snapshot/current() read remains, as asked. On the create path: NONE. Round 9''s direction (a) already sources model/mode from the create config with zero timing dependency, and QC''s own note that model/mode attach at a later record revision confirms config capture was correct — a record read would have stayed wrong forever. So the probe path is deleted outright rather than kept in reduced form. On the resume path facts are null, so there is no other source; the record is read ONLY AFTER an append has succeeded, at which point the commit is proven. Re-appending the same row id then replaces it in place — append is documented as replace-by-id (\"keeps only the latest value for the same plugin and id\"), so this is a correction in place, not a second row. Worth being explicit: this is NOT the \"correction row\" I discarded as non-expressible in round 2; that one needed an update verb, while this one uses the replace semantics that already exist. I was right to discard (c) then and right that it is expressible now, for different reasons.\n3. Budget: 8 attempts over ~15.75s, up from 4 over ~1.7s, backoff 250/500/1000/2000/3000/4000/5000. The flush is already fire-and-forget (`void` from the before-hook), so this never delays a session open — it only decides how long an idle agent keeps trying. Final failure still logs the message with stage \"append\".\n\nTESTS pin the NEW invariant by recording the ORDER of sink calls, which is the thing that broke\n- \"attempts the append before any other host call\" and \"never consults agent liveness before the write\" assert the call sequence, not just outcomes.\n- Mutation-verified: reintroducing a liveness gate ahead of the write fails 8 tests; reading controls before the write fails 5; dropping the Unknown-agent retry fails 2; the round-8 append-at-session-open guard still holds. A test also asserts the shipped budget exceeds 5s, so this cannot silently shrink back to r10''s numbers.\n- Also covered: idle-agent resume flushing after 5 consecutive rejections; no controls read at all when the create config already supplies model/mode; no rewrite when refinement adds nothing; a controls read that throws is treated as \"unknown\", not a chip failure; non-availability errors are not retried.\n\nSelf-correction this round: 4 new tests failed first run. Two were a harness defect (`rejectWith` did not actually cause rejections unless `rejectAppends` was also set, so the \"exhausted budget\" and \"non-retried error\" tests were asserting on a happy path), and two asserted a single append on the resume path, which is now legitimately two writes because of the refinement pass. I fixed the tests and made the harness semantics explicit rather than loosening assertions.\n\nNOTHING ELSE CHANGED\n- Privacy-by-construction: still no preview field anywhere, still length + sha256[:12] + MCP names only, still server-only node:crypto reduction. The whole serialized row is still asserted free of prompt text.\n- Paseo-tools stays null-when-unknown (TEST has it unset, so the em dash is correct).\n- The caveat line still renders on the row, not behind the toggle.\n\nKNOWN LIMITS, unchanged and honest\n- The create path relies on `agent.created` firing. If a future daemon path creates an agent without emitting it, that row is dropped after the TTL rather than written early — a visible missing chip, which is the better failure direction than a corrupt early write.\n- plugin-created agents on TEST carry no systemPrompt, so the length/hash detail remains NOT-EXERCISABLE there; QC should scope r11 accordingly.\n- 390px bounds remain QC''s gate — jsdom computes no layout, so the component test pins the flex contract only.\n\nREADY FOR r11: restart TEST, then QC. The plugin must be in the TEST paseo home and reloaded if the leader has not already done so — the deploy pipeline still ships only plugins/freebuff, and web-only deploys do not refresh cached plugin client code.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["commit 180d59efd (fix), bee1e0512 (r9), e4a8d189e (r8), ba24ad537 (feature)", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/server/chip-queue.test.ts", "plugins/ctx-inject/index.server.ts", "QC evidence: /path/to/home/paseo-qc/r10-*"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T17:19:38.060Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3448, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-27T17:19:46.916Z', '{"task_id": "task-c61d87f772", "title": "C3 chat view tooltip: context-inject info for the agent", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE — commit 180d59efd. QC r10 regression fixed, 48/48 green (23 ordering/retry, 13 capture, 12 chip), typecheck clean, lint 0, format clean. QC WAS RIGHT AND I ACCEPT IT: my round-9 probe() required ref().current() != null (a LIVE SESSION HANDLE) before I would even ATTEMPT the append, but timeline.append is served by agent.timeline.append -> appendTimelineItem -> requireAgent and only needs the agent''s MAP ENTRY. A live handle implies a map entry but not conversely — an agent can be committed and still have no live session while a provider starts up or is 403-disabled. So the gate was a strict SUPERSET of the write''s precondition, and using it as the retry trigger inverted the logic into \"do not write until a stronger condition holds\", which on slow/403 setup meant the append was NEVER issued. My round-9 symptom reasoning was half right: a try/caught current() returning null genuinely cannot distinguish \"not ready\" from \"unknown\" (silent em dashes), but I fixed a READ-AMBIGUITY problem with a gate on the WRITE, and that gate blocked writes that would have succeeded. r10 evidence confirms the diagnosis: \"agent never became available\" is a message only my probe could emit, and it fires before any append. FIX per QC priority order: (1) probe DELETED, not weakened — no liveness check anywhere in front of the append; the append''s own rejection is the only ground truth for its own precondition. (2) Verified whether any snapshot read remains: on the create path NONE, because round 9''s direction (a) already sources model/mode from the create config — and QC''s note that model/mode attach at a later record revision CONFIRMS config capture was the right call, a record read would have stayed wrong forever. So the probe path is deleted outright. On the resume path facts are null so the record is read ONLY AFTER an append succeeded (commit proven), then the same row id is rewritten; append is replace-by-id so that is a correction in place, NOT the non-expressible correction row I discarded in r9 — that needed an update verb, this uses existing replace semantics. (3) Budget 8 attempts over ~15.75s (was 4 over ~1.7s); the flush is fire-and-forget from the before-hook so this never delays a session open. TESTS pin the NEW invariant via the ORDER of sink calls: reintroducing a liveness gate ahead of the write fails 8 tests, reading controls before the write fails 5, dropping the Unknown-agent retry fails 2, and a test asserts the shipped budget exceeds 5s so it cannot silently shrink back to r10''s numbers. Self-corrected 4 first-run test failures: 2 were a harness defect (rejectWith did not cause rejections without rejectAppends, so the budget-exhaustion and non-retried-error tests asserted on a happy path) and 2 asserted a single append on the resume path which is now legitimately two writes due to the refinement pass — fixed the tests, did not loosen assertions. Privacy-by-construction, the always-visible caveat, and paseo-tools null-when-unknown all untouched. Leader restarts + QC r11."}, "by": "leader"}');
