INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3625, 'p-7719544617', 't-d1cf43b723', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-27T20:58:24.439Z', '{"agent_id": "6a24a038-c371-4830-9b2a-84a8a55f1289", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "Q2 gate: 3060 N x depth grid", "summary": "STEP 2 PROOF: grep -nE \"1\\.25|derive_ctx|CTX_MARGIN|CTX_MIN|VRAM_PREDICTED|VOID_GROW_FAIL\" q2cell.sh -> lines 27,29,34,39-43,116,143,185,192,234. Functional: q2cell.sh 32768 42 GT 32000 4 64 -> PREFLIGHT_FAIL required -c >= 40960, exit 4 - the pair that failed 3x is refused. Ladder now safe 3.7 tok/word (measured ~3.74 not 4.6) so requests are always shorter than target; cap ctx-outtok-2048. STEP 4: both dead cells moved to VOID-*-GROW_FAIL.txt with no cell-done marker; orphaned PCIe TSV kept as VOID. Root cause was mine, not the device. RELAUNCHED d32k-n42 then d32k-n28 at -c 40960, in flight. PREFILL CURVE BANKED in FINDINGS-turn3: N=42 no-MTP 8.64/8.13/8.28/7.92 t/s to 14,868 tok in 873 s, plus 9.10/8.21 and 8.28/8.50/8.64/8.45. Depth tax 3K->14.9K only ~-8% and noisy, so prefill is flat. Prefill is ~5x slower than no-MTP decode and NOT PCIe-bound, and more cache did not raise it - a THIRD defect and the ladder''s binding cost (80K ~= 2.6 h/cell). VRAM pred vs obs 6941/6941, 8111/8111, 8859/8855. 80K needs -c >= 106496; model says N=42 fits ~11,296, N=56 ~12,467 marginal, N=84 ~14,808 will not fit, so 80K starts at N=42. Two harness bugs this turn caught before any rig time.", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["/tmp/opencode/q2g/q2cell.sh", "/tmp/opencode/q2g/FINDINGS-turn3-prefill-depth-tax.md", "/tmp/opencode/q2g/CHECKPOINT.md", "/tmp/opencode/q2g/VOID-d32k-n42-nomtp-GROW_FAIL.txt", "/tmp/opencode/q2g/VOID-d32k-n28-nomtp-GROW_FAIL.txt"], "reported_at": "2026-09-27T20:58:24.438Z"}');
