INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3818, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T06:26:58.293Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 30, "note": "C4 turn 2 COMPLETE, commit d2cefbd7d. ITEM 2 (FULL-SCREEN DIALOG) DONE, contribution-level fullScreen flag exactly as the deviation approval directed. SHARED/HOST FILES TOUCHED (all within announced d-026489c88e): packages/plugin/src/client/contracts.ts (optional fullScreen?: boolean on PluginWorkspacePanelBase), packages/app/src/plugins/evaluate.ts (normalizeFullScreen: defaults false, rejects non-boolean at contribution time), packages/app/src/plugins/panel-dialog-host.tsx (viewport-fill when set), packages/app/src/plugins/evaluate.test.ts (3 normalization cases). Plus plugins/trajectory/index.client.tsx declaring fullScreen: true. Implementation: desktop desktopHeight=\"100%\", desktopMaxWidth=2400 (a named module constant — the card is width:100% and the overlay already pads, so only padding constrains width), compact snapPoints [\"100%\"]; the sheet''s own header/close bar kept per the owner''s choice; other plugin dialogs unaffected since the flag defaults false. IMPORTANT FINDING FOR QC, reported rather than glossed: AdaptiveModalSheet''s desktop card carries its own maxHeight \"85%\" (adaptive-modal-sheet.tsx:97) and the directive forbids editing that file, so desktopHeight=\"100%\" is CLAMPED to 85% of viewport height. Width does genuinely fill. A true 100% height needs a maxHeight override on the card — a one-line host change available if the owner wants it. BUILD NOTE: build:client does NOT cover packages/plugin, so editing contracts.ts required `npm run build:plugin`; I ran both. GATES: plugin vitest 81/81 (15 files, unchanged — this commit is host-side plus a panel declaration); app typecheck 69 errors before AND after with none in my touched files; lint 0 on all four host files. HONEST LIMIT: the new evaluate.test.ts case CANNOT run in this worktree — the whole packages/app suite dies on the pre-existing \"Cannot find package ''react-native''\" baseline, which I verified is IDENTICAL at HEAD with my changes stashed, so it is CI/QC-gated and I committed no resolver workaround. Next: turn 3, the toolbar rework in ledger-screen.tsx (Duration/Turns/Calls toggles + Search wired to the ported-but-unimported shared/dsh/search-index.ts)."}, "by": "leader"}');
