INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3824, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T06:40:10.270Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 50, "note": "C4 turn 3b COMPLETE, commit 7d9a2d2eb — PLUGIN TYPECHECK IS NOW ZERO (was 124 at HEAD). Also note for the announcement record: chromeKey was ALREADY fixed in a5c702124 (turn 3), so this commit covers the rest. Breakdown: 10x TS5097 fixed by allowImportingTsExtensions (the ported dsh modules import siblings as ./layout.ts, which PORT_NOTES records as the one upstream delta); 2x stale @ts-expect-error directives removed (react now resolves); 1x node:sqlite via a local shim beside the react-dom/client one (the resolved @types/node is 20.x, node:sqlite landed in Node 22.5), both marked for deletion when real types land. The rest were REAL bugs, not config: (a) events-to-rows built fold rows with conditional spreads so a null turn emitted turnId ABSENT instead of null — TrajectoryFoldRow.turnId is a required nullable field and layout.ts documents \"null rows fold into the enclosing turn\", so undefined was a latent bug that failed the plugin''s own type; the sibling inFlightRow omitted turnId entirely, same fix. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE CALLED OUT: this broke one existing assertion in events-to-rows.test which asserted `not.toHaveProperty(\"turnId\")` — i.e. the test ENCODED the bug. I changed it to assert turnId === null rather than working around the type. (b) rpc: z.input types limit as optional because the schema carries .default(500) but readPage forwarded it into a required field; the default is now a named constant in shared/trajectory.ts used by BOTH the schema and readPage so they cannot drift. (c) recorder: `in` narrows the key but not the value across ToolCallDetail (one variant types output as unknown) so candidates are read defensively. (d) two test helpers set kind then spread overrides containing kind again — the first assignment was dead. (e) node-store reads lastInsertRowid off the driver info object the shim types as unknown; narrowed with an explicit fallback. 15 files, all inside plugins/trajectory — NOTHING host-side crept in, confirmed by git status. Now turn 4: gantt strip — new client/trajectory-timeline.tsx wired to the ported-but-unimported shared/dsh/timeline.ts deriveTrajectoryTimeline, Sequence mode by default and Actual-time when the Duration toggle is active, Input=foregroundMuted/Model=accent/Tools=statusWarning, static bars only (no drag/zoom/tooltip), rendered above the FlatList."}, "by": "leader"}');
