INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3870, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T07:49:42.848Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 40, "note": "C4 fix round 1, turn 2: A1 FIXED and committed (591db744b). Plugin-only, NO shared-file announcement needed. 123/123 green (3 new), plugin typecheck 0, lint 0, format clean. Mutation-verified: reverting to the agentId-less open fails 3 tests, and dropping the run-state ranking fails 1. A9 VERIFIED COVERED BY A1, not a separate surface: workspace-screen.tsx:3758-3761 renders PluginHeaderButtons inside headerRight UNCONDITIONALLY — only the very next line is isMobile-gated — so the button IS present at 390px (icon-only, buttons/view.tsx:60-61 size large) and was dead for A1''s reason. I will still confirm on a 390 viewport in QC. Also noted for the record: Ctrl+K being dead is a command-palette concern distinct from C4; I am not touching it without evidence it should include plugin items. Two alternatives rejected with reasons in the commit: re-registering context:\"workspace\" would degrade the CC path to first-agent instead of active-agent (fails \"same trajectory\" requirement), and a host fix would need TWO shared files not one. NEXT: A7 — wire the on-demand text. Confirmed the real API to use is agents.ref(agentId).timeline.refetch() (client/src/index.ts:364 PaseoAgentTimelineHandle.refetch, returning { entries: [{ item: {type, text, messageId}, callId }] }), which already matches my TimelineEntryLike shape — no invented RPC. Still to do in A7: have TrajectoryPanel own usePaseo + useTrajectoryText and pass textFor down to ledger cells and the inspector, with visible-rows-only resolution. Then investigate the stacked-duplicate-dialog defect."}, "by": "leader"}');
