INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3881, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T08:01:54.127Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "C4 fix round 1 COMPLETE. Two commits, both plugin-only, no shared file touched: 591db744b (A1) and 22dd0337c (A7). Tests 121 -> 123 -> 130, 18 files, plugin typecheck 0, lint 0, tree clean. A9 verified covered by A1 (PluginHeaderButtons is rendered unconditionally at compact; QC r13 to confirm on the 390 viewport). A7 wired to the REAL API agents.ref(agentId).timeline.refetch() (client/src/index.ts:364) whose payload already matched the resolver shape, so no RPC was invented; visible-cells only via onViewableItemsChanged; resolvedText into cells and inspector; unresolvable rows keep (N chars) silently; nothing persisted or logged. TWO REAL BUGS found while testing A7, both invisible to the previous green suite and both fixed + mutation-verified: (1) the cache is a plain Map so filling it was invisible to React — a resolved cell would keep its length label until something unrelated re-rendered; the hook now bumps a version after each resolution and textFor reads it. (2) FlatList re-fires viewability every scroll tick with a fresh array, and publishing that into state LOOPS FOREVER (state change re-renders, which re-fires viewability) — surfaced as 4 test timeouts and it would have hung the real app; the panel now publishes only when the resolvable key SET changes. Also found: my resolver hooks originally sat AFTER the loading early-return in LiveLedger, i.e. conditional hooks — the exact ordering hazard that function''s own comment warns about. DUPLICATE-DIALOG DEFECT: DIAGNOSED AS HOST-SIDE, NOT FIXED (per brief). Not my A1 per-press resolution (openPanel runs once per press) and not a plugin double-open — dialog-store.ts holds a single module-global `current` and openPluginPanelDialog REPLACES it, so the store cannot stack. The real mechanism: PluginPanelDialogHost (panel-dialog-host.tsx:228) takes no props and has no route-focus awareness, while every sibling overlay in the same screen gates on isRouteFocused (e.g. workspace-screen.tsx:4113 visible={isRouteFocused && isImportSheetVisible}); with a module-global store, two simultaneously-mounted workspace screens during a route transition both render the same dialog. Candidate shared-file fix reported, not applied. No env merge performed."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3882, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-28T08:02:11.644Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C4 fix round 1 — A1, A7, duplicate-dialog diagnosis", "summary": "DELIVERABLE — C4 fix round 1, 2 commits, both plugin-only, NO shared file touched\n\n  591db744b  A1 header button opens through the agent path\n  22dd0337c  A7 on-demand row text wired end to end\n\nTests: 121 -> 123 (A1) -> 130 (A7). 18 files. Plugin typecheck 0 errors, lint 0, format clean, working tree clean. Zero deviations from this brief.\n\nA1 — ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED, NOT ASSUMED\nYour candidate was exactly right. The two openPanel contexts resolve panels differently: createPluginAgentActionContext.openPanel finds ANY panel by id then branches on its own context (so the Command Center path works), while createPluginWorkspaceActionContext.openPanel (actions.ts:91-95) FILTERS candidate.context === \"workspace\" and throws \"Workspace panel is unavailable: trajectory\". A header button has no agent context, so it always took the dead path — the host permits a workspace-context open of an agent panel nowhere.\n\nI own an error here: my turn-1 comment claimed the panel \"accepts a workspace-context open and selects that workspace''s first agent\". That described intent the host does not permit, and I did not check the host path when I wrote it. Corrected in the commit.\n\nFix: the button resolves the workspace''s agent at PRESS time via paseo.agents.list and opens with that agentId — the same agent path the Command Center item uses, so it shows the same trajectory, not a different agent. Ranking prefers a running agent over a more-recently-updated idle one, then recency. A workspace with no agent throws a named error the host surfaces rather than failing silently. Rejected and documented: re-registering context:\"workspace\" is a one-liner but degrades the CC path to first-agent instead of active-agent; a host fix needs TWO shared files (actions.ts AND panel-dialog-host.tsx, since the dialog host resolves by id AND context), not one.\n\nA9 — VERIFIED COVERED BY A1, no extra entry point added\nworkspace-screen.tsx:3758-3761 renders PluginHeaderButtons inside headerRight UNCONDITIONALLY; only the next line is isMobile-gated. So the button exists at 390px (icon-only, buttons/view.tsx:60-61 size large) and was dead for A1''s reason. QC r13 to confirm on the viewport, as agreed. Ctrl+K untouched.\n\nA7 — WIRED TO THE REAL API, NOTHING INVENTED\nLiveLedger owns usePaseo and supplies agents.ref(agentId).timeline.refetch() (client/src/index.ts:364), whose { entries: [{ item, ... }] } payload already matched the resolver''s TimelineEntryLike shape. Only the cells the ledger reports as in the viewable window are resolved (onViewableItemsChanged). resolvedText reaches every cell in place of the length label, clipped to one line, and the inspector gets a full-text section shown only when there is text. Unresolvable rows keep (N chars) silently. Nothing persisted, nothing logged, cache session-only. Also fixed: a tool_call carries its callId on the ITEM, not the fetch entry, so the tool branch was reading a field that is never present; and foldRowTextKey keys a fold row the same way, which is what lets the inspector (given a row, not a cell) resolve.\n\nTHREE REAL BUGS FOUND WHILE TESTING A7 — all invisible to the previous green suite, all fixed, two mutation-verified\n1. The cache is a plain Map, so filling it was INVISIBLE TO REACT. A resolved cell would keep its length label until something unrelated re-rendered the list — which is very plausibly part of why QC saw no text even where text could have resolved. The hook now bumps a version after each resolution and textFor reads it, so the function''s identity changes. Mutation-verified.\n2. FlatList re-fires viewability on every scroll tick with a fresh array, and publishing that straight into state LOOPS FOREVER (state change re-renders, which re-fires viewability). This surfaced as four test timeouts and would have hung the real app. The panel now publishes only when the resolvable key SET changes, which also stops redundant refetches.\n3. My resolver hooks originally sat AFTER the loading early-return in LiveLedger — conditional hooks, the exact ordering hazard that function''s own comment warns about. The loading branch now comes after every hook.\n\nDUPLICATE-DIALOG DEFECT: DIAGNOSED AS HOST-SIDE, REPORTED, NOT FIXED (per your instruction)\nNot my A1 per-press resolution — openPanel runs once per press. Not a plugin double-open — dialog-store.ts holds a single module-global `current` and openPluginPanelDialog REPLACES it, so the store cannot stack. r12-dup.png in fact shows ONE dialog, and it is correctly full-bleed (inset only by the overlay padding), so the full-screen fix is working.\n\nThe actual mechanism: PluginPanelDialogHost (panel-dialog-host.tsx:228) takes no props and has no route-focus awareness, while every sibling overlay in the same screen gates on isRouteFocused (e.g. workspace-screen.tsx:4113 `visible={isRouteFocused && isImportSheetVisible}`). Because the dialog store is module-global, two simultaneously-mounted workspace screens during a route transition each render the same dialog. Candidate shared-file fix: give the host an isRouteFocused prop and gate on it, mirroring its siblings — announced, NOT applied, since it is host scope and outside C4''s plugin boundary.\n\nWHAT QC r13 SHOULD VERIFY\n390px entry via the header button; the header button opening the ACTIVE agent''s trajectory; resolved text appearing on keyed visible rows and (N chars) persisting on unkeyed ones with no error state or console noise; and that no double dialog appears on a single Command Center open. Note the duplicate issue may still reproduce on r13 since I did not touch it.\n\nPre-existing and untouched: repo-wide typecheck red; packages/app tests unrunnable in this worktree (react-native resolver baseline, no workaround committed); format:check flags packages/server/package.json and pnpm-workspace.yaml, both unmodified and not mine. No env merge performed.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["591db744b (A1)", "22dd0337c (A7)", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-header-button.ts", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-text.ts", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-panel.tsx", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-text-wiring.test.tsx"], "reported_at": "2026-09-28T08:02:11.644Z"}');
