INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3893, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T08:06:06.351Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "C4 fix round 1 FULLY COMPLETE — 3 commits this round, all gates green, tree clean. Commits: 591db744b (A1 header button agent-path, plugin-only), 22dd0337c (A7 on-demand text end-to-end, plugin-only), 4b6d482d0 (duplicate-dialog host fix, 1 shared file under addendum d-12a0c8b77a). Tests 121 -> 123 -> 130 (18 files); plugin typecheck 0; app typecheck 69 (unchanged baseline, none in my file); lint 0. DUPLICATE-DIALOG MECHANISM NOW PROVEN FROM CODE, not inferred: the workspace deck KEEPS inactive workspaces MOUNTED (RetainedPanel only hides them with display:none + pointerEvents:none, retained-panel.tsx:44-52), and AdaptiveModalSheet renders via createPortal(desktopContent, getOverlayRoot()) on web (adaptive-modal-sheet.tsx:726-728) which ESCAPES that hidden wrapper — so an inactive workspace''s host still put a real VISIBLE dialog on the global overlay root, stacking on the active one''s. The dialog store is exonerated: single module-global `current`, openPluginPanelDialog replaces it, never stacks. Crucially the fix needed NO new plumbing: RetainedPanel already publishes active state as RetainedPanelActiveContext and EXPORTS useRetainedPanelActive, so the host gates on existing context. The authorization''s stop condition (needs a prop it does not receive) was therefore NOT reached — the announced scope held at exactly 1 file, 2 regions (line 19 import, lines 225-247 the gate + the mechanism written beside it). No regression test added: no existing test file covers this host (nothing in packages/app/src/plugins/*.test.* imports PluginPanelDialogHost) and a new one could not run in this worktree without the resolver workaround, which is not committed — CI/QC is the gate, as authorized. Handing to leader for env merge + deploy + QC r13."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3894, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-28T08:06:24.566Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C4 duplicate-dialog host fix (d-78a2802dec)", "summary": "DELIVERABLE — commit 4b6d482d0, duplicate-dialog defect fixed\n\nTHE STOP CONDITION WAS NOT REACHED — no new plumbing needed\nI verified before editing whether the gate was reachable in the announced file. It was, so I did not have to stop. RetainedPanel already publishes its active state as context and EXPORTS useRetainedPanelActive (retained-panel.tsx:3-7), so the host gates on existing context. No prop threading, no second file.\n\nANNOUNCED RANGE (d-12a0c8b77a), exactly as stated before editing\n  packages/app/src/plugins/panel-dialog-host.tsx\n    line 19        added import of useRetainedPanelActive\n    lines 225-247  the active gate on PluginPanelDialogHost, with the\n                   mechanism documented beside the check\nDiff is 17 insertions, 1 deletion, 1 file. No other behaviour changed.\n\nMECHANISM — PROVEN FROM CODE, NOT INFERRED FROM THE SCREENSHOT\nThis is the part I got wrong in my earlier diagnosis, and the correction matters:\n1. The workspace deck KEEPS inactive workspaces MOUNTED. RetainedPanel only hides them, with `display: \"none\"` and `pointerEvents: \"none\"` (retained-panel.tsx:44-52). I had assumed a route transition mounted two screens; the real cause is the retained-workspace deck, which is a permanent condition.\n2. AdaptiveModalSheet renders its content through `createPortal(desktopContent, getOverlayRoot())` on web (adaptive-modal-sheet.tsx:726-728). That portal ESCAPES the hidden wrapper. So an inactive workspace''s PluginPanelDialogHost put a real, VISIBLE dialog on the global overlay root, stacking on the active workspace''s. QC''s Playwright runs are web, so this is the path taken.\n3. The dialog store is exonerated: a single module-global `current`, and openPluginPanelDialog REPLACES it. It cannot stack by itself.\n\nSo: one open produced one dialog per RETAINED workspace screen, and only the active one should draw.\n\nThe context defaults to true, so a host mounted outside a RetainedPanel — and every test host — behaves exactly as before.\n\nNO REGRESSION TEST, AND WHY\nThere is no existing test file for this host: nothing in packages/app/src/plugins/*.test.* imports PluginPanelDialogHost, and there is no panel-dialog-host.test.*. Adding a NEW one would not \"fit the existing evaluate/host test files\", and it could not run in this worktree without the react-native resolver workaround, which is not committed. Per the authorization I am stating the reason and skipping rather than committing an unrunnable file; CI/QC is the gate.\n\nFULL C4 COMMIT LIST (12 commits, feat/trajectory-plugin)\n  79b81409f  header button (addHeaderButton, no host change)\n  d2cefbd7d  fullScreen contribution flag -> viewport-fill dialog\n  8a2ae9d31  explicit desktopHeight also sets the card ceiling\n  a5c702124  dsh toolbar: Duration/Turns/Calls + search\n  7d9a2d2eb  plugin typecheck 124 -> 0 errors\n  1abd3095b  gantt strip (3 lanes, sequence/actual)\n  6ab8f41f7  kind rails, tool success glyph, group wall-span description\n  c590c440f  on-demand text resolver + session-only cache\n  591db744b  A1: header button opens through the agent path\n  22dd0337c  A7: on-demand text wired end to end\n  4b6d482d0  duplicate-dialog host fix (this commit)\n  (plus the earlier trajectory foundation commits predating this task)\n\nTEST COUNTS\n  C4 progression: 71 -> 81 -> 89 -> 104 -> 121 -> 123 -> 130 across 18 files.\n  Fix round 1: 121 -> 123 (A1) -> 130 (A7). Plugin typecheck 0. App typecheck 69\n  (unchanged pre-existing baseline, none in any file I touched). Lint 0 on all\n  touched files. Format clean. Working tree clean.\n\nSHARED-FILE INVENTORY (C4, all announced)\n  packages/plugin/src/client/contracts.ts                      d-026489c88e\n  packages/app/src/plugins/evaluate.ts                         d-026489c88e\n  packages/app/src/plugins/evaluate.test.ts                    d-026489c88e\n  packages/app/src/plugins/panel-dialog-host.tsx                d-026489c88e\n  packages/app/src/components/adaptive-modal-sheet.tsx          d-026489c88e addendum\n  packages/app/src/plugins/panel-dialog-host.tsx (active gate)  d-12a0c8b77a addendum\nNothing else outside plugins/trajectory was modified at any point in C4.\n\nDEVIATION LOG\n  1. fullScreen on the CONTRIBUTION rather than PluginOpenPanelOptions — leader-approved.\n  2. Recorder identity persisted as `sourceMessageId`, not an integer `seq`. The brief assumed a seq exists; it does not (the SDK''s timeline.item event is {sessionId, item, timestamp} and the item payload has no seq; a seq exists only on a fetch ENTRY the recorder never sees). Same privacy class as approved, no host file changed. Leader-approved the intent; the field name is mine and is explained in c590c440f.\n  3. Search does not match resolved text — the ported index folds at derive time and never sees the post-fetch cache, so extending it means re-indexing on cache change. Explicitly permitted.\n  4. A1 fixes plugin-only rather than the host, to keep the Command Center path on the active agent.\n  5. No regression test for the host gate (reason above, as authorized).\n\nFOR QC r13\nOne Command Center open must now produce exactly one dialog. 390px entry via the\nheader button should work (A1+A9). Resolved text appears on keyed visible rows\nwhile unkeyed rows keep (N chars) with no error state or console noise. Note the\nduplicate fix is web-path specific (the portal); native uses <Modal>, which has\nits own handling, so QC should confirm the web path and I have not asserted\nanything about native.\n\nNo env merge or deploy performed — tree is clean and ready for yours.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["4b6d482d0 (duplicate-dialog fix)", "packages/app/src/plugins/panel-dialog-host.tsx", "packages/app/src/components/retained-panel.tsx (read-only evidence)", "packages/app/src/components/adaptive-modal-sheet.tsx:726-728 (read-only evidence)"], "reported_at": "2026-09-28T08:06:24.565Z"}');
