INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3911, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T08:45:33.404Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 25, "note": "C4 fix round 2 — A1 PARTIAL. DIAGNOSIS (mechanism established from code, and it is NOT QC''s hypothesis (a)/(b)/(c) as framed). PROVEN CHAIN, three verifiable facts: (1) packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/model.ts:134-146 PluginButtonStore.run sets pending=true, then `try { await action() } finally { replace(pending:false) }` — pending is cleared ONLY if the action''s promise SETTLES. (2) Same file line 135: `if (!entry || !entry.button.visible || entry.button.disabled || entry.pending) return;` — a stuck pending makes every later press a SILENT no-op. (3) packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/view.tsx:117-121 pressButton toasts ONLY on rejection. Therefore \"nothing happens, no toast, no console error\" is the exact signature of a NEVER-SETTLING onPress. It is NOT a swallowed throw (my no-agent path throws and WOULD toast, which QC observed does not happen) and NOT a missing handler (a missing handler is also silent, but then the FIRST press would have failed too, and QC''s first press worked). CONCLUSION: the wedge is PluginButtonStore.pending, and it is permanent for the session once set. WHY MY A1 CODE IS THE ONLY THING THAT CAN WEDGE IT: my onPress awaits client.paseo.agents.list() — grep confirms NO timeout exists anywhere on that path (createPaseoApi, client/src/index.ts:551-554, binds only an optional scope signal; the list overloads at :200-207 take no timeout) — before it ever reaches openPanel. So a list() that does not settle after navigation leaves the button pending forever with zero diagnostics. NOT PROVEN, AND I SAY SO: I could NOT reproduce why list() fails to settle. The app suite cannot run in this worktree (documented react-native resolver baseline, no committable workaround) and this is a cross-component lifecycle interaction (route nav -> button store -> plugin runtime -> daemon request) I cannot exercise without the host. FIX IS THEREFORE WEDGE-ELIMINATION, NOT ROOT-CAUSE: make the press path always settle by racing list() against a short timeout, so pending can never stick and a timeout REJECTS (host toasts) instead of failing silently. Plugin-only, no shared file, file I own. Also proving the two unverified A1 behaviours: (1) switch-freshness via a test where the agent ranking changes between presses; (2) no-agent workspace rejects with a named error, not silence (already covered, re-verifying)."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3912, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T08:47:23.691Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "C4 fix round 2 COMPLETE — commit 03dd66df7, PLUGIN-ONLY, no shared file. 133/133 (18 files), plugin typecheck 0, lint 0, format clean, tree clean. DIAGNOSIS (differs from QC''s hypotheses, established from host code): the wedge is PluginButtonStore.pending, not a stale closure and not a swallowed throw. buttons/model.ts:134-146 run() sets pending=true and clears it only in a finally, i.e. only if the action SETTLES; line 135 then returns early on entry.pending, so a stuck pending is a permanently silent no-op; buttons/view.tsx:117-121 pressButton toasts ONLY on rejection. So \"nothing + no toast + no console error\" is the precise signature of a NEVER-SETTLING action. QC''s (b) missing handler and (c) error-outside-catch are ruled out: my no-agent path throws and WOULD toast (QC observed it does not), and a missing handler would also have broken press #1. QC''s (a) stale client/signal is close but the closure cannot go stale — the plugin runtime is created once per installation at registry.ts:99 and contribute does not re-run on navigation. My A1 onPress is the only plugin code that can wedge it: it awaits paseo.agents.list() before openPanel, and there is NO timeout anywhere on that path (createPaseoApi client/src/index.ts:551-554 binds only an optional scope signal; list overloads at :200-207 take no timeout). EXPLICIT LIMIT: I did NOT prove WHY list() fails to settle after navigation — the app suite cannot run in this worktree (react-native resolver baseline, no committable workaround) and this is a cross-component interaction I cannot exercise without the host. This is wedge-ELIMINATION, not a proven root-cause fix, and the report says so. Fix: race the agent list against a 4s timeout so pending can never stick and a timeout REJECTS (host toasts) instead of failing silently. MUTATION-VERIFIED: removing the timeout makes the never-settling test hang to vitest''s 5s limit — the real-world symptom reproduced at unit level. BOTH UNVERIFIED A1 BEHAVIOURS NOW PROVEN BY TEST: (1) switch-freshness — a second press after the active agent changes opens the NEW agent; (2) no-agent workspace rejects with a named error naming the workspace, so the host toasts and silence is impossible. HANDING TO LEADER: env merge + deploy chain, then QC r14. Recommended QC focus: navigate away and back, then press — the button must either open a panel or toast; it must never be silent. If it toasts a timeout, that is the wedge guard working and the underlying non-settling list is then a separate host/daemon question worth its own task rather than more plugin work."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3913, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-28T08:47:37.029Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C4 fix round 2 — header button wedge (QC r13)", "summary": "DELIVERABLE — commit 03dd66df7, plugin-only, no shared file\n\nTests 130 -> 133 (18 files). Plugin typecheck 0, lint 0, format clean, tree clean.\n\nDIAGNOSIS — I verified each of your three hypotheses; the answer is not any of them as framed, and the real cause is a host mechanism my A1 code triggers\n\n1. packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/model.ts:134-146 — PluginButtonStore.run sets `pending: true`, then `try { await action() } finally { replace(pending:false) }`. `pending` clears ONLY if the action''s promise SETTLES.\n2. Same file, line 135 — `if (!entry || !entry.button.visible || entry.button.disabled || entry.pending) return;` A button left `pending` returns immediately on every later press, SILENTLY.\n3. packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/view.tsx:117-121 — pressButton toasts ONLY on rejection.\n\nTherefore \"nothing happens, no toast, no console error\" is the exact signature of a NEVER-SETTLING action.\n\nRuling out your hypotheses:\n- (c) error outside the catch path: NO. My no-agent path throws, and pressButton catches rejections and toasts them. QC observed NO toast, so nothing rejected. This also rules out \"swallowed throw\" generally.\n- (b) onPress never fires: NO. A missing handler would also have broken press #1, which worked.\n- (a) stale client/signal captured by the closure: NO. The plugin runtime is created ONCE per installation (registry.ts:99) and contribute does not re-run on navigation, so the closure cannot go stale. Your hypothesis was closest, but the stale thing is the host''s `pending` FLAG, not a stale closure.\n\nMy A1 onPress is the only plugin code that can wedge it: it awaits `paseo.agents.list()` before ever reaching `openPanel`, and there is NO timeout anywhere on that path — createPaseoApi (client/src/index.ts:551-554) binds only an optional scope signal, and the list overloads (:200-207) accept no timeout. A list that does not settle leaves the button `pending` for the rest of the session, reporting nothing.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT PROVE — stated plainly\nI could NOT establish WHY `agents.list()` fails to settle after navigation. The app suite cannot run in this worktree (documented react-native resolver baseline, no committable workaround), and this is a cross-component interaction — route navigation, button store, plugin runtime, daemon request — that I cannot exercise without the host. So this is WEDGE-ELIMINATION, not a proven root-cause fix. I am not claiming to have found the underlying cause.\n\nTHE FIX\nRace the agent list against a 4s timeout, so the press path always settles: `pending` can never stick, and a timeout REJECTS so the host toasts a message naming the workspace, instead of failing silently. A button that cannot wedge is strictly better than one that silently dies, and if the underlying non-settling list recurs it now surfaces as a diagnosable message rather than a dead control.\n\nMUTATION-VERIFIED: removing the timeout makes the never-settling test HANG to vitest''s 5s limit — the real-world symptom reproduced at unit level, which is the strongest evidence available without the host.\n\nTHE TWO UNVERIFIED A1 BEHAVIOURS ARE NOW PROVEN BY TEST\n1. Switch freshness: a second press after the active agent changes opens the NEW agent. The agent is resolved per press, so nothing needs re-registering.\n2. No-agent workspace: rejects with a named error (\"No agent in workspace w1 to open a trajectory for\"), so the host toasts. Silence is now structurally impossible.\n\nDEVIATIONS: none. No shared file touched, so no announcement was needed.\n\nFOR QC r14\nNavigate away and back, then press. The button must either open a panel or toast — it must never be silent. If it toasts a TIMEOUT, that is this guard working: the non-settling agent list is then a separate host/daemon question that deserves its own task rather than more plugin work, and I would want that diagnosed before claiming the underlying issue closed.\n\nNo deploy performed — tree clean for the chain.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["03dd66df7", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-header-button.ts", "plugins/trajectory/client/trajectory-header-button.test.ts", "evidence: packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/model.ts:134-146 and :135", "evidence: packages/app/src/plugins/buttons/view.tsx:117-121"], "reported_at": "2026-09-28T08:47:37.029Z"}');
