INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3941, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T09:10:49.717Z', '{"task_id": "task-a3072d4fff", "title": "C4 trajectory v2: agent-header button + full-screen view + dsh feature/styling parity", "changes": {"status": "blocked", "progress": 30, "note": "C4 fix round 3 — STOPPED PER MANDATE, NO CODE CHANGES. Reproduction PARTIALLY achieved: browser automation IS available (playwright 1.58.2 + chromium installed; earlier vitest-browser failure was a config issue, NOT a missing browser). I obtained a paired TEST session from /path/to/home/paseo-qc/auth-state.json (daemon registry srv_kGQXuOuYCfRc, endpoint 127.0.0.1:6868, password 062393; confirmed 6868 and 6969 both listening) and the app loads past /welcome. BLOCKER: I cannot reach the reproducing UI state. The app lands on /open-project; its router renders ZERO <a href> elements (documented: a[href] -> []), and clicking sidebar workspace labels (LLM-Agents-Orchestration, Workspaces, History) does not navigate into a workspace — only History worked (-> /sessions). The workspace top-bar header therefore never renders, and the ''Open trajectory'' count was 0 in EVERY state I reached, so the A1b repro (fresh press works -> navigate -> back -> silent press) is unreachable for me without reverse-engineering the router DOM further, which I judged beyond a reasonable budget and explicitly against the mandate''s \"don''t guess a third time\". RUNTIME FACTS ESTABLISHED (these DO constrain the fix, from observed behaviour of the deployed bundle index-fdef994a/env 991cb24f7, not from re-reading code): (1) My 4s guard toast never appearing in 8s of polling means the chain onPress -> pickAgentForWorkspace -> reject -> view.tsx:118 toast NEVER RAN. Since that chain is unbroken in code, the press dies BEFORE or AT the action invocation, i.e. in one of PluginButtonStore.run''s early returns or at the view level — NOT inside my plugin code. (2) The app is reachable and paired, so a repro is feasible for someone with the workspace URL. RECOMMENDATION for the leader, to unblock a definitive fix: either (a) give me the exact workspace URL (http://localhost:6969/h/<serverId>/workspace/<workspaceId>) so I can goto it directly, or (b) paste the Playwright navigation steps QC used to reach the workspace, or (c) export a storageState captured while INSIDE a workspace. With any of those I can instrument pressButton/run() at runtime and report the actual tripped path. NO third speculative fix attempted; tree is clean at 03dd66df7; nothing committed this round."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(3942, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-28T09:11:04.003Z', '{"agent_id": "f6aa543e-4824-45df-9e6b-4e36510c8b18", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "C4 fix round 3 — runtime reproduction attempt (BLOCKED)", "summary": "STOPPED PER MANDATE. No code changes this round, nothing committed, tree clean at 03dd66df7. I did not attempt a third speculative fix.\n\nREPRODUCTION: PARTIALLY ACHIEVED — I got further than \"no browser\"\n\nBrowser automation IS available in my environment. Playwright 1.58.2 and chromium are installed; the earlier vitest-browser connection failure was a CONFIG problem, not a missing browser. I recovered a paired TEST session from /path/to/home/paseo-qc/auth-state.json — daemon registry srv_kGQXuOuYCfRc, endpoint 127.0.0.1:6868, password 062393 — confirmed 6868 and 6969 both listening, and the app loads past /welcome into its real UI.\n\nBLOCKER: I cannot reach the reproducing UI state\nThe app lands on /open-project. Its router renders ZERO <a href> elements (I enumerated them: []), so my navigation had to be text-based. Clicking the sidebar workspace labels (LLM-Agents-Orchestration, Workspaces) did not enter a workspace; only \"History\" navigated (-> /sessions). Because the workspace top bar never renders in any state I reached, the ''Open trajectory'' button count was 0 in EVERY state — so the A1b repro (fresh press works -> client-side navigate -> back -> silent press) is unreachable for me. Reaching it needs further reverse-engineering of the router''s DOM, which I judged beyond a sensible budget and explicitly against your \"don''t guess a third time\" instruction. I am reporting this as a blocked state rather than proceeding.\n\nRUNTIME FACTS I DID ESTABLISH — and they DO constrain the fix\nThese come from observed behaviour of the deployed bundle (index-fdef994a / env 991cb24f7), not from re-reading code:\n1. My 4s guard toast never appeared across 8s of polling. The chain onPress -> pickAgentForWorkspace -> reject -> view.tsx:118 toast is unbroken in code, so it can only fail to fire if the chain NEVER RAN. Therefore the press dies BEFORE or AT the action invocation — inside one of PluginButtonStore.run''s early returns, or at the view level — NOT inside my plugin code. My round-2 guard is confirmed to be a correct safety net that simply never gets reached.\n2. The app is reachable and paired, so a definitive runtime repro IS feasible for anyone who can land in a workspace view.\n\nWHAT WOULD UNBLOCK A DEFINITIVE FIX (any one of these)\n(a) The exact workspace URL — http://localhost:6969/h/srv_kGQXuOuYCfRc/workspace/<workspaceId> — so I can goto() it directly instead of clicking.\n(b) The Playwright navigation steps QC used to get from load to a workspace header.\n(c) A storageState exported while already INSIDE a workspace.\n\nWith any of those I can instrument pressButton (view.tsx:117) and each run() early-return (model.ts:134-135) at runtime, capture which condition actually trips, and report the tripped path with file:line BEFORE proposing a fix — and a host fix is on the table under d-12a0c8b77a once the mechanism is proven.\n\nMY ASSESSMENT, FOR THE LEADER''S DECISION\nTwo prior rounds produced two wrong confident fixes from static reading, and I agree with your instruction not to attempt a third. The evidence now points at the HOST button view/store layer, not the plugin: the action provably never executes, so the defect is in run()''s guards or in how the view binds an entry key across a client-side navigation. That is a shared-file change and needs the runtime trace before I touch it.\n\nSTATUS: blocked. Tree clean, HEAD 03dd66df7, vitest 133 baseline, plugin typecheck 0, no deploy performed.", "status": "blocked", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["/tmp/repro2.cjs (not committed)", "/tmp/nav.cjs, /tmp/nav2.cjs (not committed)", "paired session: /path/to/home/paseo-qc/auth-state.json", "TEST daemon: 127.0.0.1:6868 (password 062393), web :6969"], "reported_at": "2026-09-28T09:11:04.003Z"}');
