INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4188, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T16:53:41.270Z', '{"task_id": "task-4879b96968", "title": "G0: plugins/trajectory CI workflow (gating prerequisite, not dsh-derived)", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "ACCEPTED 2026-09-28, commit e26caed54 (.github/workflows/paseo-trajectory-plugin.yml, 82 lines, ONE file, nothing else in .github/workflows changed). Leader-verified: ci contract test scripts/ci-workflow.test.mjs still 9/9 PASS (it deepEquals .github/ci-paths.yml routing, so a standalone file is legal and a ci.yml job would not be); YAML parses, 1 job 9 steps; hoisted vitest run 146/146 pass; repo-wide format IS red at base (pnpm-workspace.yaml + 1) and lint IS red at base (9 errors), so scoping those steps to the plugin is correct - a gate that always fails gates nothing; npx vitest from the plugin fails with \"sh: 1: vitest: not found\", confirming the dev''s correction of my brief. The dev refused to model on a file I told it to copy, because that file does not exist - correct call, see d-3a2b6f5c1a."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4189, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T16:53:44.389Z', '{"task_id": "task-17a27083bc", "title": "G1: the trajectory plugin is ungated at three levels — not a workspace member, no CI, and the pre-commit typecheck cannot see it; monorepo typecheck is red at base (225 undeclared-dep errors)", "changes": {"note": "LEADER ERROR CORRECTED 2026-09-28, see d-3a2b6f5c1a. The original detail claimed .github/workflows/paseo-orchestration-plugin.yml gates plugins/paseo-orchestration and that the plugin had no CI workflow. BOTH WRONG. VERIFIED: .github/workflows contains android-apk-release, ci, deploy-app, deploy-relay, deploy-website, desktop-packages, desktop-release, desktop-rollout, docker, nix-update-hash, nix, paseo-manual-pipeline, paseo-trajectory-plugin (new), release-notes-sync. There is NO paseo-orchestration-plugin.yml on this branch or in git log --all, and grep -rl paseo-orchestration over the repo returns nothing. plugins/ contains ctx-inject, freebuff, trajectory - there is no plugins/paseo-orchestration. The only real CI contract is ci.yml routing through .github/ci-paths.yml, asserted by deepEqual in scripts/ci-workflow.test.mjs (9 tests, still passing after G0). CORRECTED candidates: (a) make plugins/ workspace members so ci.yml''s typecheck and test jobs cover the plugin, which also deletes the standalone workflow and its symlink shim - the real structural fix, and it closes the T0 open item about the plugin not being a workspace member; (b) scope the lefthook pre-commit typecheck job the way format and lint already are, or baseline-diff it so it fails only on NEW errors - smallest change that restores signal; (c) add plugins/trajectory routing to .github/ci-paths.yml as a ci.yml job, which REQUIRES updating the deepEqual contract in scripts/ci-workflow.test.mjs deliberately, so it is a joint change and not a quiet one; (d) declare the undeclared deps in packages/app, packages/website, packages/desktop package.json; (e) fix the monorepo typecheck to green at base, which is the prerequisite for any pre-commit typecheck to mean anything. Also note the G0 shim''s latent coupling: it links zod and vitest from packages/plugin''s install, and both currently resolve to the plugin''s pinned versions (zod 4.4.3, vitest 4.1.10), but packages/plugin floats them with carets - if that install moves, CI typechecks the plugin against a version the plugin does not declare. Adding the plugin as a workspace member (a) removes the shim and the hazard together."}, "by": "leader"}');
