INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4193, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T17:00:34.535Z', '{"task_id": "task-020b153277", "title": "S2 (dsh Phase 2, c8ece8325c): tail-follow correctness before virtualizing", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "ACCEPTED 2026-09-28, commit 26424dc30 (2 files, +139/-22, plugin-only, worktree clean). Leader-verified: followRef at ledger-screen.tsx:73 is the only follow site, read at :270, written at :296, no leftover state; onContentSizeChange deps are now [] so its identity is stable; threshold kept at 24px and NAMED BOTTOM_FOLLOW_THRESHOLD_PX with dsh''s 2px and the reason for diverging recorded in the comment rather than silently narrowed; no getItemLayout/windowSize/maxToRenderPerBatch added (grep over the diff confirms); the FlatList stand-in is now React.forwardRef so React actually attaches the ref; 149/149 plugin tests pass on an independent run. Two real defects fixed, both verified by reading the diff: (1) blind re-arm - a scroll event with no contentSize was read as \"at the bottom\" because the old fallback set contentHeight=0, making 0+viewport >= 0-24 always true, so the next append yanked a scrolled-up view back to the tail; now undefined returns early and leaves follow alone. (2) follow was state read in one place and never rendered, so a flip re-rendered the whole screen mid-scroll; it is a ref, and the flip now costs zero renders. The dev measured before changing anything and reported that follow''s FUNCTION was already correct, keeping the four functional criteria as a regression guard rather than dressing a no-op as a fix - correct call. INCIDENTAL FINDING, confirmed by the leader and now tracked in G1: the plugin''s own `npm run test` fails on a clean checkout with \"vitest: not found\", because the plugin declares test/typecheck scripts but has no install of its own and the root carries no vitest. CI works around it with symlinks plus a by-path binary, so the documented dev loop is broken while CI has a bespoke path."}, "by": "leader"}');
