INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4246, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-09-28T18:30:28.288Z', '{"task_id": "task-37304e8bb5", "title": "S3e (dsh 92de5bb6d4, part e): browser e2e pinning the mounted-row ceiling and row geometry — needs a cross-tree write into packages/app/e2e", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 50, "note": "FIRST HALF LANDED, commit c1ecaf8b8, 2 files (client/ledger-screen.window.test.tsx + the plugin-local vitest.config.ts), plugin-only, worktree clean. BROWSER HALF STILL GATED on owner authorisation. Leader-verified independently: 173/173 across 21 files, lint 0/0, tsc exit 0. THE REAL FlatList HAS NOW RUN FOR THE FIRST TIME in this plugin - all six client test files mocked react-native wholesale, so the virtualization path had never executed. vitest.config.ts:50 introduces test.projects, the default project excluding the new spec at :79, and a real-list project at :104-106 aliasing react-native to react-native-web at :99. Mounted counts are 24 at 50, 200, 800 and 3200 turns, folded and unfolded - bounded by initialNumToRender and INDEPENDENT of history size. The spec asserts all three properties, not one: independence (paired small/large comparison at :117), the ceiling at :131-132, and a NON-ZERO FLOOR at :134-135, so 0==0 cannot satisfy it and a ceiling alone cannot pass for an accidentally huge window. THE GATE GOT WIDER: 172 -> 173 tests, 18 -> 21 files. TWO INSTRUMENTS THAT PRODUCED A WRONG ANSWER WHILE APPEARING TO MEASURE SOMETHING, both self-reported by the dev: the first attempt read 0 rows because createRoot().render() is async in React 19 and the first paint had not flushed - and the 0 looked exactly like the finding the leader had predicted, so filing it would have produced a non-finding; and the first red was smallMounted 24 / largeMounted 48, which reads precisely like \"the window grows with N\", when mountLedger had actually mounted a second screen without unmounting the first so every count doubled. The dev refused to file either as a finding about the system and said what each actually was. That is the FOURTH such instrument on this track. It also measured the container-height pin the leader told it to add and found it INERT under jsdom - removing it changes nothing, because the bound comes from initialNumToRender while the scroll metrics are 0 - and kept the pin with a comment stating it exists so the spec matches the browser the gated half will run in, not because it works here. NOT ATTEMPTED AND NOT APPROXIMATED: real windowing in Chromium, geometry drift, and anchor stability across a prepend. Those need the browser and the cross-tree authorisation, and are not to be claimed on the strength of this work."}, "by": "leader"}');
