report -> v119 inverted rationale -> v121 over-claim -> v123 reversal -> v127 fix a non-bug -> v128 reversal -> v129 confound decomposition -> v130 WITHDRAWS v129 and v128. The v129 confound analysis was itself built on a bad denominator, so the 3-turn run of ''increasingly sophisticated self-correction'' resolves to one undetected unit error. v129 is the same SPEC-vs-SOURCE defect as v127, not a new class.", "Health 7-8, carried forward from wake 5, NOT re-scored. Rationale for not downgrading: detection latency is still one tick and the reversal is self-caught, which is what the 7-8 band already accounts for. But flagging for the leader''s attention: three of the last four turns invalidated a previous turn''s own number. If a fourth occurs, this crosses from drift into a correctness problem the leader should own rather than absorb.", "Wake spacing remains compressed (wake 10 at 10:00:44, wake 11 at 10:01:31) — 3rd off-cadence fire in a row. paseo owns scheduling, noted not acted on.", "UNCHANGED, not re-polled: t-f3ba82ac9c IDLE; t-a124729a8a PR #30 open; t-abf10888f3 + t-34d7bdf5d6 frozen undeliverable; t-2328df2e93 complete.", "no digest, no escalation, no messages (wakes_remaining 15 > 1)"], "reported_at": "2026-09-29T10:01:58.117Z"}');
