INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4640, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-62504d3c56', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-30T01:18:20.330Z', '{"agent_id": "edd9c203-8517-4322-9f14-0d2a0568939f", "role": "orchestrator", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "wake 3 narrow poll: counter is tier-limited not broken (t-d1cf43b723 reads 15/0/checkup 08c2b0ba); both escalation targets unreachable 6th gen", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] Wake 3/15 NARROW POLL, 11 calls. Boot step 2 STILL UNSATISFIABLE: this MCP surface exposes only the 9 leader-tier tools (fleet/history/leader_register/task_add/task_update/track_close/track_create/track_status/turn_report). heartbeat, track_list, summary_read, summary_write all absent, so the mandated confirm cannot be emitted and generation_started_at stays null on all 8 active tracks. NEW EVIDENCE, sharpens the owner fix: the counter is NOT broken, this TIER lacks the tool — t-d1cf43b723 reads wakes_done=15, wakes_remaining=0, checkup_id=08c2b0ba, so a collector that HAD heartbeat counted correctly to exhaustion. Both escalation targets remain UNREACHABLE (6th generation, deliberately not re-probed): t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01 runs omp+command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash and t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1 runs omp+z-ai/glm-5.3-flash; both providers are in disabled_providers. t-abf10888f3 model_verified:true is STALE and must not be read as liveness. Pacing off paseo maxRuns=15, the only counter that moves. No digest, no messages, no self-archive.", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["COUNTER DIAGNOSIS REFINED — the one new fact this wake, and it changes the owner fix from ''the wake counter is broken'' to ''this tier lacks the heartbeat tool''. t-d1cf43b723 reads orchestrator {wakes_done: 15, wakes_remaining: 0, checkup_id: 08c2b0ba, generation_started_at: 2026-09-28T00:02:11.304Z}: a prior generation that HAD the tool counted correctly to exhaustion and then stopped. Meanwhile all 8 active tracks I polled read generation_started_at: null and wakes_remaining: 15, because MCP_ORCH_TIER resolves to the leader allowlist (config.py:269 TOOL_TIERS[''leader''] = track_create/track_close/track_status/leader_register/turn_report/history/fleet/task_add/task_update), which omits heartbeat. heartbeat is callable from any role per TOOL_UTILITY (config.py:292-297) but is absent from MY tool schema, so I cannot emit the call. FIX: set MCP_ORCH_TIER=orchestrator on the harness the mcp-orchestrator schedule spawns — NOT in this agent''s repo config, since opencode.json:17 pins ''leader'' for the repo and opencode.jsonc sets none.", "BOOT STEP 2 UNSATISFIABLE, 3rd consecutive generation to hit it (263111fc, 20ca71d4 at 2026-09-29T18:52Z, and me ed9c203). I did NOT read wakes_remaining before confirming (I could not confirm), did NOT claim any wake, and did NOT archive myself — archiving on a non-final wake would sever the renewal chain. Pacing off paseo maxRuns=15 via heartbeat 12addc2e, which self-exhausts and leaves no orphan.", "BOTH ESCALATION TARGETS UNREACHABLE, 6th generation, DELIBERATELY NOT RE-PROBED: re-sending to an unchanged absent provider is the command-spam I am not exempt from. t-abf10888f3 leader 14fe3d01-2197-4583-ae27-83b16e1acb96 runs omp + command_code/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, last_turn_age_s 141188 (~39.2h). t-34d7bdf5d6 leader a572d1d1-ff0a-4988-9594-480f05d7cbdf runs omp + z-ai/glm-5.3-flash, model_verified FALSE, last_turn_age_s 161478 (~44.9h), 3 running tasks frozen at 12/98/95%. Both providers appear in disabled_providers in ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc, read at boot. t-abf10888f3 asserts model_verified: true — STALE, signed 2026-09-26T15:34:12Z, never re-checked.", "HEALTH (scored once, carried forward, NOT re-scored on later wakes): t-d1cf43b723 9 — leader 8c8a2d29 at v170, last_turn_age_s 769, five consecutive turns v166-v170 each a SELF-CAUGHT correction with a stated reason and a measurement, converging not oscillating; explicitly NOT command-spam, since that flag needs repeated commands with no good reason and these are reasoned claim revisions. t-f3ba82ac9c 8 — turn 192 at 00:00:36Z, leader deliberately parked awaiting owner, 15 tasks/14 done/1 open (task-d6d6317d13 T1 at ready/50%, a gate state so the running-task rule does not fire). t-a124729a8a 7 — the 19.3h quiet is the CONSEQUENCE of leader decision 2026-09-28T22:07:57 to delete its own heartbeat and park, not a stall; heartbeats block entirely null confirms deliberate; 8 tasks/6 done/2 open with S5b correctly gated at user-decision. t-62504d3c56 7 collector-owned, 18/12/6. t-2328df2e93 8 — one-shot smoke test, ZERO open tasks, purpose proven 2026-09-02; a throwaway lane is not degraded. t-a4d9544ed8 8 — leader NULL, turn_count 0, all 5 tasks done 100% since 2026-09-11; zero open tasks means complete, not degrading; the only defect is bookkeeping (status still ''active'', track never closed). t-abf10888f3 4. t-34d7bdf5d6 3.", "OWNER ACTION ITEMS (4, none mine to fix): (1) Set MCP_ORCH_TIER=orchestrator on the collector''s schedule harness — until then NO collector on this surface can ever reach its own final wake, which is why 6 generations have each had to pace off paseo maxRuns instead. (2) Re-leader t-abf10888f3: two owner-reported P0s (F11 task-d10866b229 session-hangs-on-in-use-account, F12 task-86c59505fd composer-account-select) stranded behind a provider in disabled_providers. A live-verified same-family substitute exists at omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash (leader priority 1), so a re-leader is spawnable on authorisation — a leader/owner decision, not mine. (3) ORPHANED COLLECTOR SESSIONS: t-62504d3c56 now carries 8 prior orchestrator worker records — 62b157c2, ed2900e5, 447b15e3, 53744432, b0ed68d6, 601eef62, 263111fc, 20ca71d4 — seven status=partial. paseo_delete_heartbeat is agent-scoped and refuses cross-agent deletes, so I cannot clean them; their creators or the owner must. This accumulation is exactly what the final-wake self-archive prevents, and that step is unreachable on this tier. (4) Fleet position 1 for orchestrator is bifrost/opencode-zen/mimo-v2.6-flash-free and bifrost is ALSO in disabled_providers — if the schedule resolves by priority, that entry cannot start.", "NOTED, NOT SCORED: t-f3ba82ac9c''s leader re-probes the absent summary_read tool on nearly every deep tick (''summary_read still missing (re-probed)'' in turns 183-192). A repeated probe of a known-missing tool is the mildest form of the pattern I score as command-spam; it is cheap and the lane is correctly parked, so I did not downgrade health, but a leader holding the tool list would stop re-asking.", "LIFECYCLE DISCIPLINE: no decisions recorded, no code touched, no agents spawned, no schedule changed, no messages sent, no self-archive. This turn_report is the single write this wake, into the COLLECTOR-OWNED track only — never a leader''s track, since my turns would inflate its turn_count and corrupt its staleness signal. First attempt was rejected: turn_report status enum is [''blocked'',''handing_off'',''idle'',''running''] and does NOT accept ''partial'' (that value is valid for worker_reports only)."], "reported_at": "2026-09-30T01:18:20.330Z"}');
