INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(4655, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-62504d3c56', 'worker_reported', '2026-09-30T02:48:58.891Z', '{"agent_id": "edd9c203-8517-4322-9f14-0d2a0568939f", "role": "orchestrator", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "FINAL WAKE 15/15: 8-track digest written, 2 escalations rejected (provider gone), self-archive", "summary": "[#Orchestrator] FINAL WAKE 15/15 (paseo maxRuns). 8-track digest written to orchestration/state/mcp/orchestrator-digest.json, prior rotated to .prev.json. COUNTER CORRECTION, and I will not dress this up: the server read wakes_remaining=15, wakes_done=0, generation_started_at=null, checkup_id=null on my FINAL wake. I did NOT get a server-assigned final wake. Boot step 2 was unsatisfiable all generation because this tier exposes only the 9 leader-tier tools and heartbeat is not among them, so generation start was never stamped. I took the full collection because this was the last paseo maxRuns=15 wake, the only counter I can observe expiring - not because the server told me so. ESCALATION: 2 attempted, 0 delivered, 2 REJECTED, both ''references unavailable provider freebuff-plugin''. Health 9/8/8/8/7/7/4/3. HEADLINE: t-d1cf43b723 v174 - the leader refutes its own track premise, asserting the expert cache is bypassed when n_rows>16 at N=128 while t0002 prefill arms chunk at ub512/ub2048/ub8192, so the cache does not participate in the measurements the track exists to explain. Unverified by me. Self-archiving.", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["COUNTER — stated plainly because I refused to infer it. Final-wake track_status on t-62504d3c56 at now=2026-09-30T02:48:05.890Z reads orchestrator {wakes_total:15, wakes_done:0, wakes_remaining:15, generation_started_at:null, checkup_id:null}. Never decremented in 15 reads. I took the final collection on paseo maxRuns=15, not on server authority. Digest field ''counter_correction'' records this so no future reader mistakes my pacing for a server-assigned final wake.", "DIGEST persisted to orchestration/state/mcp/orchestrator-digest.json (9,635 bytes, 8 tracks, per issue #48 §7 shape), prior generation rotated to orchestrator-digest.prev.json. Health: t-d1cf43b723 9, t-f3ba82ac9c 8, t-a4d9544ed8 8, t-2328df2e93 8, t-62504d3c56 7, t-a124729a8a 7, t-abf10888f3 4, t-34d7bdf5d6 3. Task counts read from the store: 58/47/11, 14/13/1, 18/12/6, 9/6/3, 46/26/20, 5/2/3, 0/0/0, 5/5/0.", "ESCALATION RESULT, recorded only after the attempt. 2 attempted, 0 delivered, 2 failed. 14fe3d01 (t-abf10888f3) REJECTED and a572d1d1 (t-34d7bdf5d6) REJECTED, both ''references unavailable provider freebuff-plugin''. I re-read the live catalog IMMEDIATELY before sending (fleet live=true, checked_at 2026-09-30T02:48:26.014Z): zero freebuff entries, zero command_code entries, zero z-ai entries - so a provider restored mid-generation could not have been missed. Recorded UNDELIVERABLE-NEEDS-HUMAN, not retried: a leader whose provider is gone is UNREACHABLE, not idle. 6th consecutive generation. The other 6 tracks scored >=6, so no message per the rule.", "HEADLINE FINDING - t-d1cf43b723 v174, logged as a substantive ''stuck''-class anomaly separate from the process health score. Leader 8c8a2d29 asserts: guard at moe-cache.cu:9439 fires FALLBACK when n_routes>n_slots; n_routes=top_k*n_rows; at N=128 that is n_rows>16, so the expert cache participates only up to 16 prefill tokens per call; t0002''s prefill arms chunk at ub512/ub2048/ub8192, therefore the cache does not participate in the measurements the track was started to explain. This is the track''s own premise refuted by its own leader after nine turns (v166-v174) of self-correction. I did NOT verify the arithmetic; the digest says so and names it as three code lines to check. Health stays 9 because the score is on process and the process is exemplary.", "t-f3ba82ac9c command-spam anomaly, confirmed at wake 10 on the event log: turns 184/186/188/191/193 all report ''no events since pass 16'' across ~18h, and ''pass 16'' predates the idle determination; turns 185/187/189/190/192 re-probe the absent summary_read. Health held at 8 - the track is sound (14/15 done, parked by decision), only tick hygiene is defective.", "OWNER ACTION ITEMS (5). (1) Set MCP_ORCH_TIER=orchestrator on the collector''s schedule harness - not this repo''s opencode.json, which pins ''leader''. Until then no collector on this surface can reach its final wake; this is the 3rd generation to report it and 11 orphaned collector sessions now exist because the confirm step and the self-archive step share the same missing tool. (2) Re-leader t-abf10888f3 and t-34d7bdf5d6: 4 owner-reported P0s stranded 39-45h; omp/opencode-go/glm-5.3-flash is live_verified at leader priority 1, same family as the binding model. (3) 11 orphaned collector sessions on this track; paseo_delete_heartbeat is agent-scoped and refuses cross-agent deletes, so I cannot clean them - creators or owner must. (4) Fleet orchestrator position 0 is omp/bifrost/opencode-zen/mimo-v2.6-flash-free and bifrost is also in disabled_providers. (5) turn_report status enum rejects ''partial'' (allowed: blocked|handing_off|idle|running); valid for worker_reports only, and the error hint does not say so.", "LIFECYCLE DISCIPLINE across the whole generation. Exactly two lifecycle actions: created my OWN checkup heartbeat 12addc2e at boot, and on this final wake two send_agent_prompt attempts plus paseo_archive_agent on myself. No other agent was ever messaged or archived. No decisions recorded, no code edited, no commits, no dev/QA spawned, no schedule changed. All turns written to the collector-owned track t-62504d3c56 only - never a leader''s track, since my turns would inflate its turn_count and corrupt its staleness signal."], "reported_at": "2026-09-30T02:48:58.891Z"}');
