INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5528, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-10-02T01:29:25.166Z', '{"task_id": "task-d833025a8e", "title": "T7-F: clear-cap delete semantics (empty Save must remove the scalar)", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "DONE. Commit eb7769fc2 on feat/provider-config (chain e92d11e60 -> dee548451 -> 0902c1795 -> eb7769fc2). MECHANISM: explicit null delete marker, on the PATCH entry schema only (new MutableDaemonProviderConfigPatchEntrySchema = base .partial().extend({maxContextTokens: nullable}).passthrough()). Keeping the marker off the published schema means a client can never receive one back. Store splits markers in BOTH patch directions - the overrides it persists (applyMutableProviderConfigToOverrides) and the mutable view it hands back (new omitDeletedProviderFieldsFromConfig alongside the existing omitProvidersFromConfig). Non-obvious: ProviderOverrideSchema types the field number|undefined, so parsing a raw null THROWS invalid_type - markers must be stripped BEFORE the parse as well as after the merge; a strip-after-only fix fails every clear. Emptied provider entry stays as {} rather than pruned. Emptyed-entry choice documented. GATES: typecheck protocol 0 / server 0 / app 70 (byte-identical to 0902c1795, known +1 react-dom/client TS7016); lint 0/0 on 6 files; format clean; protocol suite 706/706 (63 files); server scoped 111 green; app scoped 65 green. DEFECT GUARD: verified failing-before by stashing only the store fix - 4 of 5 new store guards error on the unhandled null; one test records that {} still merges to a no-op. New tests: 5 store (3 override-merge + 2 end-to-end patch/disk/reload) + 3 client patch-encoding. Tree clean, donor symlinks removed. No protocol feature gate (old server has no cap to clear; documented in commit body). No PR."}, "by": "leader"}');
