INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5565, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-10-02T02:58:51.068Z', '{"task_id": "task-5198266570", "title": "T8: mobile trajectory close button — single-row toolbar, no overlap", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "T8 LANDED: commit 321ee2ca7 (one scoped commit, plugin + host, LEFTHOOK=0, no PR). Pre-flight df -i IFree=67 (>=30 floor, proceeded); end-of-task IFree=60, no ENOSPC, no new files.\n\nROOT CAUSE (both owner defects, one element): NOT a wrapping toolbar - the bar is flexDirection row + default nowrap so a child cannot wrap. The \"X on a second row\" and the \"orphaned rounded-square\" are BOTH the sheet floating close layer: position absolute, top 0, paddingTop insets.top+SPACING[3], zIndex 1, rendered as a sibling BEFORE the body. Because the plugin surface starts flush at 0,0, on 390/430pt that puts the 32pt surface2-filled square at y~56-88, below the toolbar row (y~20-54), on top of the column header + sequence strip. It is the only filled X in the dialog, so it read as an orphan while the ghost toolbar glyph read as missing.\n\n(b) RULING: dropped the compact floating control outright - surfaceOwnsClose now suppresses on EVERY form factor. The toolbar is a sibling of the FlatList, not a ListHeaderComponent, so its X never scrolls away; PanelNotice carries trajectory-notice-close for the notice/loading states. Both preconditions are genuinely true, so no scroll case remains to justify a fallback. resolveSheetClose deleted (it was just a negation); showSheetClose = surfaceOwnsClose !== true, keeping AdaptiveModalSheet under the complexity ceiling.\n\nGREP PROOF: surfaceOwnsClose in exactly 2 files (definition + panel-dialog-host.tsx:230) across 36 AdaptiveModalSheet call sites; edgeToEdge has exactly one consumer (same line). Flip is trajectory-only in effect.\n\nGATES: trajectory vitest 239 -> 240 green (one run), plugin tsc 0; app typecheck 69 with the error SET diffed against the T4-B baseline (added none, removed none); lint 0 errors on all 4 touched files; format:files run. New test asserts the phone single-row contract: bar flexDirection row, 2 children, both siblings of the bar, field flex:1 + minWidth 0, close flexShrink 0, hitSlop 9."}, "by": "leader"}');
