INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5584, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-10-02T03:19:27.997Z', '{"task_id": "task-e40d2063fb", "title": "T9: human-readable row durations (32s / 3m45s)", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "T9 LANDED. Commit b7c5b81e0 (one scoped commit, plugin only, LEFTHOOK=0, no PR, no host file). Pre-flight df -i IFree=31 (>=30 floor, proceeded); post-commit IFree=14, no ENOSPC.\n\nHELPER: formatDurationMillis in plugins/trajectory/shared/dsh/record.ts. Already the single funnel - formatElapsedSeconds delegates to it, so no consolidation needed. formatTimelineOffset (shared/dsh/timeline.ts) also delegates and has zero production callers, so the strip''s visual SCALE is untouched per spec.\n\nRULES: <1000ms -> \"N ms\"; >=1000ms and <60s -> whole seconds; >=60s -> \"XmYs\" with the seconds part always shown (60,000ms renders \"1m0s\" - literal reading of the spec; dropping a zero seconds part would be a second unrequested rule). Every tier FLOORS: 32,400 -> 32s, 224,999 -> 3m44s, 1,999 -> 1s, 129,999 -> 2m9s. Documented in the function doc including the no-hour-tier consequence (an hour-long call reads 60m0s) and that a negative duration is wrong data, not a short duration, so it renders as the em dash.\n\nCALL SITES (all via the one helper, zero per-site logic): ledger-cells.tsx:244 DurationText STATS column (+ its stale \"N,NNN ms\" comment); trajectory-inspector.tsx:69 detail Duration field; trajectory-timeline.tsx:242 strip tooltip; shared/dsh/layout.ts:229 formatGroupDuration -> groupDescription wall span and own-duration totals.\n\nTESTS: +9 in new shared/dsh/record.test.ts (0/130/999/999.9/1000/32000/59999/60000/61000/225000, floor cases 32400/224999/1999/129999/59400/2500, unknown null/NaN/Infinity, negatives, formatElapsedSeconds parity). Four existing test files updated to new strings: 1,500 ms -> 1s x3, 2,400 ms -> 2s x3, ledger-screen fold assertion, tooltip regex /ms|—/ -> exact tier alternation.\n\nGATES: trajectory vitest 240 -> 249 green (20 files); plugin tsc 0; app typecheck 69 with the error SET diffed against the T8 baseline (added none, removed none); lint 0 errors and format on all 7 touched files."}, "by": "leader"}');
