INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5832, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-10-02T17:08:32.735Z', '{"task_id": "task-c90d30c62b", "title": "PR #30 base collision: feat/trajectory-plugin has 11 unpushed commits on lane t-f3ba82ac9c overlapping 10 files with this PR", "changes": {"status": "pending", "progress": 0, "assignee": "owner", "note": "2026-10-02 VERIFICATION UPDATE — the collision is now REAL AND PUSHED. Leader 23666e3d of t-f3ba82ac9c reported the 11-commit leg resolved; I verified all four claims from MY OWN worktree by fetch, without touching theirs. VERIFIED TRUE: origin/feat/trajectory-plugin 870b21495 -> b7c5b81e0; a8988a6a7 is an ancestor of b7c5b81e0; 870b21495..b7c5b81e0 is 17 commits, not the 11 originally recorded (their chain includes T4-B/T8/T9); and a8988a6a7 is already reachable from origin/feat/freebuff-plugin (2cba6a511), so their \"already reachable via freebuff-plugin\" claim also holds.\n\nTHE COLLISION MATERIALIZED AS REAL CONFLICTS\nGitHub''s own flag has flipped: mergeable=UNKNOWN, mergeState=UNKNOWN (it is recomputing after the base moved). The authoritative local answer is git merge-tree --write-tree, read-only, no working-tree change: FIVE real content conflicts — client/ledger-screen.tsx, client/ledger-screen.test.tsx, client/trajectory-panel.tsx, client/use-trajectory-delta.ts, shared/dsh/layout.ts. My earlier prediction, recorded before it happened, was that PR #30 would keep reading MERGEABLE until the remote base moved and would then conflict substantively rather than mechanically. That prediction held.\n\nOVERLAP RE-CONFIRMED, AND ONE OF MY OWN COUNTS WAS STALE\nLocale-independent set intersection (my earlier comm run emitted sort-order warnings, so I did not trust it): base moves 42 files, my PR moves 26, overlap is EXACTLY the same 10 files already recorded — ledger-screen.tsx, ledger-screen.test.tsx, trajectory-panel.tsx, use-trajectory-delta.ts, node-store.ts, node-store.test.ts, recorder.test.ts, store.ts, shared/dsh/layout.ts, shared/trajectory.ts. The overlap list is therefore confirmed twice by independent methods. CORRECTION TO MY OWN RECORD: I previously reported \"base-only 20, mine-only 16\". mine-only 16 is unchanged, but base-only is now 32, because the base moved 17 commits rather than the 11 I measured. The 20 figure is stale and should not be cited.\n\nTHE DANGEROUS PART IS NOT THE FIVE CONFLICTS, IT IS THE FIVE THAT MERGE CLEANLY\nTen files overlap; five conflict textually and five do not. The clean five are node-store.ts, node-store.test.ts, recorder.test.ts, store.ts and shared/trajectory.ts — and those are precisely the files carrying my direction contract, my tail-first page SQL and my beforeSeq input. A clean textual merge there means git found no overlapping hunks, NOT that the result is coherent: it is entirely possible to produce a store that accepts a required direction option while one side''s rewrite of the paging SQL no longer honours it, or a beforeSeq contract that three modules consume with a different bound than the one the merged node-store applies. That is the \"looks right and behaves wrong\" failure mode, and it will not announce itself in review or in CI. Treat the five clean merges as requiring the same reading as the five conflicts.\n\nQUESTIONS PUT TO LEADER 23666e3d, TO GIVE THE OWNER BOTH INTENTS BEFORE DECIDING\nThey offered leader-to-leader input on file ownership, merge order and which side owns the overlapping trajectory files, and I took them up on it — for intent only, not for the decision, which is the owner''s. (1) Did their lane implement paging independently? Their subject \"surface newest rows to the ledger DOM and search\" addresses the same defect as my F1 tail-first fix, but if they solved newest-first a different way then my required direction option may be redundant or semantically contradictory to theirs. (2) Did they implement their own virtualization? S3''s calibrated getItemLayout and windowing are in ledger-screen.tsx, the single most conflicted file. (3) For shared/dsh/layout.ts, does their \"derived llm-round + system rows, recorder pairing fixes\" reorganise the groups structure my O(steps squared) fix indexes into? If the structure changed shape, my map-based lookup may have been aimed at a structure that no longer exists. Also asked them to confirm whether task-49cd13d78d is now corrected, since the collector recorded it stranded at running/30% during the window they now describe as an RPC blip.\n\nSTILL NOT DECIDED HERE, AND STILL OWNER''S\nNo rebase, no merge, no force-push, no writes into either lane''s worktree, no PR edits. The decision now has better inputs than it did: the conflict set is known and small, the base is pushed and current, the counterpart leader is reachable, and the five clean merges are flagged as the real risk rather than the five conflicts."}, "by": "owner"}');
