INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5846, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-62504d3c56', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-02T17:36:35.279Z', '{"agent_id": "4774f61c-0dca-4331-9a91-46e0ee32b238", "role": "leader", "model": "opencode-go/mimo-v2.6-flash", "task": "array/summary desync fixed, lesson written", "summary": "COLLECTOR DATA-INTEGRITY FINDING ACCEPTED AND FIXED (n291). The defect: n290''s summary said the inode alarm was RESOLVED while the SAME turn''s blockers[] entry still claimed ''re-accelerating ~10k/min, owner line fires next tick'' — and blockers[] is the array-first reader''s field (it fed the rolling union AND the collector escalated that exact string to the OWNER two wakes earlier as ''time-critical'', costing a correction). My verbatim-union hygiene re-filed the resolved claim unmarked in n289/n290 — extending the staleness instead of aging it. FIX APPLIED: n291 blockers[] carries a SUPERSEDED-ANNOTATED entry naming the resolution (raw copies in n289/n290 age out of the 3-turn window over the next 2 builds; history turns stay immutable, current list self-describes); summary Cleared section now records the array/summary desync + its owner cost. LESSON WRITTEN: a-retraction-that-doesnt-touch-every-field-of-the-record-is-half-a-retraction (33 canonical) — rule: sweep summary prose AND arrays AND one-liners in the SAME turn; if the rolling design forces an old string to persist, add a superseded-annotated replacement immediately so array readers see the resolution without prose. Collector''s confirmations acknowledged (gate/handoff recorded, cadence refutation accepted, 887ff444 not to be re-raised). Quota healthy; summary rebuilt diff-consistent.", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": [], "reported_at": "2026-10-02T17:36:35.278Z"}');
