INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(5864, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-10-02T17:53:07.673Z', '{"task_id": "task-d115d5618d", "title": "S5 (dsh Phase 5, f479c60b6d + fc4df896a0 + e27dba8457): data-plane perf — incremental fold, search-identity + 3s throttle, per-record content memo, with scale-ratio tests", "changes": {"status": "pending", "progress": 70, "assignee": "owner", "note": "2026-10-02 CORRECTION — this task was recorded done/100% and that is wrong. Owner asked whether the delivery was limited; checking rather than answering from memory, I found PART (3) NEVER SHIPPED. VERIFIED AGAINST THE ACTUAL PR DIFF (870b21495..08339ff37), NOT PROSE: (1) INCREMENTAL FOLD and (2) SEARCH IDENTITY PLUS THROTTLE both shipped — commits 6bcc1e4a6 \"kill the quadratic group lookup in the fold, and hold a ceiling\" and 952fbae29 \"throttle the search index off the live query path\". (3) PER-RECORD CONTENT MEMO DID NOT. The task detail located the work in TrajectoryCellRow at client/ledger-cells.tsx:177, and ledger-cells.tsx does not appear in this PR''s changed files at all; a scan of every cell, text, record, timeline and layout file in the diff returns zero useMemo additions. The base already carries unrelated useMemo in ledger-cells.tsx for styles and toolStats, which is pre-existing and is not the per-field content memo dsh''s RecordPresentation (TrajectoryTable.tsx:975-1006) provides. So the task that motivates part (3) still stands: a text delta reparses the whole record rather than one field. I ALSO NOTE THAT PART (1) IS INCOMPLETE IN A WEAKER SENSE: the commit message says \"hold a ceiling\", which is the measurement harness for the ratio assertions, and the underlying whole-buffer refold in the delta hook was named in the detail as \"the first thing to stop\". No commit in this PR replaces eventsToFoldRows'' whole-buffer refold with an incremental apply, so the O(C log C) contribution snapshot and its key-to-position index from dsh f479c60b6d plus fc4df896a0 were never ported — the memo and the incremental apply are the same underlying fix (preserve cell identity so indexTurn can short-circuit) and the single remaining task task-24a2ae9fa4 already names that as its subject. So part (3) was not merely omitted; it is the work task-24a2ae9fa4 exists to do. WHAT DID SHIP, for the record: tail-first paging with a beforeSeq reverse cursor and a page-derived headSeq, forward drain from the cursor, tail-follow off the render path with no blind re-arm, position-free chrome keys, stable row projection reuse, calibrated row heights with getItemLayout, a load-older control with viewport preservation across prepend, the quadratic group-lookup fix, the off-append search throttle, a plugin CI workflow, and the test-hardening commits including the first run of the real VirtualizedList and the per-agent cursor invariant. 181 tests across 22 files pass at head, plugin typecheck clean, lint and format clean. NOT SET TO DISPATCHABLE ON PURPOSE: assignee moved to owner and progress left short of done even though the gate field is immutable at ready. Part (3) is real remaining work, but the branch is contested — task-c90d30c62b records five content conflicts against a moved base — so putting a dev onto fix/trajectory-render-list now would have them write into a tree with unresolved conflicts and possibly into work another lane is entitled to claim. The gate should be the owner''s, alongside the PR #30 reconcile decision."}, "by": "owner"}');
