INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6007, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-03T01:23:06.070Z', '{"agent_id": "556e5438-ddf9-403b-b71f-21eee8e2b5d6", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "T10 max-context defaults: base fix + design note before code", "summary": "T10 turn 1 — diagnosed and designed, no code yet.\n\nSETUP DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED: my worktree branch feat/t10-max-context-defaults was created off the STALE LOCAL feat/freebuff-plugin (cc2d81cde, 105 commits behind origin/feat/freebuff-plugin=6569504ae), so none of the max-context files existed in the worktree. Branch had zero own commits and a clean tree, so I reset --hard onto origin/feat/freebuff-plugin (lossless, nothing of mine to lose). All T10 files now present. Leader should create future worktrees off the REMOTE ref.\n\nDESIGN NOTE (owner-visible, addresses the brief''s round-trip flag):\n\n1. Ambiguity flag (brief asked me to raise it): \"default is K not M\" read as bare-number=K (leader''s reading) vs placeholder-only. I implement bare=K. Consequence to state plainly: a user who previously typed a bare token count (\"128000\") now gets 128,000,000. No stored config is affected (config holds a number, not text), only newly typed text; preview line + placeholder self-correct. Reverting item 2 is a 3-line isolated revert.\n\n2. Round-trip resolution (the real conflict): under bare=K, format can never emit a bare number, because every bare number re-reads as K. Non-thousand-multiples (131072, 32768 — realistic powers of two) had no exact text. Options weighed: (a) new raw-token unit = new parse surface + confusion; (b) round to nearest expressible = silently changes a stored ceiling (rejected, lies); (c) accept a FRACTION only with an explicit suffix. Chose (c). Provably sufficient: any integer/1000 has <=3 decimals, so a 3-decimal cap never rejects text format can emit. Bare fractions (\"1.5\") stay invalid — bare already means K.\n\n3. Math.round on the product is mandatory, measured not assumed: without it ~1.3% of values drift (1001 -> \"1.001 K\" -> 1000.9999999999999). With <=3 decimals the error is <0.5 tokens, so rounding is lossless for anything format emits. Brute-forced 650k values (1..300k, powers of two, randoms to 1e15): 0 round-trip mismatches.\n\n4. Empty stays \"No limit\"; the 280 K placeholder is a HINT ONLY and never seeds a value (owner''s T7-F constraint held).\n\n5. No protocol/config change. No docs change — docs/custom-providers.md documents the config NUMBER, not the input grammar; the grammar stays in code comments per AGENTS.md doc rules.\n\nInvalid-hint i18n strings stay unchanged in all 9 locales: the brief states they remain accurate (\"Enter a number, optionally followed by K or M\") and editing them would mean authoring 8 translations I cannot verify. Only the placeholder changes, and it is a locale-independent numeric example.\n\nBaseline: 33 tests green in the 2 target files (symlinked node_modules from same-commit worktree /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk @ 6569504ae — identical commit, added to .git/info/exclude so it cannot be committed).", "status": "partial", "pr": "", "artifacts": [], "reported_at": "2026-10-03T01:23:06.069Z"}');
