INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6018, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-03T01:27:29.191Z', '{"agent_id": "2eb265f4-6ec0-49f5-97f4-52a1a4b161df", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "T10 max-context defaults — 280 K placeholder, bare number means K, exact round-trip", "summary": "T10 COMPLETE — commit b173916c0 on feat/t10-max-context-defaults (12 files, +139/-38), clean tree, no PR.\n\nDELIVERED: (1) placeholder \"100 M\"->\"280 K\" in all 9 locales (numeric example, no translation invented). (2) Bare number parses as K (\"280\"->280000); M explicit-only (\"2 M\"); DEFAULT_SUFFIX documents it. (3) Round-trip invariant PRESERVED and proven: format always spells the unit out (a bare number reads back as K and would multiply a stored cap by 1000), and non-whole-thousand counts keep exact text via a fraction allowed only beside an explicit unit (131072 -> \"131.072 K\"). math.round required, measured: \"131.072\"*1000 lands under 131072 in binary float. Brute-forced 1..300000 + powers of two + randoms to 1e15: 0 mismatches; a permanent sweep test (1..50000 + 2^0..2^30) guards it.\nCONSTRAINTS HELD: empty still \"No limit\", placeholder hint-only — new test asserts empty previews \"No limit\" with \"280 K\" placeholder showing, so nobody later seeds a 280K cap (T7-F). Daemon contract (number, explicit null) untouched; server tests use config numbers, not typed text, so no collateral.\nDELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED: invalid-hint strings in 9 locales (brief says they stay accurate; editing means 8 unverifiable translations), and provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx (verified it only mounts the field) — announced as out of scope, so T11 has one less shared file.\n\nGATES: target tests 33->40 green (post-format and post-commit). oxlint 0/0. oxfmt stable. typecheck 82 with my change = 82 on pristine base, same environment: ZERO new errors; the one hit in my file is the pre-existing react-dom/client import at original line 13.\n\nTWO PRE-EXISTING FAILURES on origin/feat/freebuff-plugin, NOT MINE, both redden merged CI: (a) i18n resources.test.ts key-parity fails on BASE — missing settings.providers.models.failedToSave + settings.sections.* in non-English locales (proved by stashing my i18n edits; no maxContext key in the diff); (b) pnpm-workspace.yaml fails format:check repo-wide. Please route both.\n\nENV DISCLOSURE: node_modules absent here, so symlinked from /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk — verified SAME commit (6569504ae) before linking; symlinks in .git/info/exclude so uncommittable, tree clean. Hence typecheck 82 not the documented 69 (51 are TS7016/TS2307 from the shared install). Full-green typecheck needs a real install or CI — flagged, not claimed.\n\nOwner-callable ambiguity from the accepted note stands: bare=K means typing a bare token count (\"128000\") now yields 128,000,000. No stored config affected (number, not text), preview line shows the parsed count at once, and reverting item 2 is a 3-line isolated change if the owner meant placeholder-only.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["b173916c0 feat(settings): max-context field defaults to 280 K, bare number means K", "packages/app/src/components/provider-max-context.ts (bare=K parse, exact format)", "packages/app/src/components/provider-max-context.test.ts (40 tests incl. round-trip sweep)", "packages/app/src/components/provider-max-context-field.test.tsx (280 K placeholder, bare-280 save)"], "reported_at": "2026-10-03T01:27:29.190Z"}');
