INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6041, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-03T01:49:11.760Z', '{"agent_id": "2eb265f4-6ec0-49f5-97f4-52a1a4b161df", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "T11 per-sub-provider model prefix — config, store semantics, row resolution, sheet sections, i18n, docs", "summary": "T11 COMPLETE — 5 commits cad65e114..3fef821e7 on feat/t11-subprovider-prefix, stacked on T10''s b173916c0 as instructed (T10''s commit preserved, nothing rebased or reset). Clean tree, no PR.\n\nAll 5 requirements met. Config: additive optional modelPrefixes; patch side nullable per key so one tag clears without touching siblings; keys uncapped and uncharset-restricted (measured: live catalog has ''wafer.ai''). Store: nulls are dropped BEFORE either schema sees them — deepMerge assigns null rather than deleting, so a null left in the map would have failed ProviderOverrideSchema on the way to disk and MutableDaemonConfigSchema on the way back, rejecting the WHOLE patch. That was the highest-risk item and both merge paths are covered by tests (persisted pure fn + store→disk→reload). Rendering: rows resolve per-sub-provider with provider-wide fallback, sub-provider read from metadata.providerId behind a typeof check, never inferred from the model id. Sheet: provider-wide section KEPT plus one section per served sub-provider, enumerated from served (not search-filtered) models, deduped+sorted, saving state keyed per sub-provider. Composer fallback keeps the provider-wide tag because its options carry no metadata.\n\nGATES: app 231/231 (13 files incl. every consumer of the changed modules), server store 50/50, protocol 709/709 incl. the ws-outbound AOT validator. Lint 0/0. Typecheck: verified ZERO new errors — one real TS2345 my change introduced (composer fallback passing tags where a string was expected) was caught and fixed; the only file of mine in the remaining error list is T10''s provider-max-context-field.test.tsx carrying its known pre-existing react-dom/client TS7016.\n\nMY OWN MISTAKES, OWNED: (1) committed 90ddca9e3 after leaving an unused emptyPrefixTags helper that lint caught — fixed immediately in its own commit; (2) typecheck + lint now run as separate commands, because piping them through tail masked a non-zero exit and I committed past a lint error once.\n\nENV DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED — worth propagating to every worker: my node_modules was symlinked to the same-commit worktree /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk, and @getpaseo/* resolved THROUGH it, so packages/server silently loaded THAT worktree''s protocol package. My modelPrefixes field was stripped by a stale schema and a correct merge test failed for the wrong reason. Fixed by rebuilding each packages/*/node_modules as a real dir whose @getpaseo scope points at MY packages (also had to include dot-entries like .bin, link packages/highlight|relay|plugin, and supply undeclared jiti). If another worker''s cross-package test result looks impossible, check this before believing it.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["cad65e114 feat(config): per-sub-provider modelPrefixes map with key-level delete", "e512965fd feat(settings): resolve each model row''s tag from its sub-provider", "90ddca9e3 refactor(settings): drop the unused emptyPrefixTags helper", "3e7dd8bfe feat(settings): per-sub-provider prefix field patch and addressable fields", "3fef821e7 feat(settings): one model tag section per served sub-provider"], "reported_at": "2026-10-03T01:49:11.759Z"}');
