INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6117, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-10-03T05:05:28.110Z', '{"task_id": "task-b5e2cac248", "title": "T12: ctx cap REAL ENFORCEMENT — harness-level limit injection (owner directive 2026-10-03)", "changes": {"status": "running", "progress": 70, "note": "PHASE A COMPLETE — design note posted, awaiting owner approval. NO code written, no commits. Branch feat/t12-ctx-enforcement off f199f79bb. Note at T12-ctx-enforcement-DESIGN-NOTE.md (untracked).\n\nVERDICTS: opencode ENFORCEABLE natively (config provider.<id>.models.<m>.limit.context via the ALREADY-WIRED decorateServerEnv seam at bridge.ts:97; confirmed in Paseo''s pinned SDK 1.18.23 types.gen.d.ts:905/1323/2616; opencode deep-merges OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT LAST so injected keys win; binary decompile shows it auto-compacts at limit.context - maxOutputTokens). claude ENFORCEABLE (CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW env or --autocompact flag; extraArgs already forwards arbitrary flags so no new plumbing; range 100k-1M, can only lower, compaction not refusal; CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS is a TRAP - only applies to unrecognised model ids). omp ONLY via config file (--config overlay / models.yml modelOverrides), UNPROVEN whether it reaches the compaction path; its catalog contextWindow is read then DISCARDED by map-omp-model.ts:40-54. acp NOT ENFORCEABLE - full ClientRequest union has no context channel; update.size proven = total window, used = fill, from upstream docs.\n\nRECOMMENDED SEMANTICS: harness-native compaction injection per harness. Rejected Paseo-refuses-new-turns (unusable mid-task, no recovery, doesn''t reduce an over-cap context, and would be the only option for acp) and rejected prompt truncation (silently drops user content). METER TRUTH: saturating is ALREADY done at context-window-meter.tsx:49; the gap is composer/index.tsx:273 feeding raw runtime — set displayMax = min(runtime, cap) there.\n\nTWO SPEC CORRECTIONS: (1) the composer reads agent.lastUsage.contextWindowMaxTokens, not \"a raw runtime value in the adapter\" as framed - same conclusion, imprecise mechanism; (2) for omp the capped number has no harness-side counterpart at all, so the cap file''s overclaiming comment is wrong for a second reason.\n\nOWNER DECISIONS NEEDED: (a) is SOFT/compaction enforcement acceptable as the answer, given a hard ceiling is impossible for claude+acp? (b) acp: visible \"not enforced\" affordance vs omit the field? (c) omp --config live probe now or defer omp?"}, "by": "leader"}');
