INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6141, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-03T05:21:53.121Z', '{"agent_id": "ab6fbd8f-1c61-4d51-9332-6aebeae46760", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "T13 group sheet model list per sub-provider below each prefix setting — code half delivered, 3 commits, all gates green", "summary": "T13 CODE HALF COMPLETE — 3 commits d3e62e1e6 / 768370583 / d67e1cdb2 on feat/t13-subprovider-model-groups (base 6927d72ac). Tree clean, no PR, app+docs only (verified: no server/protocol/i18n delta).\n\nDELIVERED: each served sub-provider''s models render inside that sub-provider''s group, under the \"Model tag · <sub>\" field the tag decorates. Flat Discovered list gone. [Context limit][Model tag][Model tag·sub + rows]xN[remainder][Custom].\n\nREMAINDER (req 1''s open choice): served models with no metadata.providerId render LAST under the EXISTING models.discovered header → ZERO new i18n keys, zero translation risk, no dead key (that key had exactly one consumer, the header I replaced). Consequence: a provider with no sub-providers is pixel-identical to today. Rejected putting them under the provider-wide field (would show a strict subset of the rows modelPrefix actually governs) and a \"Model tag·other\" field (needs a config key = protocol+server work).\n\nSEARCH (req 2): sections from UNFILTERED served models, rows from FILTERED — T11''s \"search must not make a configured tag unreachable\" preserved, not reversed. An emptied group keeps its field, shows no card, drops its count (a \"0\" would claim the sub serves nothing). Req 3 intact: per-sub save state and provider-wide fallback untouched; testIDs prefixed provider-sheet-model-row-* / provider-model-sub-section-<sub> / provider-model-remainder-section, deliberately NOT model-row-* which model-browser.tsx:799 owns (testIDs are document-wide).\n\nENV TRAP WAS REAL: sibling''s protocol dist has 0 hits for modelPrefixes (built 00:29 vs T11 commits 01:20-01:49). Repointed @getpaseo at MY packages and rebuilt protocol/highlight/relay/client; mine now shows 2+16 hits. Trusting the sibling would have silently erased T11''s field from types.\n\nGATES: 293/293 (18 files; mine 31 pure + 7 component); oxlint 0/0 scoped; format:check PASS 4803; typecheck 163 with IDENTICAL normalized error set to baseline — zero new. Tests falsified by 4 mutations, all caught: sections-from-filtered, rows-collapsed-to-first-group, remainder-always-rendered, and group-key-from-model-id-instead-of-metadata (the exact error T11''s note warned about). Two of my own draft assertions were wrong; I fixed the tests, not the code.\n\nLINT NOTE: root `npm run lint` is repo-wide RED at 10 errors in files I never opened (pre-existing debt). Mine is 0/0.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": ["d3e62e1e6 feat(settings): pair sub-provider tag fields with the model rows under them", "768370583 feat(settings): list each sub-provider''s models under its own tag field", "d67e1cdb2 docs(custom-providers): say the sheet groups rows under each tag field", "provider-model-prefix.ts buildSubProviderModelSections + SubProviderModelSection", "provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx ProviderSubModelGroup + remainder section + probeable testIDs", "provider-diagnostic-model-groups.test.tsx (7 tests)", "provider-model-prefix.test.ts 20 -> 31 tests"], "reported_at": "2026-10-03T05:21:53.121Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6142, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'decision_recorded', '2026-10-03T05:21:53.122Z', '{"decision_id": "d-72e6179469", "source": "leader", "irreversible": false}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6143, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'task_updated', '2026-10-03T05:25:06.809Z', '{"task_id": "task-b5e2cac248", "title": "T12: ctx cap REAL ENFORCEMENT — harness-level limit injection (owner directive 2026-10-03)", "changes": {"status": "done", "progress": 100, "note": "PHASE B COMPLETE — 3 commits on feat/t12-ctx-enforcement: f6a7f797f (meter displayMax=min(runtime,cap)), cf261120b (claude autocompact + 100k floor), 5ad8fea6c (opencode limit.context injection + registry single-source wiring). 19 files +1008/-18. No PR, no deploy.\n\nENFORCEMENT NOW REAL for opencode + claude:\n• opencode: injects provider.<id>.models.<m>.limit.context via the already-wired decorateServerEnv seam. Only runtime-catalog models capped (no phantom entries). Solved the ordering problem the obvious implementation misses: caps are written at SPAWN but models are learned AFTER, so each generation records a cap fingerprint and the agent requests a fresh generation when the live one lacks them — otherwise caps learned post-spawn sit inert.\n• claude: extraArgs.autocompact with the 100k floor.\n• meter: displayMax = min(runtimeReported, cap), cap via useDaemonConfig + config.providers[agent.provider].maxContextTokens (T7 precedent). Meter already saturated so no meter change.\n\nONE SOURCE: resolveProviderContextCap() is now the single reader of the configured value, used by BOTH the registry mapper (what Paseo advertises) and the clients (what the harness enforces), wired via ProviderClientFactoryOptions.maxContextTokens + AgentSessionConfig.maxContextTokens + claude assertConfig.\n\nGATES: 220/220 opencode+registry+cap tests; claude options 11/11; app context-window 11/11; lint 0/0 on 14 files; format:check repo-wide CLEAN (4808 files); typecheck 19768 = baseline EXACTLY, zero new (verified by stripping line numbers and diffing the full error multiset — only diff is one pre-existing error whose text differs by property order inside its type printout).\n\nMY MISTAKES, OWNED: (1) added getCurrentContextCapsKey to OpenCodeServerManagerLike but did not update TestOpenCodeHarness -> +67 TS errors in one shot; caught by before/after measurement, not assumed. (2) used `it` in a test file importing only describe/expect/test -> TS2593. (3) omitted required providerOptions on OpenCodeAgentConfig in 3 new tests. (4) 3 oxlint no-useless-fallback-in-spread errors in my own context-cap.ts.\n\nENV DEFECTS affecting gates (PRE-EXISTING, not mine, both subagents proved by stash): `npx vitest run src/server/agent/providers/claude` exits 1 because that scope includes *.real.e2e.test.ts needing OPENROUTER_API_KEY and spawning real agents — use --exclude \"**/*.e2e.test.ts\" (repo convention, as in npm run test:unit); with exclusion 30 files/410 tests pass. packages/app composer scope has 6 suites that fail to COLLECT on unbuilt @getpaseo/plugin (same root cause as the 19768 typecheck errors) — needs npm run build:client.\n\nCAUGHT BY SUBAGENTS, both corrections to my design note: (a) claude''s [100k,1M] range is enforced by REJECTION (argParser throws), not flooring — so without the clamp a 50k cap would CRASH the agent at startup, making the floor load-bearing, not cosmetic; >1M also throws, so caps above 1M emit nothing rather than being clamped down. (b) SDK forwards extraArgs keys VERBATIM, not kebab-cased.\n\nDEFERRED per leader (untouched): acp affordance, omp --config probe. Note text §4/§8 left as-is but §3''s \"floored at 100k\" is now superseded by (a).\n\nNOT RUNTIME-VERIFIED: no live agent was driven to observe compaction actually firing. QC r28 must prove that; claude cannot test sub-100k."}, "by": "leader"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6144, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'turn_reported', '2026-10-03T05:25:16.068Z', '{"n": 325, "status": "idle", "summary": "PHASE B COMPLETE — 3 commits on feat/t12-ctx-enforcement, 19 files +1008/-18. No PR, no deploy (leader batches after QC "}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6145, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-f3ba82ac9c', 'worker_reported', '2026-10-03T05:25:16.069Z', '{"agent_id": "236a054c-6d31-403c-8909-0d2d91da4864", "role": "dev", "model": "opencode-go/space-bunny-free", "task": "T12 Phase B: ctx cap real enforcement — opencode limit.context injection, claude autocompact floor, meter displayMax", "summary": "PHASE B COMPLETE — 3 commits on feat/t12-ctx-enforcement, 19 files +1008/-18. No PR, no deploy (leader batches after QC r28).\n\nf6a7f797f meter | cf261120b claude | 5ad8fea6c opencode + registry wiring.\n\nENFORCEMENT IS NOW REAL for the two harnesses that can be enforced:\n• opencode — injects provider.<id>.models.<m>.limit.context through the ALREADY-WIRED decorateServerEnv seam (no new plumbing). Only models seen in the runtime catalog are capped, so no phantom provider.models entry is invented.\n• claude — extraArgs.autocompact with the 100k floor.\n• meter — displayMax = min(runtimeReported, cap), cap read via useDaemonConfig + config.providers[agent.provider].maxContextTokens (the T7 precedent). Meter already saturated, so no meter change was needed.\n\nONE SOURCE OF TRUTH, as instructed: resolveProviderContextCap() is now the single reader of the configured value, used by BOTH the registry mapper (what Paseo advertises) and the provider clients (what the harness enforces), threaded via ProviderClientFactoryOptions.maxContextTokens → AgentSessionConfig.maxContextTokens → claude assertConfig. No second resolver.\n\nTHE NON-OBVIOUS PROBLEM I SOLVED: caps are written into config at SPAWN, but the model list is only learned from the catalog AFTERWARD — so the obvious implementation silently leaves caps inert until something else restarts OpenCode. Each server generation now records a cap fingerprint and the agent requests a fresh generation when the live one lacks the desired caps. Covered by a test asserting a \"new\" acquisition, plus the reuse case.\n\nGATES: opencode+registry+cap 220/220; claude options 11/11; app context-window 11/11; lint 0/0 on 14 files; format:check repo-wide CLEAN (4808 files); typecheck 19768 = baseline EXACTLY. I verified zero-new properly: stripped line numbers and diffed the entire error multiset, since my inserted tests shifted lines and a naive comm produced 43 phantom \"new\" errors. The only real diff is one pre-existing error whose message differs by property order inside its type printout.\n\nMY MISTAKES, OWNED: (1) I added getCurrentContextCapsKey to OpenCodeServerManagerLike and did not update TestOpenCodeHarness — +67 TS errors at once, caught by measuring rather than assuming. (2) used `it` in a file importing only describe/expect/test. (3) omitted required providerOptions on OpenCodeAgentConfig in 3 new tests. (4) 3 oxlint no-useless-fallback-in-spread in my own context-cap.ts.\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO MY OWN DESIGN NOTE, caught by subagents inspecting the binary: (a) claude''s [100k,1M] range is enforced by REJECTION — the argParser throws — so the floor is load-bearing, not cosmetic: without the clamp a 50k cap would CRASH the agent at startup, and a >1M cap also throws, so it emits nothing rather than clamping down. (b) the SDK forwards extraArgs keys verbatim, not kebab-cased.\n\nENV DEFECTS blocking naive gate commands (pre-existing, both proved by stash): the claude vitest scope includes *.real.e2e.test.ts that need OPENROUTER_API_KEY and spawn real agents — use --exclude \"**/*.e2e.test.ts\" (repo convention); with it 30 files/410 tests pass. 6 packages/app composer suites fail to COLLECT on unbuilt @getpaseo/plugin — needs npm run build:client.\n\nDEFERRED per your instruction, untouched: acp affordance, omp --config probe. Note §4/§8 unchanged, but §3''s \"floored at 100k\" is superseded by (a).\n\nNOT RUNTIME-VERIFIED — the honest gap: I never drove a live agent to watch compaction actually fire. Everything above is source- and decompile-derived plus unit tests. QC r28 must prove the effect, on opencode, since claude cannot express a sub-100k cap.", "status": "done", "pr": "", "artifacts": [], "reported_at": "2026-10-03T05:25:16.069Z"}');
INSERT INTO orch_events(id, project_id, track_id, type, ts, payload) VALUES(6146, 'p-b5bd663dcf', 't-a124729a8a', 'task_updated', '2026-10-03T05:26:02.977Z', '{"task_id": "task-c90d30c62b", "title": "PR #30 base collision: feat/trajectory-plugin has 11 unpushed commits on lane t-f3ba82ac9c overlapping 10 files with this PR", "changes": {"status": "pending", "progress": 0, "assignee": "owner", "note": "2026-10-03 RESOLUTION KNOWLEDGE — written here deliberately, because it existed only in one session''s prose and the collector correctly flagged that as a one-session-drop loss. Everything below is worked out and does NOT need redoing. Tree is clean at 08339ff37, backup ref backup/render-list-08339ff37 exists, PR #30 untouched, nothing deployed.\n\nSTATE: GitHub now reports PR #30 mergeable=CONFLICTING mergeState=DIRTY, matching the merge-tree prediction made before it happened.\n\nTHE COLLECTOR''S base-collision HYPOTHESIS IS RULED OUT. It proposed that a second leader editing the same checkout caused both the base divergence and the duplicated FoldState. Tested cheaply against committed objects: each committed ledger-screen.tsx declares FoldState exactly ONCE (mine at :37, base at :33, common ancestor 870b21495 at :26); base b7c5b81e0 is internally consistent with 9 closedTurns/ALL_OPEN refs and 0 openTurns refs; and b7c5b81e0 is a published commit contained on ci-freebuff-baseline, env/p0-sdk-integration, feat/t10, feat/t11 and feat/t12. So the base is a clean committed state and the duplication was produced by git''s merge, not a same-tree collision. Dead end. INCIDENTAL CORRECTION: env/p0-sdk-integration DOES exist locally and contains b7c5b81e0 — I earlier recorded it as absent from this remote, which was wrong, and it is the likely PROD integration branch.\n\nTHE DECISION IS ONE PRODUCT CALL, NOT TWO. n34 described it as two questions. It is one. Keying is FORCED, not chosen: S4 prepends older history, turn numbers renumber on prepend, and the base keys closedTurns by turn.turn, so a collapsed turn''s state would migrate to whichever turn slid into its slot. Identity keying is required. The only genuine product call is the DEFAULT presentation, and it has an asymmetry that should settle it: PROD ALREADY SHIPS ALL-OPEN, while PR #30 silently flips it to all-folded. Adopting all-open therefore changes no shipped behaviour AND fixes a real defect in my lane, which is that an open-set seeded at mount leaves every turn arriving afterwards collapsed. Recommendation: all-open, recorded in the PR description so the owner is not surprised at test time. Note S4''s load-older control at the top of the ledger was designed for the folded presentation, so the two are coupled and a switch to all-open may want the control reviewed.\n\nEXACT PER-HUNK RESOLUTIONS, all worked out. layout.ts hunk 1: keep BOTH — the base''s Map<number | null, TurnBucket> for the unnumbered preamble bucket plus my groupIndex widened to Map<number | null, Map<string, LaidGroup>>; git''s auto-merge had already fused groupIndex.set into their bucket helper, which confirms the union. layout.ts hunk 2: keep my groupFor widened to (turn: number | null, ...) and their pushMessage signature. layout.ts hunk 3: TAKE THE BASE SIDE AND DELETE MY BLOCK — they independently found the same recordId collision and fixed it better, assistant nul row.seq, with measured evidence (QC r20 turn-id reuse across sessions, 95 assistant rows sharing 34 ids) and both downstream symptoms named (virtualizer dedupe drops the later row, search index overwrites the earlier). My turnId+step+seq suffix was redundant. Their block also carries mergedIdentity and deltaFields that their streaming work requires. use-trajectory-delta.ts: PURELY ADDITIVE, keep both declarations — my olderInFlight load-older lock and their idle-poll timer plus IDLE_MS, which fixes a real bug where an already-open panel never learned about new events (QC r19, 24 chunks seq 9847-9986, zero rows rendered). trajectory-panel.tsx: PURELY ADDITIVE, keep both prop sets. ledger-screen.test.tsx hunk 1: take base (their View mock serializes style so the flex contract is assertable). Hunk 2: union, my listProbe plus their three imports. Hunk 3: union — keep their APPENDED_ROW, ROWS_WITH_APPENDED_TURN and TURN_NUMBERS_WITH_APPENDED, and merge render/renderRows to accept compact, extraTurn, turnNumbers (null meaning derive from row order), hasOlderHistory, loadingOlder, onLoadOlder and onClose. Hunk 4: union both prop sets. ledger-screen.tsx, all 13 hunks: migrate FoldState from {openTurns, openSteps} to {closedTurns, closedSteps}, both keyed by IDENTITY; keep turnKeyOf, KeyedTurn, stepIdentity, turnKeys, allStepKeys, allCollapsed, my calibrated TURN_HEADER_HEIGHT 22 / STEP_HEADER_HEIGHT 17 / TURN_RULE_HEIGHT 10 over their uncalibrated 28 and 10, my getItemLayout, my anchorRef and scrollOffsetRef, my followRef (S2 moved follow off the render path, so their useState follow is deliberately NOT adopted), my identity-based row keys, and adopt their Setup-bucket numbering so the unnumbered preamble does not push Turn 1 down. allOpen becomes the ALL_OPEN constant; everythingCollapsed becomes allCollapsed(keyedTurns); toggleTurn and toggleStep flip membership in closedTurns/closedSteps; allTurnsOpen and allStepsOpen test absence from the closed sets; toggleAllTurns and toggleAllSteps move between ALL_OPEN and everythingCollapsed. That resolution WAS completed and verified structurally — one declaration each of FoldState, KeyedTurn, turnKeyOf, stepIdentity, ALL_OPEN, allCollapsed, zero stale openTurns/openSteps/INITIAL_FOLD refs — and then I destroyed it myself with an abort-and-re-merge cycle while chasing a reproducibility question. The four other files'' resolutions were lost in that same cycle. All of it is recoverable from the hunks above in one pass.\n\nTWO PROCESS LESSONS, both mine. First, I ran git add on files that still contained conflict markers. That clears git''s conflict flag while KEEPING the marker content, so git reported zero conflicted files and I nearly took that as success; plugin typecheck caught it with 29 TS1185 errors. Never trust a conflict count as proof of resolution — grep for markers and typecheck. Second, the same night, a comm run emitted sort-order warnings and still printed a plausible overlap count, and my own resolver script threw IndexError while leaving a file in a state I misread. Three separate tools produced green-looking output that was false. The duplicated FoldState is a fourth: git produced it legitimately by landing base''s declaration in a region my branch never touched while the conflicted region''s copy was resolved separately.\n\nSTILL OWED and not done: commit the resolved merge; review the five CLEAN merges semantically, especially node-store.ts, store.ts and shared/trajectory.ts where a clean merge can leave a required direction option that the merged paging SQL no longer honours; rerun the 181 tests plus typecheck, lint and format; then the PROD deploy, which is still blocked on this merge and on the branch question."}, "by": "owner"}');
