Two known suspects in plugins/trajectory/client/ledger-screen.tsx:
1. :265-281 onScroll calls setFollow(atBottom) on EVERY scroll tick. It bails out when the value is unchanged, so the re-render only happens on the tick where follow flips — but that flip lands mid-scroll, which re-renders the entire screen (all memos depend on things the screen owns). dsh compares against a threshold constant (BOTTOM_FOLLOW_THRESHOLD_PX = 2) with a plain ref boolean (TrajectoryTable.tsx:1728), not React state, precisely so following does not re-render the tree. Consider the same: a ref for the follow decision, state only for whatever genuinely needs to repaint.
2. :259-263 onContentSizeChange fires scrollToEnd on every content-size change whenever follow is true. dsh anchors with anchorTo:''end'' on the virtualizer instead (ae1008b4fb), so following is a virtualizer property rather than an imperative scroll call.

Scope: make tail-follow correct and cheap BEFORE S3 virtualizes the list. Do not add virtualization knobs here — S3 owns that. Acceptance: tail-follow still engages only at the bottom, stops permanently on scroll-up, and re-arms on a fresh append at the bottom; a mid-scroll follow flip does not re-render the whole screen. Cover with a test in the existing ledger-screen.test.tsx harness.', 'ready', 'done', 100, 'dev', '2026-09-28T15:43:49.800Z', '2026-09-28T17:00:34.534Z', '', '[]');

