(b) getItemLayout + windowSize + maxToRenderPerBatch + removeClippedSubviews. RNW 0.21 defaults are maxToRenderPerBatch 10 and windowSize 21 (react-native-web/dist/vendor/react-native/VirtualizedList/index.js:52-55, :77-80); dsh''s equivalent ceiling is windowSize 21 x batch 10 = 210 and its e2e asserts MAX_MOUNTED_ROWS=160 on an 88-turn fixture. dsh also virtualizes EAGERLY when older history exists, bypassing the VIRTUALIZATION_THRESHOLD of 100 (TrajectoryTable.tsx:1774-1775) — mirror that once S1''s reverse cursor exists.
(c) STABLE-ID ADDRESSING. client/ledger-screen.tsx:793-801 chromeKey emits turn-${record.turn} / step-${turn}-${title} / rule-${turn}, and record.turn is index+1 (:739) — POSITIONAL. Prepending older history renumbers every turn and remounts every chrome row. Cell rows are already content-derived and stable (virtual-rows.ts:41-46 over trajectoryRecordId). This is dsh''s 13fed3721f and it is a hard prerequisite for S4''s load-older. Also fix the latent collision: layout.ts:350 builds assistant recordIds as `assistant\0${turnId}\0${step ?? 0}`, so two assistant messages in one turn with a null step collide on `assistant\0{turn}\00` (recorder.ts:280-281 yields null when no turn is open). No fixture exercises it.
(d) useStableVirtualRowStructure equivalent. dsh''s TrajectoryTable.tsx:136-153 returns the PREVIOUS array instance when every key and height is unchanged, so estimateSize/getItemKey keep stable identity and the measurement cache survives text-only deltas. Today every rebuild at :109-146 allocates a new {key,height,cells} object per row, which is why the React.memo at :618 NEVER HITS and every mounted row re-renders on every append. This is the single cheapest fix with the largest measured payoff in the whole sequence.
