MEASURED (this machine, real exported functions, median of 9 reps):
- TrajectorySearchIndex.update: 32.03ms per append at 24,800 cells, versus 0.0003ms when the identity short-circuit fires. The short-circuit CANNOT fire on the live path: shared/dsh/search-index.ts:93-95 guards on array identity, client/ledger-screen.tsx:88 passes a fresh [turns] wrapper every append, and turns is itself freshly allocated by deriveTrajectoryLayout. The fallback is not cheap — indexTurn calls recordSources (:116) for every cell, allocating a ~20-element array and running JSON.stringify three times BEFORE sameSources can compare. This is the largest single measured cost in the plugin.
- 8 full Theta(N) passes per append, not the 6 first reported: eventsToFoldRows refolds the ENTIRE buffer (client/use-trajectory-delta.ts:55), then deriveTrajectoryLayout, allOpen, index.update, expandTurns, the virtualRows build, deriveTrajectoryTimeline, and an UNMEMOIZED turnNumbers1ToN at :178.
- The common path is empirically LINEAR over a size ladder (880 -> 1205 us/1k rows, 88 -> 6400 turns), so the ladder''s job is to hold a ceiling, not to catch a quadratic.
- There IS one confirmed quadratic, in SHAPE not size: layout.ts:312 does groups.find(...) per message/tool row, giving O(steps^2) per turn. Measured 8x the rows -> 30x the time (178ms at 12,801 rows for a single turn of 6,400 steps). A pure size ladder never sees it; a degenerate 1-turn x 4000-steps fixture does.
- toggleTurn is O(T x S): it scans ALL openSteps doing startsWith(prefix) per key (ledger-screen.tsx:148-163).
- TrajectoryCellRow (client/ledger-cells.tsx:177) is a plain function component, not memoized. RecordPresentation in dsh is deliberately NOT React.memo but uses per-field useMemo — do not blanket-add React.memo; memoize the content, not the shell.

Three parts, and dsh''s ordering discipline applies:
(1) INCREMENTAL FOLD. dsh''s incremental apply() (f479c60b6d) shipped 2026-08-10 18:38 and its key-to-position index (fc4df896a0) shipped 2 HOURS LATER at 20:38 — apply() went out incomplete and had to be finished. Ship both together. Store contributions by key with a key->position index; a content update with the same anchor replaces in place, a new contribution or anchor change rebuilds and sorts. dsh is explicit that this is O(C log C) on publication and does NOT claim end-to-end O(1) — do not over-claim here either. In our code the equivalent seam is the buffer->rows->layout chain, and eventsToFoldRows refolding the whole buffer is the first thing to stop.
(2) SEARCH IDENTITY + THROTTLE. Fix the short-circuit so it can fire (stop handing update() a fresh wrapper), and add dsh''s 3s commit throttle (SEARCH_INDEX_THROTTLE_MS = 3_000, TrajectoryView.tsx:33) with first-update-immediate and a trailing batch. dsh never tuned the 3s value after landing and left no rationale — do not pretend we know why 3s; keep the value and note it as inherited.
(3) PER-RECORD CONTENT MEMO. Mirror RecordPresentation (TrajectoryTable.tsx:975-1006) — per-field useMemo on the content fields so a text delta reparses one record. Note it is deliberately NOT React.memo in dsh.

HARD CONSTRAINT from dsh''s architecture note :75, and it is a correctness rule, not a tuning preference: "Display memoization and search indexing stay separate. Search must include off-screen records and may lag live changes by the throttle interval; Table rendering must update the visible changed record immediately and must not inherit the index''s commit cadence." The list must NOT throttle its own render on the search index''s schedule.

MEASUREMENT FIRST, since the plan is worthless without numbers: build a scale fixture generator (turns ladder 8/88/400/1600/6400, plus cells-per-turn 7 and 25, plus the degenerate 1-turn x 4000-steps shape) and ratio-assert t(4N)/t(N) < 8 on deriveTrajectoryLayout, groupTrajectoryVirtualRows, search-index update/search, eventsToFoldRows, and deriveTrajectoryTimeline. Ratio against a same-run baseline, never an absolute ms — shared CI hardware is 2-3x slower than this machine. Expect the degenerate axis to FAIL today; that failure is the deliverable. Consider extracting the four private seams (expandTurns, the virtualRows builder, turnNumbers1ToN, allStepKeys) into shared/dsh/ as pure exports first so 3 more of the 8 passes and the O(TxS) toggle become measurable with zero React.

