THE MEASURED PROBLEM, restated so it is not re-derived
TrajectorySearchIndex.update costs 28.7 ms per append at 19,200 cells and 90.4 ms at 57,600. The identity short-circuit is worth about four orders of magnitude, but it cannot fire on an append, and no local cleverness fixes that: deriveTrajectoryLayout constructs FRESH CELL OBJECTS for every cell on every call, so indexTurn cannot recognise an unchanged record and recomputes recordSources - three JSON.stringify passes - for all of them. The throttle already landed bounds this cost but never reduces it.

THE DEV RAISED A BLOCKER, AND THE LEADER RESOLVES IT
The dev''s concern was that if the layout preserves cell identity, turns stops being a fresh array, the short-circuit starts firing, and matches becomes a function of layout identity - "a throttling decision about how stale search is allowed to be, and whether the unfiltered list may share the index''s cadence."

That coupling is already resolved, and the dev had built the resolution before noticing it was also an answer to this. dsh''s architecture note fixes the rule: the unfiltered list must not inherit the index''s cadence; a filtered list IS the index''s output and may be as fresh as the index. client/ledger-screen.tsx already implements exactly that split - createCommitThrottle at :185-188, conditioned so the commit is throttled ONLY while no query is active (:199-203) and immediate on a live query (:216), with the reasoning written at :199-216. Staleness is therefore governed by the throttle, which is unchanged. Identity-preservation changes HOW OFTEN the index recomputes, not HOW STALE it is allowed to be. The two mechanisms are orthogonal and no new staleness decision is required.

So: proceed. The binding constraint is not the staleness question, it is dsh''s own history - apply() shipped 2026-08-10 18:38 and its key-to-position index shipped 2 hours later at 20:38, apply() first and incomplete, and dsh''s ledger note calls that the biggest ordering mistake available. **Ship the incremental apply and the position index as ONE change set, or not at all.**

SHAPE, from dsh
A snapshot builder that stores contributions by key with a key-to-position index: a content update with the same anchor replaces one contribution in place, a new contribution or anchor change rebuilds and sorts. dsh is explicit that this is O(C log C) on publication and does NOT claim end-to-end O(1) - do not over-claim here either. In our code the seam is the buffer -> rows -> layout chain, and the whole-buffer refold in the delta hook is the first thing to stop.

ONE QUESTION THE LEADER STILL WANTS ANSWERED
Does preserving cell identity require any change to the OUTPUT TYPE of deriveTrajectoryLayout, or is it purely an implementation change with the identical shape? If it needs a new field or structure on the returned model, that is a contract change on a pure function three other modules consume (ledger-screen, the timeline derivation, the search index) and it gets announced and tested as such. If the shape is identical, this is an internal change with a much smaller blast radius. Answer this in your report - the dev has read the layout and the leader has not, and the answer changes how much ceremony this needs.

VERIFICATION
Ratio-assert, never absolute milliseconds - shared CI hardware is 2-3x slower. t(4N)/t(N) < 8 against a same-run baseline. Keep the existing degenerate-axis coverage (1 turn x N steps) even though the groups.find quadratic is now fixed: that axis is what would catch a replacement reintroducing O(steps^2) in a different shape. Construct the discriminating case for the incremental path specifically: an append that changes ONE record and leaves the rest untouched must not do work proportional to the total. The dev''s own lesson from this series applies: make the gate chain unconditional - a grep matching nothing returns non-zero and a && chain will silently skip a step, which is how a live lint error reached a commit in S5.

BOUNDARIES
Stay inside plugins/trajectory. No public shape change without announcing it. Do not touch the row height constants or the list props. If making the gate unconditional would require changing a repo script, report it rather than working around it. Gates: plugin tests, plugin tsc --noEmit, format:check and lint scoped to what you changed, each run independently and unconditionally. --no-verify authorized for the pre-commit typecheck, bypass disclosed, no git config changes. Commit to fix/trajectory-render-list. No PR, no merge, no deploy, no daemon restart.

SEQUENCING - the owner''s budget may gate this
Week quota is at 79%, resets Sep 30 05:00. This is the largest remaining change, and S3e (the browser e2e that pins the mounted-row ceiling and closes the pixels gap S4 explicitly left open) is still waiting on owner authorisation. Raise it before starting if you think the order should be the other way; I would rather reorder explicitly than have the week run out mid-change.', 'user-decision', 'pending', 0, 'dev', '2026-09-28T18:19:40.241Z', '2026-09-28T18:19:40.241Z', '', '[]');

