All 5 requirements met. Config: additive optional modelPrefixes; patch side nullable per key so one tag clears without touching siblings; keys uncapped and uncharset-restricted (measured: live catalog has ''wafer.ai''). Store: nulls are dropped BEFORE either schema sees them — deepMerge assigns null rather than deleting, so a null left in the map would have failed ProviderOverrideSchema on the way to disk and MutableDaemonConfigSchema on the way back, rejecting the WHOLE patch. That was the highest-risk item and both merge paths are covered by tests (persisted pure fn + store→disk→reload). Rendering: rows resolve per-sub-provider with provider-wide fallback, sub-provider read from metadata.providerId behind a typeof check, never inferred from the model id. Sheet: provider-wide section KEPT plus one section per served sub-provider, enumerated from served (not search-filtered) models, deduped+sorted, saving state keyed per sub-provider. Composer fallback keeps the provider-wide tag because its options carry no metadata.

GATES: app 231/231 (13 files incl. every consumer of the changed modules), server store 50/50, protocol 709/709 incl. the ws-outbound AOT validator. Lint 0/0. Typecheck: verified ZERO new errors — one real TS2345 my change introduced (composer fallback passing tags where a string was expected) was caught and fixed; the only file of mine in the remaining error list is T10''s provider-max-context-field.test.tsx carrying its known pre-existing react-dom/client TS7016.

