DIAGNOSIS CONFIRMED. applyProviderContextCap (provider-model-context-cap.ts:48) only rewrites what Paseo''s UI advertises; no harness is ever told.

PER-HARNESS:
• opencode — ENFORCEABLE, natively. Seam ALREADY WIRED: bridge.ts:97 decorateServerEnv parses+reserializes OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT (server-manager.ts:331, opencode-agent.ts:1435). Key provider.<id>.models.<m>.limit.context confirmed in Paseo''s PINNED sdk 1.18.23 (types.gen.d.ts:905/1323/2616), not assumed. Binary deep-merges OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT LAST (local scope, after project config) so injected keys WIN. Decompiled 1.18.31 auto-compacts natively: shouldCompact = auto!==false && limit.context!==0 && totalTokens >= (limit.context - maxOutputTokens); overflow auto-compacts and continues, hard ContextOverflowError only if it cannot fit. Caveat: effective point is cap minus maxOutputTokens; limit.input branch wins if set.
• claude — ENFORCEABLE, CONTRADICTING the spec''s "no knob known". CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW (env, highest precedence) / --autocompact; effective window = min(modelWindow, autoCompactWindow). NO new plumbing: extraArgs already open (options.ts:51), SDK forwards arbitrary keys as --<kebab>. TRAP: CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS applies ONLY to model ids Claude Code does not recognize; for real claude-* ids it also needs DISABLE_COMPACT. Output-token knobs (MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS/MAX_THINKING_TOKENS) are per-message, NOT the window. Range 100k-1M, can only LOWER, compaction not refusal.
• omp — config-file only, UNPROVEN. Catalog contextWindow is read (rpc-types.ts:106) then DISCARDED by map-omp-model.ts:40-54, so omp''s cap is currently a Paseo-local invention with zero harness counterpart. All 19 RPCs (rpc-types.ts:497-548) + argv builder carry no context field. Routes: --config overlay w/ compaction.thresholdTokens, or models.yml modelOverrides.contextWindow — both need Paseo writing a file it never writes. Probe showed config get/list unchanged, so UNPROVEN.
• acp — NOT ENFORCEABLE, stated plainly. Full ClientRequest union (13 methods) has no context channel; SetSessionConfigOption only picks agent-advertised options. update.size PROVEN = "Total context window size in tokens", used = fill (upstream types.gen.d.ts:3648-3671) — Paseo''s mapping correct. usage_update UNSTABLE upstream.

SEMANTICS: harness-native compaction injection per harness. REJECTED refuses-new-turns (unusable mid-task, no recovery, doesn''t reduce an over-cap context, acp''s only option). REJECTED prompt truncation (silently drops content). HONEST CAVEAT: enforcement is SOFT; a hard ceiling is impossible from outside on claude/acp.

METER TRUTH: saturating ALREADY done at context-window-meter.tsx:49 (Math.min(100,...)). Gap is composer/index.tsx:273 feeding raw lastUsage. Set displayMax = min(runtime, cap) there — saturation then IS the QC proof.

TWO SPEC CORRECTIONS: (1) composer reads agent.lastUsage.contextWindowMaxTokens, not an adapter-side "raw runtime value" — same conclusion, imprecise mechanism; (2) for omp the capped number has no harness counterpart at all, so the cap file''s overclaiming comment is wrong for a second reason.

QC r28: claude FLOORS AT 100k, so a 50K cap is only meaningful on OPENCODE — assert compaction near cap + meter saturation.

