ENV: HEAD parity verified before linking (mine 6927d72ac == /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk 6927d72ac). The stale-sibling trap was CONFIRMED live, not hypothetical: sibling packages/protocol/dist/provider-config.d.ts has 0 hits for modelPrefixes (built 00:29, before T11''s 01:20-01:49 commits). Fixed by copying per-package node_modules, repointing every @getpaseo link at MY packages, and rebuilding protocol/highlight/relay/client in MY tree — my dist now shows modelPrefixes 2+16 hits and require.resolve from packages/app lands on MY dist. Root nm symlinked, /node_modules appended to this worktree''s info/exclude, tree clean.
BASELINE (measured before any edit): 4 target test files 78/78 green; app typecheck 163 errors / 92 files — matches the documented baseline, so the env is sound rather than silently degraded.

DESIGN (see decisions): group key = readModelSubProviderId, the same accessor collectSubProviderIds uses; one pure merge fn buildSubProviderModelSections(subProviderIds, filteredModels) in provider-model-prefix.ts; sections from UNFILTERED models (T11 invariant: search must not make a tag unreachable), rows from FILTERED; remainder = served models with no metadata.providerId, rendered as the last section under the EXISTING models.discovered header, which means ZERO new i18n keys and ZERO translation risk; provider with no sub-providers renders byte-identical output to today.', 'running', '[]', '[]', '[]', '["T13 DESIGN NOTE (owner-visible; research first, no code yet). Env: HEAD parity verified before linking; the stale-sibling trap CONFIRMED live (sibling protocol dist has 0 modelPrefixes hits, built 00:29 vs T11 commits 01:20-01:49). Fixed by repointing every @getpaseo link at MY packages and rebuilding protocol/highlight/relay/client here; my dist has modelPrefixes 2+16 and app resolution lands on my dist. Baselines measured BEFORE any edit: 4 target files 78/78 green, app typecheck 163 errors / 92 files (matches documented baseline).\n\nREADING: sheet today = [Context limit][Model tag][Model tag · sub]×N[Discovered: FLAT list][Custom models]. After T13 the flat list disappears; each sub''s rows sit inside its own group, directly under its own ''Model tag · sub'' header. Provider-wide Model tag and Context limit stay at the top. Custom models stay a separate last section.\n\n(1) GROUP KEY = readModelSubProviderId — the SAME accessor collectSubProviderIds uses. Not the first ''/'' segment of model.id, not a hardcoded ''opencode'' check. Any other derivation can disagree with the section list, and a disagreement silently strands rows in a group with no header. One function, two call sites, cannot drift.\n\n(2) ONE pure function buildSubProviderModelSections(subProviderIds, filteredModels) in packages/app/src/provider-selection/provider-model-prefix.ts, beside collectSubProviderIds so the enumeration contract lives with its sibling. Returns [{subProviderId, models}]: sub sections in subProviderIds order, then any sub the filtered models alone mention (sorted), then the remainder (subProviderId undefined) last, omitted when empty. One function rather than a group+merge pair — two functions would let a caller pass one list and render the other.\n\n(3) REMAINDER HOME = its own last-before-Custom section headed by the EXISTING models.discovered key. Consequences: ZERO new i18n keys (so zero translation risk and key parity trivially green), no dead key, and — the property I care most about — a provider with no sub-providers renders the single ''Discovered'' section exactly as today, so every non-aggregating provider is visually unchanged. REJECTED: hanging remainder rows under the provider-wide Model tag section — it reads as ''the models this tag governs'', but modelPrefix is the fallback for every sub row WITHOUT a per-sub tag too (resolveModelPrefixTags), so that section would show a strict subset of the rows it actually affects; a lie in the layout. REJECTED: a ''Model tag · other'' section — needs a config key for a sub-provider that by definition has no id, i.e. protocol+server work, outside this task''s app-only scope (T12 owns those).\n\n(4) SEARCH: sections come from the UNFILTERED models, rows from the FILTERED ones. Deliberate, preserves T11''s stated invariant (''a search box must not make a configured tag unreachable'') which the brief lists under requirement 3. A group with no matching rows therefore renders its tag field with no model card and no count rather than disappearing; every match still shows, in its own group. REJECTED: hiding empty groups — reads cleaner but strands configuration behind a keystroke. Empty-state and Custom behaviour unchanged.\n\n(5) ONE card per group, not two: the tag field and the group''s rows share a single settingsStyles.card, because that style carries borderRadius lg + border + overflow hidden and a second stacked card would draw a doubled rounded seam. Model rows already carry borderTopWidth, giving exactly the hairline the field needs above the first row. Verified against styles/settings.ts:card.\n\n(6) PERF: the group replaces ProviderSubModelPrefixSection, keeping its rationale intact (save callback created once per sub, not per sheet render — parent onSave is already useCallback, handleSave keyed [onSave, subProviderId]). Row arrays stay referentially stable because filteredDiscovered is memoised on [discoveredModels, q], so the 10s ''fetched at'' clock tick cannot re-render every row.\n\n(7) i18n: NO new keys at all. Verified models.discovered has exactly ONE consumer repo-wide — the flat header I am replacing — so reusing it leaves no dead key.\n\n(8) BLAST RADIUS measured: tag consumers are composer/agent-controls, use-agent-form-state, use-schedule-form-provider-snapshot, metadata-generation-page and provider-selection.ts; all call buildProviderModelPrefixes/resolveModelPrefixTags and are untouched. Grouping is presentational only.\n\n(9) FILES (shared-file announce, lane rule d-12a0c8b77a): packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx; packages/app/src/provider-selection/provider-model-prefix.ts + .test.ts; NEW packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-model-groups.test.tsx (mine, no collision); docs/custom-providers.md line 778 (one sentence: ''renders one field per section'' becomes ''each section lists that sub-provider''s models beneath it''). NOT touched: packages/server, packages/protocol (T12''s), composer, provider-selection consumers, i18n resources.\n\n(10) TESTS: pure — grouping by sub, remainder last, empty remainder omitted, filtered rows never stranded (a sub only the filtered list mentions still gets a section), section order preserved, blank/whitespace providerId landing in the remainder via the same accessor (cross-checked against collectSubProviderIds output). Component — render ProviderDiagnosticSheet with mocked hooks and a children-rendering AdaptiveModalSheet, then assert: each group''s rows sit under its own sub header; a search matching one sub keeps that sub''s rows and drops the others while BOTH tag fields remain; the remainder section appears only when no-sub rows exist; Custom unaffected; per-sub testIDs still unique.\n\n(11) RISKS / what QC must re-probe: the sheet''s section order changed, so QC r27''s flat-''Discovered'' card probe is stale by construction — r28 should probe group containers, not the old flat list. And I could NOT verify offline how many of opencode''s 86 served rows declare metadata.providerId, so whether a remainder section is visible on TEST is an open question QC should report rather than assume either way."]', '{"lesson_topic": "stale-sibling @getpaseo dist", "docs_updated": []}', 'ab6fbd8f-1c61-4d51-9332-6aebeae46760', 'opencode-go/space-bunny-free', '{"n": 323, "ts": "2026-10-03T05:11:16.463Z", "summary": "T13 turn 1 — DESIGN NOTE posted, ZERO code written yet (env setup + research only).\n\nENV: HEAD parity verified before linking (mine 6927d72ac == /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk 6927d72ac). The stale-sibling trap was CONFIRMED live, not hypothetical: sibling packages/protocol/dist/provider-config.d.ts has 0 hits for modelPrefixes (built 00:29, before T11''s 01:20-01:49 commits). Fixed by copying per-package node_modules, repointing every @getpaseo link at MY packages, and rebuilding protocol/highlight/relay/client in MY tree — my dist now shows modelPrefixes 2+16 hits and require.resolve from packages/app lands on MY dist. Root nm symlinked, /node_modules appended to this worktree''s info/exclude, tree clean.\nBASELINE (measured before any edit): 4 target test files 78/78 green; app typecheck 163 errors / 92 files — matches the documented baseline, so the env is sound rather than silently degraded.\n\nDESIGN (see decisions): group key = readModelSubProviderId, the same accessor collectSubProviderIds uses; one pure merge