INTERPRETATION CONFIRMED vs pinned dsh @ afd92680f2: the owner''s read is right. dsh renders own-duration for EVERY cell kind (TrajectoryCell.tsx:89); ours had it only for tool rows inside STATS, so a streamed assistant message — the most common row — carried no time anywhere. The panel lacked status / started / timing source / assistant-timing block / token split.

PART 1: data path EXISTED, no recorder change. Tool spans = recorder''s tool/result durationMs (call->result); message/thinking spans = stream-event merge. The real defects were display + a wrong anchor: tool rows were stamped at the RESULT time while their duration already spanned call->result, so every tool looked like it started when it finished and the group wall span sat a duration late (dsh anchors at callTime). Now: call-time anchor, a fifth DUR column shared with the header, and live elapsed ONLY for an unanswered call (a settled row keeps the duration it took; no timer runs when nothing is open). Still unmeasured and shown as an em dash: single-event message, tool call outside any turn, TTFT/generation/throughput.

PART 2: closed in dsh''s vocabulary via a pure layer (inspector-fields.ts) — Status Completed/Pending/Failed, Started + unix toggle, dsh''s timing split, TokenRows split (each only when reported), tool args as Payload, explicit "not recorded" for schema. TTFT/generation/throughput ported AS UNMEASURED in dsh''s wording. PORT_NOTES: 6 ported / 1 partial / 5 gaps / 1 n/a, each gap naming the recorder fact it waits on.

ADVERSARIAL REVIEW (agent d64f7639, read-only, pinned dsh): no fabrication, no double counting, no timer leak, no hook-order problem. Its 5 defects are all fixed in 23d2fe63d: reasoning rows had no running time (plainCell treated thinking as derived) while the README claimed one; the two surfaces disagreed when a row had a duration but no absolute stamp; "timing source" named the wrong clock for tool spans; DurationText could wrap (600m0s) and de-align row heights; the width test had been weakened to ignore rail/gaps/padding, hiding ~58px of CONTEXT on a phone.

