(1) SUB-PROVIDERS ENUMERATED, live count: opencode''s upstream catalog on this machine has 226 sub-provider ids (~/.cache/opencode/models.json: anthropic, openai, opencode, opencode-go, github-copilot, google, deepseek, zai, minimax, alibaba*, ... ). Owner-visible consequence: rendering one section per sub-provider is only sane because Paseo''s daemon already narrows the catalog to ACCESSIBLE ones — opencode-agent.ts:1845-1861 isAccessible = connected.has(id) || source === "api". So sections track credentials, not a 226-row static list.

(2) WHERE THE SUB-PROVIDER ID COMES FROM: opencode model ids are literally "<subProviderId>/<modelId>" (opencode-agent.ts:822 id: `${provider.id}/${modelId}`), and the adapter also sets metadata.providerId / metadata.providerName (828-829). Precedent parser: parseModel at 4996-5004 splits on "/" with providerID = parts[0]. metadata survives to the client (registry:381 spreads the model; AgentMetadata is {[key:string]: unknown} so providerId arrives as `unknown` and must be narrowed with a typeof check).

(3) DERIVATION DECISION — the load-bearing one: derive the sub-provider from metadata.providerId when it is a non-empty string, NOT from the first segment of model.id. A slash-prefix heuristic would misread any provider whose ids contain "/" for unrelated reasons (ACP providers with namespaced ids), silently applying the wrong tag. Provider-agnostic and cannot misfire; no hardcoded "opencode" check.

(4) SECTION ENUMERATION BASIS: distinct sub-provider ids found in the provider''s SERVED models (discoveredModels), so sections appear/disappear as credentials change — self-maintaining, no stale list. Non-opencode providers yield zero sub-sections and are visually unchanged.

(5) READING TO CONFIRM: I keep the provider-wide Model tag field and ADD one section per sub-provider beneath it, rather than replacing it. Removing the provider-wide field would break every existing config''s rendering, since it is the documented fallback. Say the word if you want it replaced.

(6) THE REAL RISK — merge-only delete semantics one level deeper (T7-F lesson): deepMerge (daemon-config-store.ts:80-99) ASSIGNS null rather than deleting, so a null inside a prefix map would land in the merged object and then FAIL ProviderOverrideSchema.parse. Existing scalar delete markers (splitProviderDeleteMarkers:166-178) know nothing about maps. So modelPrefixes needs its own key-level null handling in BOTH merge paths: the persisted path (368-391) and the mutable-view path (omitDeletedProviderFieldsFromConfig:200-221, scalar-only today). This is where a naive implementation would silently corrupt config; it gets dedicated tests.

(7) PROTOCOL COMPAT: additive optional only — published modelPrefixes: record(string, string.max(24)).optional(); patch side record(string, string.max(24).nullable()).optional() so a null VALUE deletes that one key. modelPrefix is never narrowed or removed. Wire schemas stay pure (no transform/catch/preprocess) per docs/protocol-compatibility.md. No contradiction with T7-F.

ALSO FOUND (will bite implementation): ProviderModelPrefixField hardcodes testIDs (provider-model-prefix, -input, -save). N instances would collide, so it needs an optional id-suffix prop before it can be rendered N times.

FILE SCOPE: protocol provider-config.ts + messages.ts; server daemon-config-store.ts; app provider-model-prefix.ts, provider-model-prefix-field.ts/.tsx, provider-selection.ts, provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx; i18n 9 locales; docs/custom-providers.md. Will commit in vertical slices.

