sages.ts; server daemon-config-store.ts; app provider-model-prefix.ts, provider-model-prefix-field.ts/.tsx, provider-selection.ts, provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx; i18n 9 locales; docs/custom-providers.md. Will commit in vertical slices.\n\nNo contradiction with T7-F or the protocol constraints found — proceeding to implementation unless you redirect item (5).", "rationale": "Research was mandated before code and the derivation choice (metadata.providerId vs slash-prefix) is load-bearing: it silently applies the wrong tag if guessed. Item (5) is a reading of \"split into multiple sections\" that affects every existing config.", "source": "leader", "irreversible": false, "author": "2eb265f4-6ec0-49f5-97f4-52a1a4b161df"}');

FILES TOUCHED, exactly: packages/app/src/provider-selection/provider-model-prefix.ts (+ .test.ts, existing suite); packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-sheet.tsx; NEW packages/app/src/components/provider-diagnostic-model-groups.test.tsx (mine, no collision); docs/custom-providers.md (one sentence). NOT touched, verified by git diff --name-only: packages/server, packages/protocol (T12''s), all 9 i18n resources, composer/agent-controls, model-browser.

ENV WARNING FOR EVERY WORKER IN THIS LANE, now proven not theorized: the stale-sibling @getpaseo trap is REAL. /path/to/home/paseo-wt/p0-sdk''s packages/protocol/dist has ZERO hits for modelPrefixes (built Oct 3 00:29, before T11''s 01:20-01:49 commits). Symlinking node_modules from a same-commit sibling resolves @getpaseo/* through it and silently reads stale dist — T11''s modelPrefixes field does not exist there. Working fix: verify HEAD parity, then COPY each packages/*/node_modules and repoint every @getpaseo link at YOUR packages (never symlink the per-package dirs), then rebuild protocol/highlight/relay/client in YOUR tree. Confirm by grepping your own dist for the field T11 added, not by trusting the commit hash.

Also propagatable: 46 pre-existing test files carry an identical TS7016 for react-dom/client because the shared install has no @types/react-dom. Writing a jsdom test with raw createRoot adds a NEW instance of that baseline error; @testing-library/react (repo convention, 26 files) avoids it — which is why the new suite uses RTL.

QC r28 MUST re-probe: r27''s flat-''Discovered'' selector is stale by construction, the flat list is gone. Use provider-model-sub-section-<sub>, provider-model-remainder-section, provider-sheet-model-row-<id>. Two things I could not settle offline, for QC to answer rather than assume: (1) how many of opencode''s 86 served rows declare metadata.providerId, i.e. whether a remainder section is visible on TEST at all — I deliberately added no new ''Other models'' header to avoid 9 unverifiable translations, so its presence hinges entirely on this; (2) the visual card seam, since the field and its rows share ONE card by design (settingsStyles.card carries borderRadius+border, so a second card would draw a doubled rounded seam) and jsdom computes no layout.

